{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01GAGTvhDuMn9TJgJJG4RGzn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Payments System Frontend System Design — Interview Questions\n2\t\n3\tA comprehensive reference of deep questions across all segments, organized by theme and difficulty. Covers the full frontend surface of a checkout and payment processing system (think Stripe, Braintree, PayPal, Adyen).\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## 1. Checkout Flow & Form UX\n8\t\n9\t> Extremely common opening section — interviewers use checkout flow to probe component architecture, form validation strategy, and UX judgment all at once.\n10\t\n11\t### Core\n12\t\n13\t- Walk me through how you would architect a multi-step checkout flow (cart → shipping → payment → confirmation). Where does state live, how do you handle back-navigation, and how do you prevent users from skipping steps?\n14\t- How do you design a credit card input form that provides real-time feedback — card type detection, formatted input masking (e.g., `4242 4242 4242 4242`), expiry validation, and CVV length rules — without blocking the user while they type?\n15\t- What is the correct strategy for inline vs. summary error display in a payment form? When should you validate on `blur` vs. `change` vs. `submit`, and how do you avoid frustrating users with premature errors on partially-typed card numbers?\n16\t- How do you handle address autocomplete (Google Places API, Smarty Streets) in a checkout form — including debouncing, fallback to manual entry when the API is unavailable, and ensuring the autofilled address is still validated server-side?\n17\t- A user fills out the payment form and hits \"Pay Now,\" but the network request takes 3 seconds. Describe your loading state strategy: what is disabled, what is shown, and how do you prevent double-submission?\n18\t- How would you design the order summary panel in a checkout flow so it stays in sync with cart mutations (quantity changes, coupon application, tax recalculation) without full-page reloads?\n19\t- How do you approach progressive disclosure in a checkout form — e.g., showing the billing address form only when it differs from shipping, or revealing the installment options only for purchases above a threshold?\n20\t\n21\t### Deep\n22\t\n23\t- Stripe's \"Link\" feature auto-fills payment details for returning customers across merchants. If you were building a similar saved-payment-method flow, how would you design the UX handoff between \"guest checkout\" and \"recognized user\" without causing a jarring re-render mid-form, and how do you handle the case where the saved method has expired?\n24\t- A/B tests on checkout forms consistently show that reducing the number of visible fields increases conversion — but fewer fields can also increase fraud and failed deliveries. How do you architect a checkout form component system that allows product and risk teams to toggle field visibility, validation rules, and required/optional status from a feature-flag config without frontend deploys?\n25\t- Describe how you would implement a \"smart retry\" UX after a card decline. Specifically: how do you preserve the user's previously entered data (without re-storing raw card numbers), which fields do you clear vs. keep, and what messaging hierarchy do you use to distinguish a soft decline (insufficient funds) from a hard decline (stolen card) given that your frontend may only receive a generic error code?\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## 2. Payment Security & PCI Compliance\n30\t\n31\t> Always asked for senior/staff roles. Interviewers expect you to know why iframes exist and what PCI DSS scope means for frontend architecture choices.\n32\t\n33\t### Core\n34\t\n35\t- What is PCI DSS scope, and how does using a hosted payment field solution like Stripe Elements or Braintree's Hosted Fields reduce the scope of your application's PCI compliance obligations?\n36\t- How does Stripe Elements prevent your page from ever touching raw card data? Walk through the technical mechanism — what is rendered in your DOM, what lives in the Stripe iframe's origin, and what is exchanged between the two contexts via `postMessage`.\n37\t- Why can't you simply style a cross-origin iframe with CSS from the parent page, and how do payment providers like Stripe solve this problem while keeping card data isolated? What are the trade-offs of their \"appearance\" configuration APIs?\n38\t- Explain how a Content Security Policy (CSP) should be configured for a checkout page that loads Stripe.js. Which directives are required, which are commonly misconfigured (and why), and what does Stripe itself require you to allow that might feel uncomfortable from a security standpoint?\n39\t- What is tokenization in the context of card payments? Walk through the lifecycle: the user enters a card number, Stripe creates a `PaymentMethod` object — what is sent to your server, what is never sent, and how does your server use that token to charge the card?\n40\t- What is the risk of storing a Stripe `PaymentIntent` client secret in `localStorage` vs. a session cookie vs. an in-memory variable, and what happens if a malicious script on your page reads the client secret?\n41\t- How do you prevent clickjacking on a checkout page, and why is `X-Frame-Options: DENY` insufficient on its own for a page that also embeds legitimate third-party iframes (like Stripe Elements)?\n42\t\n43\t### Deep\n44\t\n45\t- Stripe Elements renders card input fields inside cross-origin iframes. Your designer wants pixel-perfect custom fonts loaded from your CDN inside those fields. Walk through exactly what the browser's cross-origin isolation rules allow, what Stripe's `fonts` configuration option does under the hood, and what you cannot achieve regardless of configuration — then propose a design compromise that satisfies both security and branding requirements.\n46\t- A penetration tester flags that your checkout page makes a `fetch` to `api.yoursite.com/payment-intent` from the browser, and the response contains the PaymentIntent `client_secret`. They argue this is a security vulnerability. How do you evaluate that claim? Under what conditions is it acceptable to expose a client secret to the browser, and what server-side and frontend controls must be in place to make this safe?\n47\t- You are migrating from a legacy checkout form that directly POSTed raw card data to your own server (PCI SAQ D scope) to a Stripe Elements integration (PCI SAQ A scope). Describe the full migration strategy: how do you run both implementations in parallel for a staged rollout, how do you ensure no raw card data ever hits your new infrastructure, and how do you validate the cutover is complete from a compliance standpoint?\n48\t\n49\t---\n50\t\n51\t## 3. State Management & Transaction Lifecycle\n52\t\n53\t> Tests whether candidates understand the payment intent as a state machine and can reason about eventual consistency, idempotency, and race conditions on the frontend.\n54\t\n55\t### Core\n56\t\n57\t- A Stripe `PaymentIntent` moves through states: `requires_payment_method` → `requires_confirmation` → `requires_action` → `processing` → `succeeded` (or `requires_capture`, `canceled`). How does your frontend model this state machine, and how do you decide which UI to render at each transition?\n58\t- What is idempotency in the context of payment requests, and how do you implement it on the frontend? Specifically, if a user clicks \"Pay\" and the request times out before you receive a response, how do you safely retry without charging the user twice?\n59\t- How do you handle optimistic UI in a payment flow? Unlike a social media \"like,\" a payment has real monetary consequence if the optimistic update is wrong. Where do you draw the line between responsiveness and correctness?\n60\t- Describe how you would manage the state of a multi-step checkout form across a full page refresh. What should be persisted (to `sessionStorage`, a URL param, or a server-side cart session), and what should be intentionally discarded to avoid security issues?\n61\t- What happens to an in-flight payment confirmation if the user's browser tab is closed or the device loses power during the `processing` state? How does your frontend handle re-entry — e.g., the user re-opens the tab or returns to the site 10 minutes later?\n62\t- How do you handle concurrent modifications to a shared cart — e.g., the same user opens checkout in two browser tabs simultaneously? How do you detect the conflict on the frontend and recover gracefully?\n63\t- A user completes payment but the success redirect is intercepted by an ad blocker or a browser extension that strips query params. How do you design the confirmation flow so the user reaches a correct success state even if your `?payment_intent=pi_xxx&redirect_status=succeeded` URL param never arrives?\n64\t\n65\t### Deep\n66\t\n67\t- Walk me through implementing a robust payment retry loop on the frontend. The user's card was declined (soft decline). You want to: (1) allow the user to update their card details, (2) re-confirm the same `PaymentIntent` rather than creating a new one, and (3) cap retries at a safe limit to avoid locking the card. How do you manage the state transitions, and what data do you pass back to the `confirmCardPayment` call on a retry?\n68\t- Describe how you would architect a frontend payment state machine using XState (or a comparable library). Define the states, events, guards, and side effects for the full lifecycle including 3DS authentication, network errors, and soft declines. What are the advantages of this approach over ad-hoc `if/else` logic in React component state?\n69\t- Your checkout frontend runs inside a mobile WebView embedded in a native iOS/Android app. The native app and the WebView both need to know the payment outcome. Walk through the communication architecture: how does a payment confirmation event travel from the Stripe SDK (inside the WebView) through the `postMessage` bridge to the native layer, what are the failure modes, and how do you ensure exactly-once delivery of the success event to the native app?\n70\t\n71\t---\n72\t\n73\t## 4. Real-Time Updates & Webhooks\n74\t\n75\t> Tests understanding of the async gap between \"payment submitted\" and \"payment confirmed\" — a uniquely tricky problem in payment UX.\n76\t\n77\t### Core\n78\t\n79\t- After calling `stripe.confirmCardPayment()`, Stripe returns immediately with a `PaymentIntent` object. But the actual charge confirmation comes asynchronously via webhook. How do you reconcile the frontend's view of payment status with the authoritative server-side status, and when is it safe to show the user a success screen?\n80\t- Compare polling, WebSockets, and Server-Sent Events (SSE) as mechanisms for delivering payment status updates to the frontend. Which would you choose for a payment confirmation flow, and why?\n81\t- How would you implement a polling strategy for payment status that is resilient to transient network failures, doesn't hammer your server, and gives up gracefully after a timeout? Describe the backoff algorithm and the UX at each stage.\n82\t- What is the risk of relying solely on the browser-side `stripe.confirmCardPayment()` return value to determine payment success, rather than verifying server-side via webhook? Give a specific attack scenario where this leads to revenue loss or fraud.\n83\t- Describe the \"pending payment\" screen UX for a payment that enters `processing` state (common with bank transfers, SEPA debit, or certain card networks). What do you show the user, how long do you keep them on this screen, and what happens when they close the browser?\n84\t- How do you handle a scenario where a webhook arrives at your server but the frontend user has already navigated away? How do you re-surface the payment outcome the next time the user visits?\n85\t- Your server receives a `payment_intent.succeeded` webhook but the frontend is currently showing the user a \"payment failed\" error screen (because the initial API call timed out). How do you reconcile this and correct the UI?\n86\t\n87\t### Deep\n88\t\n89\t- Design a real-time payment status notification system that must work across: (a) an active checkout tab using SSE, (b) a user who has closed the tab but re-opens the site within 10 minutes, and (c) a mobile user who has backgrounded the app. Describe the full data flow from Stripe webhook → your backend → frontend for each case, including how you handle reconnection, missed events, and event deduplication.\n90\t- Stripe sends webhooks with a `Stripe-Signature` header for verification. Your frontend needs to display a real-time status update the moment this webhook is processed. Walk through the full architecture: webhook receiver → verification → event storage → push to frontend. How do you ensure the frontend update is consistent with the database state and doesn't display a stale intermediate state?\n91\t- You are building a payment dashboard that shows live transaction status for multiple concurrent payments (think a restaurant POS processing 20 orders simultaneously). Describe how you would design the WebSocket message schema, client-side store normalization, and render optimization to ensure the UI stays responsive and correct as events arrive out of order.\n92\t\n93\t---\n94\t\n95\t## 5. Performance & Core Web Vitals\n96\t\n97\t> A checkout page's performance directly impacts conversion rate — every 100ms of latency costs measurable revenue. Interviewers expect specific metrics and techniques.\n98\t\n99\t### Core\n100\t\n101\t- Stripe.js is a ~300KB third-party script. When and how should you load it, and why does Stripe's own documentation recommend loading it on every page of your site rather than only on the checkout page? What are the performance trade-offs of each approach?\n102\t- How does injecting a Stripe Elements iframe into the DOM affect Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS), and what CSS techniques do you use to prevent the card input from causing layout shifts when it mounts?\n103\t- Describe your bundle-splitting strategy for a checkout page. Which chunks are critical path, which are deferred, and how do you decide what to inline in the HTML vs. load asynchronously?\n104\t- What is the impact of third-party payment SDKs (Stripe, PayPal button, Apple Pay, Google Pay) on your checkout page's Total Blocking Time (TBT) and Interaction to Next Paint (INP)? How do you load these without blocking the main thread?\n105\t- How would you optimize the Time to Interactive (TTI) for a checkout page that requires: authentication state check, cart data fetch, Stripe.js load, and address form render — all before the user can type a card number?\n106\t- Describe how you would use resource hints (`preconnect`, `prefetch`, `preload`) specifically for a checkout page that loads Stripe.js, Google Fonts for the branded card input, and a product image CDN.\n107\t- What are the trade-offs between server-side rendering (SSR), static generation, and client-side rendering for a checkout page? Which approach do you use, and how does it affect Time to First Byte (TTFB) and the \"page is interactive\" moment?\n108\t\n109\t### Deep\n110\t\n111\t- A/B test results show that your checkout page has a 15% higher bounce rate on 3G mobile connections compared to competitors. Your LCP is 4.2s. Walk through a systematic performance audit: which tools do you use, what hypotheses do you form, and which specific optimizations do you implement for the Stripe SDK loading, hero image, and above-the-fold form render?\n112\t- Stripe Elements renders inside an iframe, which means the browser must establish a separate network connection to `js.stripe.com`. Model the exact sequence of DNS lookup, TCP handshake, TLS negotiation, and iframe load for a user on a 50ms-latency mobile connection. Where are the optimization opportunities, and what is the irreducible minimum latency floor you cannot engineer around?\n113\t- You are asked to implement a \"one-click checkout\" experience (similar to Shop Pay or Amazon 1-Click) where returning users can complete a purchase in under 2 seconds. Describe the full performance architecture: what is pre-fetched on the product page, what is pre-loaded on hover/tap, how is the PaymentIntent pre-created, and what is the critical rendering path once the user clicks \"Buy Now\"?\n114\t\n115\t---\n116\t\n117\t## 6. Error Handling & Resilience\n118\t\n119\t> Payment errors are high-stakes and high-frequency. Interviewers probe whether you can distinguish error types and build UX that recovers without losing the user.\n120\t\n121\t### Core\n122\t\n123\t- Enumerate the categories of errors that can occur in a frontend payment flow (network errors, card declines, validation errors, authentication failures, fraud blocks, rate limits) and describe how the error handling strategy differs for each category.\n124\t- A user's card is declined with Stripe error code `card_declined` and decline code `insufficient_funds`. What do you show the user? What do you show the user if the decline code is `stolen_card`? How does your error message component know which codes warrant specific messaging vs. a generic \"payment failed\" message?\n125\t- What is 3D Secure (3DS) authentication, when is it triggered, and how does `stripe.confirmCardPayment()` handle the 3DS challenge flow? What does the user experience look like, and what are the failure modes (user cancels, 3DS times out, bank's 3DS page is down)?\n126\t- How do you distinguish between a network timeout (where the payment may or may not have processed) and a definitive payment failure (where you know the charge was rejected)? How does each case change your frontend error recovery strategy?\n127\t- Describe your strategy for handling the case where Stripe.js itself fails to load (CDN outage, network error, ad blocker). Do you have a fallback, or do you fail gracefully? What does the user see, and what do you log?\n128\t- How do you implement a circuit breaker pattern on the frontend for payment requests? If your payment API endpoint is returning 503s, how do you detect this condition and prevent the user from hammering a degraded backend?\n129\t- What is the UX strategy for a payment that fails at the very last step — after the user has entered all their details and clicked \"Pay\" — but due to a server-side error rather than a card decline? How do you preserve their form state and communicate the error without inducing panic?\n130\t\n131\t### Deep\n132\t\n133\t- Walk me through the full 3DS2 authentication flow from a frontend architecture standpoint. Specifically: how does Stripe.js detect that 3DS is required after `confirmCardPayment`, how is the challenge rendered (in an iframe? a redirect? a modal?), how do you handle the case where the device fingerprinting step triggers a full redirect rather than a seamless iframe challenge, and what happens to your React component state across that redirect boundary?\n134\t- You are building a checkout that must work in environments with extremely poor connectivity (rural mobile, flaky WiFi). Design a resilience strategy that includes: detecting offline state before submission, queuing the payment attempt for retry when connectivity returns, preventing duplicate charges, and communicating uncertainty to the user without causing them to abandon. What APIs do you use, and what are the limits of what you can guarantee on the frontend?\n135\t- Your monitoring alerts that 8% of users who click \"Pay\" are seeing an unhandled JavaScript exception in the Stripe Elements payment confirmation step. You have Sentry traces showing the error originates inside the cross-origin Stripe iframe. What do you know, and what don't you know, from that error report? How do you diagnose the root cause given that you cannot inspect Stripe's iframe code, and what mitigations do you ship while the investigation is ongoing?\n136\t\n137\t---\n138\t\n139\t## 7. Internationalization & Localization\n140\t\n141\t> Often underweighted by candidates. A globally deployed payments frontend has uniquely complex i18n requirements around currency, local payment methods, and regulatory display rules.\n142\t\n143\t### Core\n144\t\n145\t- Describe how you format currency amounts in a payments UI across different locales. What does `Intl.NumberFormat` give you, where does it fall short (e.g., currencies with non-standard subunit counts like JPY or KWD), and how do you handle amounts that arrive from your API in minor units (cents)?\n146\t- How do you display prices that include tax in markets where tax must be shown separately (US) vs. markets where prices must be shown tax-inclusive by law (EU, Australia)? How does this affect your pricing component's data contract and render logic?\n147\t- What are the specific challenges of supporting RTL languages (Arabic, Hebrew) in a checkout form — beyond just `dir=\"rtl\"` on the container? Think about icon placement (card type icon, CVV help icon), number formatting, and error message positioning.\n148\t- Stripe supports \"local payment methods\" (iDEAL in the Netherlands, BLIK in Poland, Pix in Brazil, UPI in India). How do you architect a payment method selector that is data-driven (configured per-country) rather than hardcoded, and how do each of these methods change the checkout UX flow?\n149\t- How do you handle locale-specific date formatting in a payments context — specifically card expiry dates, invoice dates, and estimated delivery windows — given that `12/03` means March 12 in Europe and December 3 in the US?\n150\t- What is your strategy for translating dynamic server error messages (card decline reasons, fraud messages) that arrive in English from your payment processor but need to be displayed in the user's language?\n151\t- How do you support multiple currencies in a single checkout — e.g., a platform where the buyer is in Germany paying in EUR but the seller is in Canada receiving CAD? What does the UI need to display, and what data must come from the server vs. what can the frontend derive?\n152\t\n153\t### Deep\n154\t\n155\t- You are expanding checkout to Japan, which has several unique requirements: prices are always displayed as whole numbers (no decimal yen), the most popular payment method is convenience store payment (konbini) which is asynchronous and cash-based, and the address form field order is reversed (postal code → prefecture → city → street, then name in family-name-first order). Walk through the specific component and data model changes required, and how you architect the address form to be locale-driven rather than requiring a separate Japanese checkout page.\n156\t- Stripe's `amount` field is always an integer in the currency's smallest unit. For most currencies this is cents, but for currencies like the Jordanian Dinar (3 decimal places, 1 JOD = 1000 fils) and currencies like the Japanese Yen (0 decimal places), the math changes. Build a robust currency utility module: given a `{amount: number, currency: string}` object, how do you correctly format the display value, and how do you validate user-entered amounts to prevent off-by-100x errors?\n157\t- Design a payment method ranking and display system for a global checkout. The backend provides a list of available payment methods for the user's country and cart value. Your frontend must: rank them by local preference (e.g., iDEAL first in NL, not Visa), display their logos with appropriate localized labels, hide methods that don't support the cart currency, and gracefully degrade if the ranking config is unavailable. Describe the data schema, component hierarchy, and fallback behavior.\n158\t\n159\t---\n160\t\n161\t## 8. Observability & Analytics\n162\t\n163\t> Tells interviewers whether you think about the full product lifecycle, not just shipping code. For a payments frontend, data quality is revenue-critical.\n164\t\n165\t### Core\n166\t\n167\t- What events would you instrument in a checkout funnel to enable a product team to measure conversion at each step and identify where users are dropping off? Give specific event names, properties, and the conditions under which each fires.\n168\t- How do you track \"payment abandonment\" — specifically distinguishing between: (a) a user who leaves the page before entering any payment details, (b) a user who starts entering card info but exits, and (c) a user who clicks \"Pay\" but the request fails? Why does this distinction matter for product decisions?\n169\t- What is your strategy for tracking errors in a payment flow without accidentally logging sensitive card data (PANs, CVVs) to your analytics or error monitoring service? What specific fields or patterns do you sanitize before sending to Sentry or Datadog?\n170\t- How do you measure the performance of the Stripe.js initialization and Elements mount time in your Real User Monitoring (RUM) data? What custom performance marks would you use, and how do you correlate slow load times with conversion drop-off?\n171\t- Describe how you would build a real-time payment success rate dashboard. What metrics do you track (success rate, decline rate broken down by decline code, 3DS completion rate), and what is your alerting threshold that should page an on-call engineer?\n172\t- How do you instrument the retry behavior after a card decline to understand whether your retry UX is effective? What metrics tell you the retry flow is working vs. that it is causing additional user frustration?\n173\t- What is the risk of sending `payment_intent_id` or `charge_id` in analytics events (e.g., to Google Analytics or Amplitude), and how do you evaluate whether to include these identifiers?\n174\t\n175\t### Deep\n176\t\n177\t- You notice in your funnel data that 23% of users who reach the payment step never click \"Pay\" — they simply leave. Your checkout form has a 4-second load time for Stripe Elements on mobile. Walk through how you would design and execute an experiment to determine whether the Elements load time is causally responsible for the abandonment rate, versus other hypotheses (price shock, trust signals, required account creation). What instrumentation do you add, and how do you isolate the variable?\n178\t- Design an observability system for a payments frontend that gives you the following within 60 seconds of a production incident: (1) the percentage of checkout attempts that are failing vs. succeeding in real time, (2) whether the failure is in the Stripe client SDK, your own API, or the network between them, and (3) which user segments (by country, payment method, device type) are most affected. Describe the events, aggregation pipeline, and dashboard panels you would build.\n179\t- Your payment success rate drops from 94% to 87% after a deploy. You need to determine whether this is a frontend regression or a backend/Stripe issue. Describe your diagnostic playbook: which logs and metrics do you look at first, how do you correlate the deploy timestamp with the metric drop, how do you check whether Stripe has an ongoing incident, and what is your rollback decision criteria? Assume you have Datadog RUM, Sentry, and Stripe's Dashboard available.\n180\t\n181\t---\n182\t\n183\t## 9. Architecture & Provider Abstraction\n184\t\n185\t> Staff/principal level territory. Tests whether you can design a payment frontend that doesn't tightly couple to a single PSP, enabling multi-provider routing and future migration.\n186\t\n187\t### Core\n188\t\n189\t- How do you architect a frontend payment abstraction layer that can route to Stripe for some transactions, Adyen for others, and PayPal for a third segment — all without the checkout UI component knowing which PSP is being used?\n190\t- Different PSPs have different client-side SDKs (Stripe.js, Adyen's Web Components, Braintree's client SDK). These all have different APIs for mounting card fields, confirming payments, and handling 3DS. How do you normalize these into a single interface that your checkout component talks to?\n191\t- What is a \"payment method types\" configuration, and how do you design a frontend data model that is PSP-agnostic — capable of expressing \"card,\" \"bank transfer,\" \"wallet,\" and \"buy now pay later\" without encoding PSP-specific field names or token formats?\n192\t- How do you handle the case where your provider abstraction layer must support PSPs that have fundamentally different authentication flows — e.g., Stripe's embedded iframe model vs. Adyen's full-page redirect for certain payment methods?\n193\t- What are the risks of building a \"thin shim\" abstraction vs. a \"rich unified API\" abstraction over multiple PSPs? Where does each approach break down in practice?\n194\t- How do you design the error model for a PSP abstraction layer? Stripe error codes differ from Adyen result codes, which differ from Braintree transaction statuses. How do you normalize these into a set of frontend-actionable error categories without losing the PSP-specific detail your support team needs?\n195\t- How would you approach lazy-loading PSP SDKs so that Stripe.js is only loaded when Stripe is the selected provider, and Adyen's SDK is only loaded when Adyen is selected — while keeping the time-to-interactive acceptable?\n196\t\n197\t### Deep\n198\t\n199\t- You are building a multi-PSP checkout where Stripe handles cards, PayPal handles its own wallet flow, and Klarna handles BNPL — all on the same checkout page. Each SDK wants to mount its own UI components into your DOM. Describe the component mounting strategy, the event communication model between each third-party component and your React state, and how you ensure that only one payment method's UI is \"active\" at a time without leaking event listeners or iframe references.\n200\t- Design the frontend architecture for a payment platform that must support provider failover: if Stripe returns a 5xx during `confirmCardPayment`, you want to retry the same charge attempt through Adyen within 2 seconds, without the user knowing a provider switch occurred. What constraints does this place on how you construct the PaymentIntent server-side, how you pass the client token to the frontend, and what the abstraction layer's retry logic looks like? Where does this approach fundamentally break down and require server-side coordination instead?\n201\t- You are tasked with migrating a checkout from Braintree to Stripe over 6 months, with a gradual rollout. Both SDKs must be active simultaneously during the migration. Walk through: how you load both SDKs without doubling blocking script weight, how you route specific user cohorts to each provider (feature flag, A/B test, or deterministic hash), how you ensure your analytics can compare success rates across both providers, and how you define \"migration complete\" from a frontend perspective.\n202\t\n203\t---\n204\t\n205\t*Generated June 2026 — covers Stripe, Adyen, Braintree, PayPal, and general PSP patterns.*\n206\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ab96e0e-8f96-4d88-841c-51b1b26eaeef","uuid":"f867ea2f-7e52-4505-a7c4-63992aacda77","timestamp":"2026-06-20T19:44:03.273Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/payments-system-design-doc.md","content":"# Payments System Frontend System Design — Interview Questions\n\nA comprehensive reference of deep questions across all segments, organized by theme and difficulty. Covers the full frontend surface of a checkout and payment processing system (think Stripe, Braintree, PayPal, Adyen).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Checkout Flow & Form UX\n\n> Extremely common opening section — interviewers use checkout flow to probe component architecture, form validation strategy, and UX judgment all at once.\n\n### Core\n\n- Walk me through how you would architect a multi-step checkout flow (cart → shipping → payment → confirmation). Where does state live, how do you handle back-navigation, and how do you prevent users from skipping steps?\n- How do you design a credit card input form that provides real-time feedback — card type detection, formatted input masking (e.g., `4242 4242 4242 4242`), expiry validation, and CVV length rules — without blocking the user while they type?\n- What is the correct strategy for inline vs. summary error display in a payment form? When should you validate on `blur` vs. `change` vs. `submit`, and how do you avoid frustrating users with premature errors on partially-typed card numbers?\n- How do you handle address autocomplete (Google Places API, Smarty Streets) in a checkout form — including debouncing, fallback to manual entry when the API is unavailable, and ensuring the autofilled address is still validated server-side?\n- A user fills out the payment form and hits \"Pay Now,\" but the network request takes 3 seconds. Describe your loading state strategy: what is disabled, what is shown, and how do you prevent double-submission?\n- How would you design the order summary panel in a checkout flow so it stays in sync with cart mutations (quantity changes, coupon application, tax recalculation) without full-page reloads?\n- How do you approach progressive disclosure in a checkout form — e.g., showing the billing address form only when it differs from shipping, or revealing the installment options only for purchases above a threshold?\n\n### Deep\n\n- Stripe's \"Link\" feature auto-fills payment details for returning customers across merchants. If you were building a similar saved-payment-method flow, how would you design the UX handoff between \"guest checkout\" and \"recognized user\" without causing a jarring re-render mid-form, and how do you handle the case where the saved method has expired?\n- A/B tests on checkout forms consistently show that reducing the number of visible fields increases conversion — but fewer fields can also increase fraud and failed deliveries. How do you architect a checkout form component system that allows product and risk teams to toggle field visibility, validation rules, and required/optional status from a feature-flag config without frontend deploys?\n- Describe how you would implement a \"smart retry\" UX after a card decline. Specifically: how do you preserve the user's previously entered data (without re-storing raw card numbers), which fields do you clear vs. keep, and what messaging hierarchy do you use to distinguish a soft decline (insufficient funds) from a hard decline (stolen card) given that your frontend may only receive a generic error code?\n\n---\n\n## 2. Payment Security & PCI Compliance\n\n> Always asked for senior/staff roles. Interviewers expect you to know why iframes exist and what PCI DSS scope means for frontend architecture choices.\n\n### Core\n\n- What is PCI DSS scope, and how does using a hosted payment field solution like Stripe Elements or Braintree's Hosted Fields reduce the scope of your application's PCI compliance obligations?\n- How does Stripe Elements prevent your page from ever touching raw card data? Walk through the technical mechanism — what is rendered in your DOM, what lives in the Stripe iframe's origin, and what is exchanged between the two contexts via `postMessage`.\n- Why can't you simply style a cross-origin iframe with CSS from the parent page, and how do payment providers like Stripe solve this problem while keeping card data isolated? What are the trade-offs of their \"appearance\" configuration APIs?\n- Explain how a Content Security Policy (CSP) should be configured for a checkout page that loads Stripe.js. Which directives are required, which are commonly misconfigured (and why), and what does Stripe itself require you to allow that might feel uncomfortable from a security standpoint?\n- What is tokenization in the context of card payments? Walk through the lifecycle: the user enters a card number, Stripe creates a `PaymentMethod` object — what is sent to your server, what is never sent, and how does your server use that token to charge the card?\n- What is the risk of storing a Stripe `PaymentIntent` client secret in `localStorage` vs. a session cookie vs. an in-memory variable, and what happens if a malicious script on your page reads the client secret?\n- How do you prevent clickjacking on a checkout page, and why is `X-Frame-Options: DENY` insufficient on its own for a page that also embeds legitimate third-party iframes (like Stripe Elements)?\n\n### Deep\n\n- Stripe Elements renders card input fields inside cross-origin iframes. Your designer wants pixel-perfect custom fonts loaded from your CDN inside those fields. Walk through exactly what the browser's cross-origin isolation rules allow, what Stripe's `fonts` configuration option does under the hood, and what you cannot achieve regardless of configuration — then propose a design compromise that satisfies both security and branding requirements.\n- A penetration tester flags that your checkout page makes a `fetch` to `api.yoursite.com/payment-intent` from the browser, and the response contains the PaymentIntent `client_secret`. They argue this is a security vulnerability. How do you evaluate that claim? Under what conditions is it acceptable to expose a client secret to the browser, and what server-side and frontend controls must be in place to make this safe?\n- You are migrating from a legacy checkout form that directly POSTed raw card data to your own server (PCI SAQ D scope) to a Stripe Elements integration (PCI SAQ A scope). Describe the full migration strategy: how do you run both implementations in parallel for a staged rollout, how do you ensure no raw card data ever hits your new infrastructure, and how do you validate the cutover is complete from a compliance standpoint?\n\n---\n\n## 3. State Management & Transaction Lifecycle\n\n> Tests whether candidates understand the payment intent as a state machine and can reason about eventual consistency, idempotency, and race conditions on the frontend.\n\n### Core\n\n- A Stripe `PaymentIntent` moves through states: `requires_payment_method` → `requires_confirmation` → `requires_action` → `processing` → `succeeded` (or `requires_capture`, `canceled`). How does your frontend model this state machine, and how do you decide which UI to render at each transition?\n- What is idempotency in the context of payment requests, and how do you implement it on the frontend? Specifically, if a user clicks \"Pay\" and the request times out before you receive a response, how do you safely retry without charging the user twice?\n- How do you handle optimistic UI in a payment flow? Unlike a social media \"like,\" a payment has real monetary consequence if the optimistic update is wrong. Where do you draw the line between responsiveness and correctness?\n- Describe how you would manage the state of a multi-step checkout form across a full page refresh. What should be persisted (to `sessionStorage`, a URL param, or a server-side cart session), and what should be intentionally discarded to avoid security issues?\n- What happens to an in-flight payment confirmation if the user's browser tab is closed or the device loses power during the `processing` state? How does your frontend handle re-entry — e.g., the user re-opens the tab or returns to the site 10 minutes later?\n- How do you handle concurrent modifications to a shared cart — e.g., the same user opens checkout in two browser tabs simultaneously? How do you detect the conflict on the frontend and recover gracefully?\n- A user completes payment but the success redirect is intercepted by an ad blocker or a browser extension that strips query params. How do you design the confirmation flow so the user reaches a correct success state even if your `?payment_intent=pi_xxx&redirect_status=succeeded` URL param never arrives?\n\n### Deep\n\n- Walk me through implementing a robust payment retry loop on the frontend. The user's card was declined (soft decline). You want to: (1) allow the user to update their card details, (2) re-confirm the same `PaymentIntent` rather than creating a new one, and (3) cap retries at a safe limit to avoid locking the card. How do you manage the state transitions, and what data do you pass back to the `confirmCardPayment` call on a retry?\n- Describe how you would architect a frontend payment state machine using XState (or a comparable library). Define the states, events, guards, and side effects for the full lifecycle including 3DS authentication, network errors, and soft declines. What are the advantages of this approach over ad-hoc `if/else` logic in React component state?\n- Your checkout frontend runs inside a mobile WebView embedded in a native iOS/Android app. The native app and the WebView both need to know the payment outcome. Walk through the communication architecture: how does a payment confirmation event travel from the Stripe SDK (inside the WebView) through the `postMessage` bridge to the native layer, what are the failure modes, and how do you ensure exactly-once delivery of the success event to the native app?\n\n---\n\n## 4. Real-Time Updates & Webhooks\n\n> Tests understanding of the async gap between \"payment submitted\" and \"payment confirmed\" — a uniquely tricky problem in payment UX.\n\n### Core\n\n- After calling `stripe.confirmCardPayment()`, Stripe returns immediately with a `PaymentIntent` object. But the actual charge confirmation comes asynchronously via webhook. How do you reconcile the frontend's view of payment status with the authoritative server-side status, and when is it safe to show the user a success screen?\n- Compare polling, WebSockets, and Server-Sent Events (SSE) as mechanisms for delivering payment status updates to the frontend. Which would you choose for a payment confirmation flow, and why?\n- How would you implement a polling strategy for payment status that is resilient to transient network failures, doesn't hammer your server, and gives up gracefully after a timeout? Describe the backoff algorithm and the UX at each stage.\n- What is the risk of relying solely on the browser-side `stripe.confirmCardPayment()` return value to determine payment success, rather than verifying server-side via webhook? Give a specific attack scenario where this leads to revenue loss or fraud.\n- Describe the \"pending payment\" screen UX for a payment that enters `processing` state (common with bank transfers, SEPA debit, or certain card networks). What do you show the user, how long do you keep them on this screen, and what happens when they close the browser?\n- How do you handle a scenario where a webhook arrives at your server but the frontend user has already navigated away? How do you re-surface the payment outcome the next time the user visits?\n- Your server receives a `payment_intent.succeeded` webhook but the frontend is currently showing the user a \"payment failed\" error screen (because the initial API call timed out). How do you reconcile this and correct the UI?\n\n### Deep\n\n- Design a real-time payment status notification system that must work across: (a) an active checkout tab using SSE, (b) a user who has closed the tab but re-opens the site within 10 minutes, and (c) a mobile user who has backgrounded the app. Describe the full data flow from Stripe webhook → your backend → frontend for each case, including how you handle reconnection, missed events, and event deduplication.\n- Stripe sends webhooks with a `Stripe-Signature` header for verification. Your frontend needs to display a real-time status update the moment this webhook is processed. Walk through the full architecture: webhook receiver → verification → event storage → push to frontend. How do you ensure the frontend update is consistent with the database state and doesn't display a stale intermediate state?\n- You are building a payment dashboard that shows live transaction status for multiple concurrent payments (think a restaurant POS processing 20 orders simultaneously). Describe how you would design the WebSocket message schema, client-side store normalization, and render optimization to ensure the UI stays responsive and correct as events arrive out of order.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Performance & Core Web Vitals\n\n> A checkout page's performance directly impacts conversion rate — every 100ms of latency costs measurable revenue. Interviewers expect specific metrics and techniques.\n\n### Core\n\n- Stripe.js is a ~300KB third-party script. When and how should you load it, and why does Stripe's own documentation recommend loading it on every page of your site rather than only on the checkout page? What are the performance trade-offs of each approach?\n- How does injecting a Stripe Elements iframe into the DOM affect Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS), and what CSS techniques do you use to prevent the card input from causing layout shifts when it mounts?\n- Describe your bundle-splitting strategy for a checkout page. Which chunks are critical path, which are deferred, and how do you decide what to inline in the HTML vs. load asynchronously?\n- What is the impact of third-party payment SDKs (Stripe, PayPal button, Apple Pay, Google Pay) on your checkout page's Total Blocking Time (TBT) and Interaction to Next Paint (INP)? How do you load these without blocking the main thread?\n- How would you optimize the Time to Interactive (TTI) for a checkout page that requires: authentication state check, cart data fetch, Stripe.js load, and address form render — all before the user can type a card number?\n- Describe how you would use resource hints (`preconnect`, `prefetch`, `preload`) specifically for a checkout page that loads Stripe.js, Google Fonts for the branded card input, and a product image CDN.\n- What are the trade-offs between server-side rendering (SSR), static generation, and client-side rendering for a checkout page? Which approach do you use, and how does it affect Time to First Byte (TTFB) and the \"page is interactive\" moment?\n\n### Deep\n\n- A/B test results show that your checkout page has a 15% higher bounce rate on 3G mobile connections compared to competitors. Your LCP is 4.2s. Walk through a systematic performance audit: which tools do you use, what hypotheses do you form, and which specific optimizations do you implement for the Stripe SDK loading, hero image, and above-the-fold form render?\n- Stripe Elements renders inside an iframe, which means the browser must establish a separate network connection to `js.stripe.com`. Model the exact sequence of DNS lookup, TCP handshake, TLS negotiation, and iframe load for a user on a 50ms-latency mobile connection. Where are the optimization opportunities, and what is the irreducible minimum latency floor you cannot engineer around?\n- You are asked to implement a \"one-click checkout\" experience (similar to Shop Pay or Amazon 1-Click) where returning users can complete a purchase in under 2 seconds. Describe the full performance architecture: what is pre-fetched on the product page, what is pre-loaded on hover/tap, how is the PaymentIntent pre-created, and what is the critical rendering path once the user clicks \"Buy Now\"?\n\n---\n\n## 6. Error Handling & Resilience\n\n> Payment errors are high-stakes and high-frequency. Interviewers probe whether you can distinguish error types and build UX that recovers without losing the user.\n\n### Core\n\n- Enumerate the categories of errors that can occur in a frontend payment flow (network errors, card declines, validation errors, authentication failures, fraud blocks, rate limits) and describe how the error handling strategy differs for each category.\n- A user's card is declined with Stripe error code `card_declined` and decline code `insufficient_funds`. What do you show the user? What do you show the user if the decline code is `stolen_card`? How does your error message component know which codes warrant specific messaging vs. a generic \"payment failed\" message?\n- What is 3D Secure (3DS) authentication, when is it triggered, and how does `stripe.confirmCardPayment()` handle the 3DS challenge flow? What does the user experience look like, and what are the failure modes (user cancels, 3DS times out, bank's 3DS page is down)?\n- How do you distinguish between a network timeout (where the payment may or may not have processed) and a definitive payment failure (where you know the charge was rejected)? How does each case change your frontend error recovery strategy?\n- Describe your strategy for handling the case where Stripe.js itself fails to load (CDN outage, network error, ad blocker). Do you have a fallback, or do you fail gracefully? What does the user see, and what do you log?\n- How do you implement a circuit breaker pattern on the frontend for payment requests? If your payment API endpoint is returning 503s, how do you detect this condition and prevent the user from hammering a degraded backend?\n- What is the UX strategy for a payment that fails at the very last step — after the user has entered all their details and clicked \"Pay\" — but due to a server-side error rather than a card decline? How do you preserve their form state and communicate the error without inducing panic?\n\n### Deep\n\n- Walk me through the full 3DS2 authentication flow from a frontend architecture standpoint. Specifically: how does Stripe.js detect that 3DS is required after `confirmCardPayment`, how is the challenge rendered (in an iframe? a redirect? a modal?), how do you handle the case where the device fingerprinting step triggers a full redirect rather than a seamless iframe challenge, and what happens to your React component state across that redirect boundary?\n- You are building a checkout that must work in environments with extremely poor connectivity (rural mobile, flaky WiFi). Design a resilience strategy that includes: detecting offline state before submission, queuing the payment attempt for retry when connectivity returns, preventing duplicate charges, and communicating uncertainty to the user without causing them to abandon. What APIs do you use, and what are the limits of what you can guarantee on the frontend?\n- Your monitoring alerts that 8% of users who click \"Pay\" are seeing an unhandled JavaScript exception in the Stripe Elements payment confirmation step. You have Sentry traces showing the error originates inside the cross-origin Stripe iframe. What do you know, and what don't you know, from that error report? How do you diagnose the root cause given that you cannot inspect Stripe's iframe code, and what mitigations do you ship while the investigation is ongoing?\n\n---\n\n## 7. Internationalization & Localization\n\n> Often underweighted by candidates. A globally deployed payments frontend has uniquely complex i18n requirements around currency, local payment methods, and regulatory display rules.\n\n### Core\n\n- Describe how you format currency amounts in a payments UI across different locales. What does `Intl.NumberFormat` give you, where does it fall short (e.g., currencies with non-standard subunit counts like JPY or KWD), and how do you handle amounts that arrive from your API in minor units (cents)?\n- How do you display prices that include tax in markets where tax must be shown separately (US) vs. markets where prices must be shown tax-inclusive by law (EU, Australia)? How does this affect your pricing component's data contract and render logic?\n- What are the specific challenges of supporting RTL languages (Arabic, Hebrew) in a checkout form — beyond just `dir=\"rtl\"` on the container? Think about icon placement (card type icon, CVV help icon), number formatting, and error message positioning.\n- Stripe supports \"local payment methods\" (iDEAL in the Netherlands, BLIK in Poland, Pix in Brazil, UPI in India). How do you architect a payment method selector that is data-driven (configured per-country) rather than hardcoded, and how do each of these methods change the checkout UX flow?\n- How do you handle locale-specific date formatting in a payments context — specifically card expiry dates, invoice dates, and estimated delivery windows — given that `12/03` means March 12 in Europe and December 3 in the US?\n- What is your strategy for translating dynamic server error messages (card decline reasons, fraud messages) that arrive in English from your payment processor but need to be displayed in the user's language?\n- How do you support multiple currencies in a single checkout — e.g., a platform where the buyer is in Germany paying in EUR but the seller is in Canada receiving CAD? What does the UI need to display, and what data must come from the server vs. what can the frontend derive?\n\n### Deep\n\n- You are expanding checkout to Japan, which has several unique requirements: prices are always displayed as whole numbers (no decimal yen), the most popular payment method is convenience store payment (konbini) which is asynchronous and cash-based, and the address form field order is reversed (postal code → prefecture → city → street, then name in family-name-first order). Walk through the specific component and data model changes required, and how you architect the address form to be locale-driven rather than requiring a separate Japanese checkout page.\n- Stripe's `amount` field is always an integer in the currency's smallest unit. For most currencies this is cents, but for currencies like the Jordanian Dinar (3 decimal places, 1 JOD = 1000 fils) and currencies like the Japanese Yen (0 decimal places), the math changes. Build a robust currency utility module: given a `{amount: number, currency: string}` object, how do you correctly format the display value, and how do you validate user-entered amounts to prevent off-by-100x errors?\n- Design a payment method ranking and display system for a global checkout. The backend provides a list of available payment methods for the user's country and cart value. Your frontend must: rank them by local preference (e.g., iDEAL first in NL, not Visa), display their logos with appropriate localized labels, hide methods that don't support the cart currency, and gracefully degrade if the ranking config is unavailable. Describe the data schema, component hierarchy, and fallback behavior.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Observability & Analytics\n\n> Tells interviewers whether you think about the full product lifecycle, not just shipping code. For a payments frontend, data quality is revenue-critical.\n\n### Core\n\n- What events would you instrument in a checkout funnel to enable a product team to measure conversion at each step and identify where users are dropping off? Give specific event names, properties, and the conditions under which each fires.\n- How do you track \"payment abandonment\" — specifically distinguishing between: (a) a user who leaves the page before entering any payment details, (b) a user who starts entering card info but exits, and (c) a user who clicks \"Pay\" but the request fails? Why does this distinction matter for product decisions?\n- What is your strategy for tracking errors in a payment flow without accidentally logging sensitive card data (PANs, CVVs) to your analytics or error monitoring service? What specific fields or patterns do you sanitize before sending to Sentry or Datadog?\n- How do you measure the performance of the Stripe.js initialization and Elements mount time in your Real User Monitoring (RUM) data? What custom performance marks would you use, and how do you correlate slow load times with conversion drop-off?\n- Describe how you would build a real-time payment success rate dashboard. What metrics do you track (success rate, decline rate broken down by decline code, 3DS completion rate), and what is your alerting threshold that should page an on-call engineer?\n- How do you instrument the retry behavior after a card decline to understand whether your retry UX is effective? What metrics tell you the retry flow is working vs. that it is causing additional user frustration?\n- What is the risk of sending `payment_intent_id` or `charge_id` in analytics events (e.g., to Google Analytics or Amplitude), and how do you evaluate whether to include these identifiers?\n\n### Deep\n\n- You notice in your funnel data that 23% of users who reach the payment step never click \"Pay\" — they simply leave. Your checkout form has a 4-second load time for Stripe Elements on mobile. Walk through how you would design and execute an experiment to determine whether the Elements load time is causally responsible for the abandonment rate, versus other hypotheses (price shock, trust signals, required account creation). What instrumentation do you add, and how do you isolate the variable?\n- Design an observability system for a payments frontend that gives you the following within 60 seconds of a production incident: (1) the percentage of checkout attempts that are failing vs. succeeding in real time, (2) whether the failure is in the Stripe client SDK, your own API, or the network between them, and (3) which user segments (by country, payment method, device type) are most affected. Describe the events, aggregation pipeline, and dashboard panels you would build.\n- Your payment success rate drops from 94% to 87% after a deploy. You need to determine whether this is a frontend regression or a backend/Stripe issue. Describe your diagnostic playbook: which logs and metrics do you look at first, how do you correlate the deploy timestamp with the metric drop, how do you check whether Stripe has an ongoing incident, and what is your rollback decision criteria? Assume you have Datadog RUM, Sentry, and Stripe's Dashboard available.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Architecture & Provider Abstraction\n\n> Staff/principal level territory. Tests whether you can design a payment frontend that doesn't tightly couple to a single PSP, enabling multi-provider routing and future migration.\n\n### Core\n\n- How do you architect a frontend payment abstraction layer that can route to Stripe for some transactions, Adyen for others, and PayPal for a third segment — all without the checkout UI component knowing which PSP is being used?\n- Different PSPs have different client-side SDKs (Stripe.js, Adyen's Web Components, Braintree's client SDK). These all have different APIs for mounting card fields, confirming payments, and handling 3DS. How do you normalize these into a single interface that your checkout component talks to?\n- What is a \"payment method types\" configuration, and how do you design a frontend data model that is PSP-agnostic — capable of expressing \"card,\" \"bank transfer,\" \"wallet,\" and \"buy now pay later\" without encoding PSP-specific field names or token formats?\n- How do you handle the case where your provider abstraction layer must support PSPs that have fundamentally different authentication flows — e.g., Stripe's embedded iframe model vs. Adyen's full-page redirect for certain payment methods?\n- What are the risks of building a \"thin shim\" abstraction vs. a \"rich unified API\" abstraction over multiple PSPs? Where does each approach break down in practice?\n- How do you design the error model for a PSP abstraction layer? Stripe error codes differ from Adyen result codes, which differ from Braintree transaction statuses. How do you normalize these into a set of frontend-actionable error categories without losing the PSP-specific detail your support team needs?\n- How would you approach lazy-loading PSP SDKs so that Stripe.js is only loaded when Stripe is the selected provider, and Adyen's SDK is only loaded when Adyen is selected — while keeping the time-to-interactive acceptable?\n\n### Deep\n\n- You are building a multi-PSP checkout where Stripe handles cards, PayPal handles its own wallet flow, and Klarna handles BNPL — all on the same checkout page. Each SDK wants to mount its own UI components into your DOM. Describe the component mounting strategy, the event communication model between each third-party component and your React state, and how you ensure that only one payment method's UI is \"active\" at a time without leaking event listeners or iframe references.\n- Design the frontend architecture for a payment platform that must support provider failover: if Stripe returns a 5xx during `confirmCardPayment`, you want to retry the same charge attempt through Adyen within 2 seconds, without the user knowing a provider switch occurred. What constraints does this place on how you construct the PaymentIntent server-side, how you pass the client token to the frontend, and what the abstraction layer's retry logic looks like? Where does this approach fundamentally break down and require server-side coordination instead?\n- You are tasked with migrating a checkout from Braintree to Stripe over 6 months, with a gradual rollout. Both SDKs must be active simultaneously during the migration. Walk through: how you load both SDKs without doubling blocking script weight, how you route specific user cohorts to each provider (feature flag, A/B test, or deterministic hash), how you ensure your analytics can compare success rates across both providers, and how you define \"migration complete\" from a frontend perspective.\n\n---\n\n*Generated June 2026 — covers Stripe, Adyen, Braintree, PayPal, and general PSP patterns.*\n","numLines":206,"startLine":1,"totalLines":206}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01L9xmJArLopArE8ZPFH1u53","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t<!DOCTYPE html>\n2\t<html lang=\"en\">\n3\t<head>\n4\t  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n5\t  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n6\t  <title>Claude Frontend System — Interactive Architecture</title>\n7\t  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Interactive architecture map covering all 10 Claude-style AI chat frontend system design prep sections.\">\n8\t  <style>\n9\t    :root {\n10\t      --bg: #0f1219;\n11\t      --surface: #171c28;\n12\t      --surface2: #1e2536;\n13\t      --text: #e8ecf4;\n14\t      --muted: #8b95a8;\n15\t      --border: #2d3548;\n16\t      --accent: #c97840;\n17\t      --accent-soft: rgba(201, 120, 64, 0.15);\n18\t      --ui: #5b9bd5;\n19\t      --client: #70ad47;\n20\t      --transport: #ffc000;\n21\t      --api: #9966cc;\n22\t      --provider: #ed7d31;\n23\t      --data: #4472c4;\n24\t      --security: #e74c3c;\n25\t      --shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,.35);\n26\t    }\n27\t    @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {\n28\t      :root {\n29\t        --bg: #f4f2ef;\n30\t        --surface: #fff;\n31\t        --surface2: #faf8f5;\n32\t        --text: #1a1d26;\n33\t        --muted: #5c6370;\n34\t        --border: #e2e6ed;\n35\t        --accent: #b85c28;\n36\t        --accent-soft: rgba(184, 92, 40, 0.1);\n37\t        --shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.08);\n38\t      }\n39\t    }\n40\t    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }\n41\t    html, body { height: 100%; margin: 0; }\n42\t    body {\n43\t      font-family: \"Segoe UI\", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\n44\t      background: var(--bg);\n45\t      color: var(--text);\n46\t      overflow: hidden;\n47\t    }\n48\t    .app {\n49\t      display: grid;\n50\t      grid-template-columns: 280px 1fr 340px;\n51\t      grid-template-rows: auto 1fr;\n52\t      height: 100vh;\n53\t    }\n54\t    header {\n55\t      grid-column: 1 / -1;\n56\t      display: flex;\n57\t      align-items: center;\n58\t      gap: 1rem;\n59\t      padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;\n60\t      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n61\t      background: var(--surface);\n62\t    }\n63\t    header h1 {\n64\t      font-size: 1rem;\n65\t      font-weight: 700;\n66\t      margin: 0;\n67\t      letter-spacing: -0.02em;\n68\t    }\n69\t    header p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--muted); }\n70\t    .header-links { margin-left: auto; display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; }\n71\t    .header-links a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }\n72\t    .header-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }\n73\t\n74\t    .sidebar {\n75\t      border-right: 1px solid var(--border);\n76\t      background: var(--surface);\n77\t      overflow-y: auto;\n78\t      padding: 1rem;\n79\t    }\n80\t    .sidebar h2 {\n81\t      font-size: 0.6875rem;\n82\t      text-transform: uppercase;\n83\t      letter-spacing: 0.06em;\n84\t      color: var(--muted);\n85\t      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;\n86\t    }\n87\t    .sidebar section { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }\n88\t    .filter-group { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.35rem; }\n89\t    .chip {\n90\t      font-size: 0.75rem;\n91\t      padding: 0.25rem 0.55rem;\n92\t      border-radius: 999px;\n93\t      border: 1px solid var(--border);\n94\t      background: var(--surface2);\n95\t      color: var(--muted);\n96\t      cursor: pointer;\n97\t      user-select: none;\n98\t      transition: all 0.15s;\n99\t    }\n100\t    .chip:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--text); }\n101\t    .chip.active { background: var(--accent-soft); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }\n102\t    .chip.layer-ui.active { border-color: var(--ui); color: var(--ui); background: rgba(91,155,213,.12); }\n103\t    .chip.layer-client.active { border-color: var(--client); color: var(--client); background: rgba(112,173,71,.12); }\n104\t    .chip.layer-transport.active { border-color: var(--transport); color: #b8860b; background: rgba(255,192,0,.12); }\n105\t    .chip.layer-api.active { border-color: var(--api); color: var(--api); background: rgba(153,102,204,.12); }\n106\t    .chip.layer-provider.active { border-color: var(--provider); color: var(--provider); background: rgba(237,125,49,.12); }\n107\t    .chip.layer-data.active { border-color: var(--data); color: var(--data); background: rgba(68,114,196,.12); }\n108\t    .chip.layer-security.active { border-color: var(--security); color: var(--security); background: rgba(231,76,60,.12); }\n109\t\n110\t    select, input[type=\"search\"] {\n111\t      width: 100%;\n112\t      font: inherit;\n113\t      font-size: 0.8125rem;\n114\t      padding: 0.45rem 0.65rem;\n115\t      border: 1px solid var(--border);\n116\t      border-radius: 6px;\n117\t      background: var(--surface2);\n118\t      color: var(--text);\n119\t    }\n120\t    .flow-btn {\n121\t      display: block;\n122\t      width: 100%;\n123\t      text-align: left;\n124\t      font: inherit;\n125\t      font-size: 0.8125rem;\n126\t      padding: 0.5rem 0.65rem;\n127\t      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;\n128\t      border: 1px solid var(--border);\n129\t      border-radius: 6px;\n130\t      background: var(--surface2);\n131\t      color: var(--text);\n132\t      cursor: pointer;\n133\t    }\n134\t    .flow-btn:hover, .flow-btn.active { border-color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft); }\n135\t    .legend { font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }\n136\t    .legend span { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 4px; vertical-align: middle; }\n137\t\n138\t    .canvas-wrap {\n139\t      position: relative;\n140\t      overflow: hidden;\n141\t      background:\n142\t        radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgba(201,120,64,.06), transparent 50%),\n143\t        var(--bg);\n144\t    }\n145\t    .canvas-toolbar {\n146\t      position: absolute;\n147\t      top: 0.75rem;\n148\t      left: 0.75rem;\n149\t      z-index: 5;\n150\t      display: flex;\n151\t      gap: 0.35rem;\n152\t    }\n153\t    .canvas-toolbar button {\n154\t      font: inherit;\n155\t      font-size: 0.75rem;\n156\t      padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem;\n157\t      border: 1px solid var(--border);\n158\t      border-radius: 6px;\n159\t      background: var(--surface);\n160\t      color: var(--text);\n161\t      cursor: pointer;\n162\t    }\n163\t    .canvas {\n164\t      width: 100%;\n165\t      height: 100%;\n166\t      cursor: grab;\n167\t      touch-action: none;\n168\t    }\n169\t    .canvas.dragging { cursor: grabbing; }\n170\t    .diagram-inner {\n171\t      position: absolute;\n172\t      width: 1200px;\n173\t      height: 920px;\n174\t      transform-origin: 0 0;\n175\t    }\n176\t    svg.connections {\n177\t      position: absolute;\n178\t      inset: 0;\n179\t      width: 100%;\n180\t      height: 100%;\n181\t      pointer-events: none;\n182\t    }\n183\t    svg.connections line, svg.connections path {\n184\t      stroke: var(--border);\n185\t      stroke-width: 1.5;\n186\t      fill: none;\n187\t      transition: stroke 0.2s, stroke-width 0.2s;\n188\t    }\n189\t    svg.connections .flow-active {\n190\t      stroke: var(--accent);\n191\t      stroke-width: 2.5;\n192\t      stroke-dasharray: 8 4;\n193\t      animation: flowDash 0.6s linear infinite;\n194\t    }\n195\t    @keyframes flowDash { to { stroke-dashoffset: -12; } }\n196\t\n197\t    .lane {\n198\t      position: absolute;\n199\t      left: 12px;\n200\t      right: 12px;\n201\t      border: 1px dashed var(--border);\n202\t      border-radius: 10px;\n203\t      background: rgba(255,255,255,.02);\n204\t    }\n205\t    .lane-label {\n206\t      position: absolute;\n207\t      left: 12px;\n208\t      top: 6px;\n209\t      font-size: 0.6875rem;\n210\t      font-weight: 700;\n211\t      text-transform: uppercase;\n212\t      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n213\t      color: var(--muted);\n214\t    }\n215\t    .node {\n216\t      position: absolute;\n217\t      width: 148px;\n218\t      padding: 0.55rem 0.65rem;\n219\t      border-radius: 8px;\n220\t      border: 2px solid var(--border);\n221\t      background: var(--surface);\n222\t      font-size: 0.75rem;\n223\t      line-height: 1.35;\n224\t      cursor: pointer;\n225\t      transition: transform 0.15s, box-shadow 0.15s, opacity 0.2s, border-color 0.15s;\n226\t      box-shadow: var(--shadow);\n227\t    }\n228\t    .node:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); z-index: 10; }\n229\t    .node.selected { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--accent-soft); z-index: 11; }\n230\t    .node.dimmed { opacity: 0.2; pointer-events: none; }\n231\t    .node.highlight { border-color: var(--accent); animation: pulse 1s ease infinite; }\n232\t    @keyframes pulse { 50% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--accent-soft); } }\n233\t    .node-title { font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.15rem; }\n234\t    .node-sub { font-size: 0.6875rem; color: var(--muted); }\n235\t    .node-tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px; margin-top: 0.35rem; }\n236\t    .node-tag {\n237\t      font-size: 0.5625rem;\n238\t      padding: 1px 4px;\n239\t      border-radius: 3px;\n240\t      background: var(--surface2);\n241\t      color: var(--muted);\n242\t    }\n243\t    .node[data-layer=\"ui\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--ui); }\n244\t    .node[data-layer=\"client\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--client); }\n245\t    .node[data-layer=\"transport\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--transport); }\n246\t    .node[data-layer=\"api\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--api); }\n247\t    .node[data-layer=\"provider\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--provider); }\n248\t    .node[data-layer=\"data\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--data); }\n249\t    .node[data-layer=\"security\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--security); }\n250\t\n251\t    .detail {\n252\t      border-left: 1px solid var(--border);\n253\t      background: var(--surface);\n254\t      overflow-y: auto;\n255\t      padding: 1.25rem;\n256\t    }\n257\t    .detail-empty { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center; }\n258\t    .detail h2 { font-size: 1.125rem; margin: 0 0 0.35rem; }\n259\t    .detail .layer-badge {\n260\t      display: inline-block;\n261\t      font-size: 0.6875rem;\n262\t      font-weight: 700;\n263\t      text-transform: uppercase;\n264\t      padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;\n265\t      border-radius: 4px;\n266\t      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n267\t    }\n268\t    .detail p { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }\n269\t    .detail h3 { font-size: 0.8125rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--accent); margin: 1rem 0 0.4rem; }\n270\t    .detail ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.55; }\n271\t    .detail li { margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }\n272\t    .section-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; }\n273\t    .section-links a {\n274\t      font-size: 0.75rem;\n275\t      padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;\n276\t      border-radius: 4px;\n277\t      background: var(--accent-soft);\n278\t      color: var(--accent);\n279\t      text-decoration: none;\n280\t    }\n281\t    .section-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }\n282\t    .flow-step {\n283\t      font-size: 0.8125rem;\n284\t      padding: 0.5rem 0.65rem;\n285\t      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;\n286\t      border-left: 3px solid var(--border);\n287\t      background: var(--surface2);\n288\t      border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;\n289\t    }\n290\t    .flow-step.active { border-left-color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft); }\n291\t\n292\t    @media (max-width: 1100px) {\n293\t      .app { grid-template-columns: 1fr; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr auto; overflow-y: auto; height: auto; min-height: 100vh; }\n294\t      body { overflow: auto; }\n295\t      .sidebar { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); max-height: none; }\n296\t      .canvas-wrap { min-height: 520px; }\n297\t      .detail { border-left: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); max-height: none; }\n298\t    }\n299\t  </style>\n300\t</head>\n301\t<body>\n302\t  <div class=\"app\">\n303\t    <header>\n304\t      <div>\n305\t        <h1>Claude Frontend System Architecture</h1>\n306\t        <p>Interactive map · all 10 prep sections</p>\n307\t      </div>\n308\t      <div class=\"header-links\">\n309\t        <a href=\"answers-html/index.html\">Answer pages</a>\n310\t        <a href=\"Claude-design-doc.md\">Question bank</a>\n311\t      </div>\n312\t    </header>\n313\t\n314\t    <aside class=\"sidebar\">\n315\t      <section>\n316\t        <h2>Search</h2>\n317\t        <input type=\"search\" id=\"search\" placeholder=\"Filter nodes…\" autocomplete=\"off\">\n318\t      </section>\n319\t      <section>\n320\t        <h2>Layer filter</h2>\n321\t        <div class=\"filter-group\" id=\"layerFilters\"></div>\n322\t      </section>\n323\t      <section>\n324\t        <h2>Section filter</h2>\n325\t        <div class=\"filter-group\" id=\"sectionFilters\"></div>\n326\t      </section>\n327\t      <section>\n328\t        <h2>Walk a flow</h2>\n329\t        <div id=\"flowButtons\"></div>\n330\t      </section>\n331\t      <section>\n332\t        <h2>Legend</h2>\n333\t        <div class=\"legend\" id=\"legend\"></div>\n334\t      </section>\n335\t    </aside>\n336\t\n337\t    <main class=\"canvas-wrap\">\n338\t      <div class=\"canvas-toolbar\">\n339\t        <button type=\"button\" id=\"zoomIn\">+</button>\n340\t        <button type=\"button\" id=\"zoomOut\">−</button>\n341\t        <button type=\"button\" id=\"resetView\">Reset view</button>\n342\t      </div>\n343\t      <div class=\"canvas\" id=\"canvas\">\n344\t        <div class=\"diagram-inner\" id=\"diagram\">\n345\t          <svg class=\"connections\" id=\"connections\"></svg>\n346\t        </div>\n347\t      </div>\n348\t    </main>\n349\t\n350\t    <aside class=\"detail\" id=\"detailPanel\">\n351\t      <div class=\"detail-empty\" id=\"detailEmpty\">\n352\t        Click a node or run a flow walkthrough to see details, interview angles, and links to answer sections.\n353\t      </div>\n354\t      <div id=\"detailContent\" hidden></div>\n355\t    </aside>\n356\t  </div>\n357\t\n358\t  <script>\n359\t    const LAYERS = {\n360\t      ui: { label: 'UI Surfaces', color: 'var(--ui)' },\n361\t      client: { label: 'Client State', color: 'var(--client)' },\n362\t      transport: { label: 'Transport', color: 'var(--transport)' },\n363\t      api: { label: 'API / BFF', color: 'var(--api)' },\n364\t      provider: { label: 'Providers', color: 'var(--provider)' },\n365\t      data: { label: 'Data', color: 'var(--data)' },\n366\t      security: { label: 'Security', color: 'var(--security)' }\n367\t    };\n368\t\n369\t    const SECTIONS = [\n370\t      { id: '01', name: 'Streaming', file: 'answers-html/01-streaming-real-time-rendering.html' },\n371\t      { id: '02', name: 'State', file: 'answers-html/02-conversation-state-management.html' },\n372\t      { id: '03', name: 'MCP Tools', file: 'answers-html/03-mcp-tool-use-ui.html' },\n373\t      { id: '04', name: 'Artifacts', file: 'answers-html/04-artifacts-sandboxed-rendering.html' },\n374\t      { id: '05', name: 'Performance', file: 'answers-html/05-performance-scalability.html' },\n375\t      { id: '06', name: 'Auth', file: 'answers-html/06-auth-security-multitenancy.html' },\n376\t      { id: '07', name: 'Resilience', file: 'answers-html/07-offline-resilience-error-handling.html' },\n377\t      { id: '08', name: 'Input', file: 'answers-html/08-input-multimodal-ux.html' },\n378\t      { id: '09', name: 'Providers', file: 'answers-html/09-api-design-provider-abstraction.html' },\n379\t      { id: '10', name: 'Killer Qs', file: 'answers-html/10-killer-questions.html' }\n380\t    ];\n381\t\n382\t    const NODES = [\n383\t      { id: 'composer', layer: 'ui', x: 40, y: 48, title: 'Composer', sub: 'Input · attach · send/stop', sections: ['02','08','01'],\n384\t        desc: 'Captures drafts, multimodal attachments, slash commands, token estimate, and stop-generation. Never part of the committed message graph until send.',\n385\t        bullets: ['Auto-grow textarea with max height cap', 'AttachmentController: drag/drop/paste', 'AbortController wired to active SSE stream', 'Draft in localStorage/IDB, separate from graph'],\n386\t        questions: ['Draft persistence', 'Mixed multimodal send', 'Stop generation chain'] },\n387\t      { id: 'sidebar', layer: 'ui', x: 220, y: 48, title: 'Sidebar', sub: '10k convos · search', sections: ['05','10','02'],\n388\t        desc: 'Virtualized conversation list with metadata-only rows, cursor pagination, FTS search, optimistic rename/delete.',\n389\t        bullets: ['Prefetch on hover/focus', 'IndexedDB cache ~1000 rows', 'No message bodies in list rows'],\n390\t        questions: ['Sidebar at 10k scale', 'Preload next conversation'] },\n391\t      { id: 'msgList', layer: 'ui', x: 400, y: 48, title: 'Message List', sub: 'Virtualized thread', sections: ['01','05','02'],\n392\t        desc: 'Windowed view of active branch path. Pinned streaming row, scroll anchoring, dynamic height cache.',\n393\t        bullets: ['Only visible rows in DOM', 'isPinnedToBottom + \"New messages ↓\"', 'Stable keys per markdown block'],\n394\t        questions: ['Virtualize 500 messages', 'Scroll anchoring', 'Avoid full-list re-render'] },\n395\t      { id: 'streamBubble', layer: 'ui', x: 580, y: 48, title: 'Streaming Bubble', sub: 'Typing → tokens → done', sections: ['01'],\n396\t        desc: 'Single assistant slot: pending indicator crossfades into incremental markdown render.',\n397\t        bullets: ['rAF batching decouples network from paint', 'Incomplete fence/table state machines', 'Backpressure: pause read(), shed highlight'],\n398\t        questions: ['Layout thrash', 'Token throttle', 'Open code fence', 'Backpressure'] },\n399\t      { id: 'toolPills', layer: 'ui', x: 760, y: 48, title: 'Tool Pills', sub: 'HITL · chains · audit', sections: ['03','06','10'],\n400\t        desc: 'Per tool_use_id UI: loading → success/error, confirm card for destructive actions, trust/egress disclosure.',\n401\t        bullets: ['UI lock + idempotency key on confirm', 'Multi-step stepper in one turn', 'Activity drawer for audit trail'],\n402\t        questions: ['Double confirm in 200ms', 'tool_result as user role', 'MCP OAuth expiry'] },\n403\t      { id: 'artifactPanel', layer: 'ui', x: 940, y: 48, title: 'Artifact Panel', sub: 'Editor + preview', sections: ['04','10'],\n404\t        desc: 'Code editor + sandboxed live preview with version timeline, diff, revert.',\n405\t        bullets: ['Heartbeat detects infinite render loops', 'postMessage bridge host ↔ iframe', 'Debounced compile in worker'],\n406\t        questions: ['iframe sandbox + CSP', 'Infinite loop detection', 'Version/revert'] },\n407\t\n408\t      { id: 'convStore', layer: 'client', x: 120, y: 200, title: 'Conversation Store', sub: 'Graph view + active leaf', sections: ['02','10'],\n409\t        desc: 'Client mirror of server message tree. Derives linear visible path via active_leaf_id. Optimistic nodes with clientRequestId.',\n410\t        bullets: ['Edit = sibling fork, not overwrite', 'Branch switcher swaps active leaf', 'BroadcastChannel for multi-tab'],\n411\t        questions: ['Edit message N', 'Branching model', 'Multi-tab sync'] },\n412\t      { id: 'streamPipeline', layer: 'client', x: 320, y: 200, title: 'Streaming Pipeline', sub: 'Buffer · parse · patch', sections: ['01','05'],\n413\t        desc: 'Token ring buffer → rAF flush → incremental markdown blocks → stable DOM patch.',\n414\t        bullets: ['Refs hold hot string; state commits per frame', 'startTransition for responsiveness', 'Canonical string never dropped on shed work'],\n415\t        questions: ['Buffer interval', 'Debounced markdown parse', 'Render lag metrics'] },\n416\t      { id: 'branchAsm', layer: 'client', x: 520, y: 200, title: 'Branch Assembler', sub: 'pathToLeaf · token budget', sections: ['02','09','10'],\n417\t        desc: 'Walk active leaf to root, reverse to chronological order, apply context window truncate/summarize policy.',\n418\t        bullets: ['Preview on client; server authoritative', 'IR blocks compiled at adapter boundary', 'Summary nodes on long threads'],\n419\t        questions: ['Context window strategy', 'Reassemble after edit', 'Provider normalization'] },\n420\t      { id: 'outbox', layer: 'client', x: 720, y: 200, title: 'Outbox Queue', sub: 'Offline · IDB', sections: ['07','02'],\n421\t        desc: 'IndexedDB queue for offline sends and upload resume. FIFO drain on reconnect with Idempotency-Key.',\n422\t        bullets: ['Optimistic user bubble while queued', 'Leader election across tabs', 'Conflict on conversation_revision mismatch'],\n423\t        questions: ['Offline message queue', 'Stream drop recovery'] },\n424\t      { id: 'clientCache', layer: 'client', x: 920, y: 200, title: 'Client Cache', sub: 'Memory · IDB · RQ', sections: ['05','02'],\n425\t        desc: 'Three-tier: in-memory hot set, IndexedDB pages, React Query server sync. Org-scoped namespaces.',\n426\t        bullets: ['LRU ~20 threads in memory', 'Paginated history prepend on scroll-up', 'Height cache for virtualizer'],\n427\t        questions: ['Caching strategy', 'Lazy-load history'] },\n428\t\n429\t      { id: 'rest', layer: 'transport', x: 200, y: 352, title: 'REST', sub: 'CRUD · control · upload', sections: ['01','07','08','03'],\n430\t        desc: 'Send message, cancel, tool execute, paginated history, presigned uploads, search, share links.',\n431\t        bullets: ['Idempotency-Key on destructive ops', 'PATCH events + revision vector', 'parseApiError taxonomy'],\n432\t        questions: ['Cancel/retry control plane', 'Error taxonomy', 'Chunked uploads'] },\n433\t      { id: 'sse', layer: 'transport', x: 480, y: 352, title: 'SSE Stream', sub: 'Token · tool · status', sections: ['01','07','09'],\n434\t        desc: 'Default LLM output transport. fetch + ReadableStream or EventSource with Last-Event-ID reconnect.',\n435\t        bullets: ['AbortController closes HTTP → stops billing', 'Resume via generation_id + cursor', 'Exponential backoff on drop'],\n436\t        questions: ['SSE vs WebSocket', 'Stream drop at token 400', 'Resume stream'] },\n437\t      { id: 'ws', layer: 'transport', x: 760, y: 352, title: 'WebSocket', sub: 'Optional sync', sections: ['01','02'],\n438\t        desc: 'Bidirectional session sync, presence, async job updates. Hybrid: SSE tokens + WS patches.',\n439\t        bullets: ['Manual heartbeat + resume protocol', 'Use when client→server churn is high', 'Not default for pure completion streams'],\n440\t        questions: ['When to pick WS', 'Multi-tab fan-out'] },\n441\t\n442\t      { id: 'gateway', layer: 'api', x: 80, y: 504, title: 'API Gateway', sub: 'Auth · rate limit', sections: ['06','07'],\n443\t        desc: 'JWT validation, org context, rate limiting, request shedding, stream lease issuance.',\n444\t        bullets: ['ctx from claims never body user_id', 'session_version invalidates access tokens', 'Stream lease for in-flight generation'],\n445\t        questions: ['JWT + RLS scoping', 'Session invalidate mid-stream', 'Rate limit UX'] },\n446\t      { id: 'convSvc', layer: 'api', x: 280, y: 504, title: 'Conversation Svc', sub: 'Graph CRUD · share', sections: ['02','06','10'],\n447\t        desc: 'Message nodes tree, branching edits, public share tokens, conversation search metadata.',\n448\t        bullets: ['message_nodes: parent_id, status, branch_label', 'active_leaf_id on conversation row', '409 on concurrent generation'],\n449\t        questions: ['Edit creates sibling node', 'Public share permissions', 'Org isolation'] },\n450\t      { id: 'streamGw', layer: 'api', x: 480, y: 504, title: 'Stream Gateway', sub: 'Checkpoints · replay', sections: ['01','07','10'],\n451\t        desc: 'Inference proxy: streams normalized events, writes partial checkpoints, supports resume cursor.',\n452\t        bullets: ['Debounced DB checkpoint every N tokens', 'Redis event buffer for Last-Event-ID', 'generation_id correlates client/server'],\n453\t        questions: ['Partial persist mid-stream', 'Continue from prefix fallback'] },\n454\t      { id: 'orchestrator', layer: 'api', x: 680, y: 504, title: 'Agent Orchestrator', sub: 'Tool loop · tasks', sections: ['03','09','10'],\n455\t        desc: 'Runs LLM ↔ tool cycles, agent task state machine, pause/resume on auth_required.',\n456\t        bullets: ['pending_tool_executions table', 'paused_auth + SSE auth_required event', 'Resume with same idempotency key'],\n457\t        questions: ['Multi-step tool chains', 'MCP OAuth mid-task', '529 fallback routing'] },\n458\t      { id: 'mcpClient', layer: 'api', x: 880, y: 504, title: 'MCP Client', sub: 'Policy · egress · audit', sections: ['03','06'],\n459\t        desc: 'Sandboxed tool execution with allowlisted egress, data minimization, immutable audit log.',\n460\t        bullets: ['Never pass full history to hostile MCP', 'Policy engine before network', 'Hashes in compliance log'],\n461\t        questions: ['Trust boundary UI', 'Malicious MCP exfiltration', 'Audit logging'] },\n462\t\n463\t      { id: 'irAdapter', layer: 'provider', x: 320, y: 656, title: 'IR + Adapters', sub: 'Anthropic · OpenAI · Gemini', sections: ['09','03'],\n464\t        desc: 'Internal representation compiled at boundary: system field vs message, tool_use vs tool role, thinking blocks.',\n465\t        bullets: ['CapabilityResolver not if(provider) in UI', 'NormalizedStreamEvent reducer', 'Model alias → pinned model_id per message'],\n466\t        questions: ['Normalize history', 'Streaming adapter', 'Extended thinking flag'] },\n467\t      { id: 'llm', layer: 'provider', x: 560, y: 656, title: 'LLM APIs', sub: 'Primary + fallback', sections: ['09','01','07'],\n468\t        desc: 'Provider SDK streams with 529 backoff, capability-matched fallback, cost estimation pre-send.',\n469\t        bullets: ['No silent stitch of two models in one bubble', 'Mid-stream: surface interrupted', 'Token counter per provider shape'],\n470\t        questions: ['Model fallback', 'Cost estimate', 'Model deprecation'] },\n471\t      { id: 'mcpServers', layer: 'provider', x: 800, y: 656, title: 'MCP Servers', sub: 'Slack · Calendar · …', sections: ['03','06'],\n472\t        desc: 'Third-party integrations via OAuth token vault (server-only refresh with serialized lock).',\n473\t        bullets: ['OAuth refresh mid-conversation', 'Scoped args only', 'Timeout → pill failed + user retry/skip'],\n474\t        questions: ['OAuth token refresh', 'Tool timeout 30s'] },\n475\t\n476\t      { id: 'pgGraph', layer: 'data', x: 160, y: 808, title: 'Postgres Graph', sub: 'Nodes · branches · ACL', sections: ['02','06','10'],\n477\t        desc: 'Source of truth: message tree, memberships, shares, agent_tasks, artifact version chain.',\n478\t        bullets: ['RLS: org_id + owner_user_id', 'status: streaming → interrupted → final', 'Unique generation_id constraint'],\n479\t        questions: ['Tree vs linear array', 'Partial message in DB'] },\n480\t      { id: 'redis', layer: 'data', x: 400, y: 808, title: 'Redis', sub: 'Locks · replay · dedup', sections: ['07','03','02'],\n481\t        desc: 'Active branch pointer, SSE replay buffer, idempotency TTL, session denylist, stream checkpoints.',\n482\t        bullets: ['(user_id, idempotency_key) dedup', 'Short TTL event buffer', 'Refresh lock for OAuth'],\n483\t        questions: ['Double booking dedup', 'SSE reconnect replay'] },\n484\t      { id: 'objectStore', layer: 'data', x: 640, y: 808, title: 'Object Storage', sub: 'Uploads · artifacts', sections: ['08','04','06'],\n485\t        desc: 'Quarantine bucket, presigned multipart uploads, attachment CDN URLs, WORM audit exports.',\n486\t        bullets: ['Magic-byte sniff at ingest', 'Stable fileId refs not base64 in state', 'Per-org S3 prefix'],\n487\t        questions: ['Large file uploads', 'PDF extract pipeline', 'Upload quarantine'] },\n488\t      { id: 'indexedDb', layer: 'data', x: 880, y: 808, title: 'IndexedDB', sub: 'Client pages · outbox', sections: ['05','07','02'],\n489\t        desc: 'Browser persistence: message pages, sidebar cache, offline outbox, upload session resume.',\n490\t        bullets: ['Key: userId:orgId:conversationId', 'BroadcastChannel invalidation', 'Partial stream on disconnect'],\n491\t        questions: ['Client cache tiers', 'Offline replay'] },\n492\t\n493\t      { id: 'authBoundary', layer: 'security', x: 40, y: 656, title: 'Auth Boundary', sub: 'JWT · org · RLS', sections: ['06'],\n494\t        desc: 'Every request derives tenant from token/key record. Defense in depth: API filter + Postgres RLS.',\n495\t        bullets: ['Multi-org context switch aborts streams', 'API key org bound, scopes enforced', 'Share token capability URL'],\n496\t        questions: ['Org switching', 'API key scope', 'Public link permissions'] },\n497\t      { id: 'sandbox', layer: 'security', x: 1040, y: 200, title: 'Sandbox iframe', sub: 'CSP · postMessage', sections: ['04','10'],\n498\t        desc: 'Origin-isolated artifact preview. allow-scripts only, no allow-same-origin. Heartbeat + render budget.',\n499\t        bullets: ['CDN imports via vendor proxy or block', 'Kill iframe on RENDER_LOOP', 'Replace iframe as recovery unit'],\n500\t        questions: ['Sandbox attacks prevented', 'Infinite loop in React artifact'] },\n501\t      { id: 'contentFw', layer: 'security', x: 1040, y: 504, title: 'Content Firewall', sub: 'Upload · inject', sections: ['06','08'],\n502\t        desc: 'Extracted upload text wrapped as untrusted document; never in system role. Instruction pattern stripping.',\n503\t        bullets: ['Client extract vs server OCR for PDF', 'Prompt injection via hidden PDF text', 'Page/token caps'],\n504\t        questions: ['Prompt injection uploads', 'PDF handling'] }\n505\t    ];\n506\t\n507\t    const EDGES = [\n508\t      ['composer', 'rest', 'POST send'],\n509\t      ['composer', 'sse', 'Abort stop'],\n510\t      ['composer', 'convStore', 'optimistic user node'],\n511\t      ['sidebar', 'clientCache', 'prefetch metadata'],\n512\t      ['msgList', 'streamPipeline', 'render commits'],\n513\t      ['streamBubble', 'streamPipeline', 'token buffer'],\n514\t      ['toolPills', 'rest', 'confirm execute'],\n515\t      ['artifactPanel', 'sandbox', 'postMessage'],\n516\t      ['convStore', 'branchAsm', 'active leaf path'],\n517\t      ['convStore', 'outbox', 'offline queue'],\n518\t      ['streamPipeline', 'convStore', 'finalize assistant'],\n519\t      ['streamPipeline', 'artifactPanel', 'code fence deltas'],\n520\t      ['branchAsm', 'rest', 'compiled context preview'],\n521\t      ['clientCache', 'msgList', 'history pages'],\n522\t      ['rest', 'gateway', 'HTTP'],\n523\t      ['sse', 'streamGw', 'token stream'],\n524\t      ['ws', 'convSvc', 'patch events'],\n525\t      ['gateway', 'convSvc', 'authorized'],\n526\t      ['convSvc', 'pgGraph', 'persist graph'],\n527\t      ['streamGw', 'orchestrator', 'generation job'],\n528\t      ['streamGw', 'sse', 'normalized events'],\n529\t      ['orchestrator', 'irAdapter', 'IR compile'],\n530\t      ['orchestrator', 'mcpClient', 'tool_use'],\n531\t      ['mcpClient', 'mcpServers', 'scoped call'],\n532\t      ['mcpClient', 'convStore', 'tool_result blocks'],\n533\t      ['irAdapter', 'llm', 'provider SDK'],\n534\t      ['streamGw', 'redis', 'checkpoints'],\n535\t      ['mcpClient', 'redis', 'idempotency'],\n536\t      ['rest', 'objectStore', 'presign upload'],\n537\t      ['clientCache', 'indexedDb', 'hydrate'],\n538\t      ['authBoundary', 'gateway', 'ctx claims'],\n539\t      ['contentFw', 'orchestrator', 'sanitized blocks'],\n540\t      ['objectStore', 'contentFw', 'extract pipeline']\n541\t    ];\n542\t\n543\t    const FLOWS = {\n544\t      send: {\n545\t        title: 'Send message → stream response',\n546\t        steps: [\n547\t          { nodes: ['composer'], text: 'User sends; optimistic user node appended to store' },\n548\t          { nodes: ['rest', 'gateway', 'convSvc'], text: 'POST validated; graph node persisted; generation leased' },\n549\t          { nodes: ['streamGw', 'orchestrator', 'irAdapter', 'llm'], text: 'IR compiled; provider streams tokens' },\n550\t          { nodes: ['sse', 'streamPipeline', 'streamBubble'], text: 'SSE chunks batched via rAF into markdown blocks' },\n551\t          { nodes: ['convStore', 'pgGraph'], text: 'Stream end finalizes assistant node in graph + DB' }\n552\t        ],\n553\t        sections: ['01','02','09']\n554\t      },\n555\t      tool: {\n556\t        title: 'Tool call → HITL confirm → resume',\n557\t        steps: [\n558\t          { nodes: ['llm', 'orchestrator'], text: 'Model emits tool_use block in stream' },\n559\t          { nodes: ['toolPills', 'streamBubble'], text: 'Pill shows loading; sensitive tools show confirm + egress disclosure' },\n560\t          { nodes: ['rest', 'mcpClient', 'redis'], text: 'Confirm POST with idempotency key; dedup if double-clicked' },\n561\t          { nodes: ['mcpServers'], text: 'MCP executes with minimized args; audit log written' },\n562\t          { nodes: ['convStore', 'orchestrator', 'llm'], text: 'tool_result as user blocks; model turn resumes' }\n563\t        ],\n564\t        sections: ['03','10']\n565\t      },\n566\t      drop: {\n567\t        title: 'Stream drops at token 400/1000',\n568\t        steps: [\n569\t          { nodes: ['sse', 'streamPipeline'], text: 'TCP close; partial text retained in bubble (never blank)' },\n570\t          { nodes: ['streamGw', 'redis', 'pgGraph'], text: 'Checkpoint row status=interrupted; cursor persisted' },\n571\t          { nodes: ['streamBubble', 'rest'], text: 'UI: Continue (resume cursor) | Retry (idempotent regen)' },\n572\t          { nodes: ['outbox', 'indexedDb'], text: 'Client mirrors partial in IDB for refresh survival' }\n573\t        ],\n574\t        sections: ['07','10','01']\n575\t      },\n576\t      edit: {\n577\t        title: 'Edit message N → branch regen',\n578\t        steps: [\n579\t          { nodes: ['composer', 'convStore'], text: 'Edit creates sibling node under same parent (fork, not overwrite)' },\n580\t          { nodes: ['branchAsm'], text: 'New active_leaf; path reassembled with token budget' },\n581\t          { nodes: ['convSvc', 'pgGraph'], text: 'Server persists branch; returns branch_generation/version' },\n582\t          { nodes: ['msgList'], text: 'UI swaps visible path; optional branch switcher keeps both subtrees' }\n583\t        ],\n584\t        sections: ['02','10']\n585\t      },\n586\t      artifact: {\n587\t        title: 'Artifact stream → sandbox preview',\n588\t        steps: [\n589\t          { nodes: ['streamPipeline', 'artifactPanel'], text: 'Code fence deltas debounced in worker' },\n590\t          { nodes: ['sandbox'], text: 'postMessage ARTIFACT_UPDATE; CSP-isolated render' },\n591\t          { nodes: ['sandbox'], text: 'Heartbeat detects infinite loop → kill iframe → error UI' },\n592\t          { nodes: ['pgGraph', 'objectStore'], text: 'Version chain persisted; revert-to-N available' }\n593\t        ],\n594\t        sections: ['04','10']\n595\t      },\n596\t      auth: {\n597\t        title: 'MCP OAuth expires mid-agent-task',\n598\t        steps: [\n599\t          { nodes: ['mcpClient', 'mcpServers'], text: '401 on tool call; orchestrator → paused_auth' },\n600\t          { nodes: ['sse', 'toolPills'], text: 'SSE auth_required event; UI modal Reconnect Slack' },\n601\t          { nodes: ['orchestrator', 'redis'], text: 'Task checkpoint: completed_steps[], pending_tool_call' },\n602\t          { nodes: ['rest', 'mcpClient'], text: 'After OAuth: POST /tasks/:id/resume same idempotency key' }\n603\t        ],\n604\t        sections: ['03','06','10']\n605\t      }\n606\t    };\n607\t\n608\t    const LANES = [\n609\t      { y: 28, h: 130, label: 'UI Surfaces', layer: 'ui' },\n610\t      { y: 178, h: 130, label: 'Client State & Pipelines', layer: 'client' },\n611\t      { y: 330, h: 110, label: 'Transport', layer: 'transport' },\n612\t      { y: 482, h: 130, label: 'API / BFF', layer: 'api' },\n613\t      { y: 634, h: 110, label: 'Providers', layer: 'provider' },\n614\t      { y: 786, h: 110, label: 'Data', layer: 'data' }\n615\t    ];\n616\t\n617\t    let scale = 0.82;\n618\t    let panX = 20;\n619\t    let panY = 10;\n620\t    let activeLayers = new Set(Object.keys(LAYERS));\n621\t    let activeSections = new Set(SECTIONS.map(s => s.id));\n622\t    let selectedNode = null;\n623\t    let activeFlow = null;\n624\t    let flowStepIndex = -1;\n625\t    let searchQuery = '';\n626\t\n627\t    const diagram = document.getElementById('diagram');\n628\t    const connections = document.getElementById('connections');\n629\t    const canvas = document.getElementById('canvas');\n630\t\n631\t    function nodeCenter(id) {\n632\t      const n = NODES.find(x => x.id === id);\n633\t      return { x: n.x + 74, y: n.y + 28 };\n634\t    }\n635\t\n636\t    function renderLanes() {\n637\t      diagram.querySelectorAll('.lane').forEach(el => el.remove());\n638\t      LANES.forEach(lane => {\n639\t        if (!activeLayers.has(lane.layer) && lane.layer !== 'security') return;\n640\t        const el = document.createElement('div');\n641\t        el.className = 'lane';\n642\t        el.style.top = lane.y + 'px';\n643\t        el.style.height = lane.h + 'px';\n644\t        el.innerHTML = `<span class=\"lane-label\">${lane.label}</span>`;\n645\t        diagram.insertBefore(el, connections);\n646\t      });\n647\t    }\n648\t\n649\t    function nodeMatchesFilters(n) {\n650\t      const q = searchQuery.toLowerCase();\n651\t      const matchSearch = !q || n.title.toLowerCase().includes(q) || n.sub.toLowerCase().includes(q) || n.desc.toLowerCase().includes(q);\n652\t      const matchLayer = activeLayers.has(n.layer);\n653\t      const matchSection = n.sections.some(s => activeSections.has(s));\n654\t      return matchSearch && matchLayer && matchSection;\n655\t    }\n656\t\n657\t    function getActiveFlowStep() {\n658\t      if (!activeFlow || flowStepIndex < 0) return null;\n659\t      return FLOWS[activeFlow]?.steps[flowStepIndex] || null;\n660\t    }\n661\t\n662\t    function getFlowHighlightEdges(stepNodes) {\n663\t      const inStep = new Set(stepNodes);\n664\t      return EDGES.filter(([from, to]) => inStep.has(from) && inStep.has(to));\n665\t    }\n666\t\n667\t    function renderNodes() {\n668\t      diagram.querySelectorAll('.node').forEach(el => el.remove());\n669\t      const flowStep = getActiveFlowStep();\n670\t      const flowNodeIds = flowStep ? new Set(flowStep.nodes) : null;\n671\t\n672\t      NODES.forEach(n => {\n673\t        const el = document.createElement('div');\n674\t        el.className = 'node';\n675\t        el.dataset.id = n.id;\n676\t        el.dataset.layer = n.layer;\n677\t        el.style.left = n.x + 'px';\n678\t        el.style.top = n.y + 'px';\n679\t\n680\t        const visible = nodeMatchesFilters(n);\n681\t        if (!visible) {\n682\t          el.classList.add('dimmed');\n683\t        } else if (flowNodeIds && !flowNodeIds.has(n.id)) {\n684\t          el.classList.add('dimmed');\n685\t        }\n686\t\n687\t        if (flowNodeIds && flowNodeIds.has(n.id) && visible) {\n688\t          el.classList.add('highlight');\n689\t        }\n690\t        if (selectedNode === n.id) el.classList.add('selected');\n691\t\n692\t        el.innerHTML = `\n693\t          <div class=\"node-title\">${n.title}</div>\n694\t          <div class=\"node-sub\">${n.sub}</div>\n695\t          <div class=\"node-tags\">${n.sections.map(s => `<span class=\"node-tag\">${s}</span>`).join('')}</div>\n696\t        `;\n697\t        el.addEventListener('click', () => selectNode(n.id));\n698\t        diagram.appendChild(el);\n699\t      });\n700\t    }\n701\t\n702\t    function renderEdges(highlightPairs) {\n703\t      const hl = new Set((highlightPairs || []).map(p => p.join('|')));\n704\t      connections.innerHTML = '';\n705\t      EDGES.forEach(([from, to, label]) => {\n706\t        const a = nodeCenter(from);\n707\t        const b = nodeCenter(to);\n708\t        const line = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'line');\n709\t        line.setAttribute('x1', a.x);\n710\t        line.setAttribute('y1', a.y);\n711\t        line.setAttribute('x2', b.x);\n712\t        line.setAttribute('y2', b.y);\n713\t        if (hl.has(from + '|' + to) || hl.has(to + '|' + from)) line.classList.add('flow-active');\n714\t        const nf = NODES.find(n => n.id === from);\n715\t        const nt = NODES.find(n => n.id === to);\n716\t        const visible = nf && nt &&\n717\t          activeLayers.has(nf.layer) && activeLayers.has(nt.layer) &&\n718\t          nf.sections.some(s => activeSections.has(s)) &&\n719\t          nt.sections.some(s => activeSections.has(s));\n720\t        if (!visible) line.style.opacity = '0.15';\n721\t        connections.appendChild(line);\n722\t      });\n723\t    }\n724\t\n725\t    function applyTransform() {\n726\t      diagram.style.transform = `translate(${panX}px, ${panY}px) scale(${scale})`;\n727\t    }\n728\t\n729\t    function selectNode(id) {\n730\t      selectedNode = id;\n731\t      activeFlow = null;\n732\t      flowStepIndex = -1;\n733\t      document.querySelectorAll('.flow-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));\n734\t      renderNodes();\n735\t      renderEdges();\n736\t      showNodeDetail(id);\n737\t    }\n738\t\n739\t    function showNodeDetail(id) {\n740\t      const n = NODES.find(x => x.id === id);\n741\t      if (!n) return;\n742\t      document.getElementById('detailEmpty').hidden = true;\n743\t      const content = document.getElementById('detailContent');\n744\t      content.hidden = false;\n745\t      const layer = LAYERS[n.layer];\n746\t      content.innerHTML = `\n747\t        <span class=\"layer-badge\" style=\"background:${layer.color}22;color:${layer.color}\">${layer.label}</span>\n748\t        <h2>${n.title}</h2>\n749\t        <p>${n.desc}</p>\n750\t        <h3>Key mechanisms</h3>\n751\t        <ul>${n.bullets.map(b => `<li>${b}</li>`).join('')}</ul>\n752\t        <h3>Interview questions</h3>\n753\t        <ul>${n.questions.map(q => `<li>${q}</li>`).join('')}</ul>\n754\t        <h3>Prep sections</h3>\n755\t        <div class=\"section-links\">${n.sections.map(s => {\n756\t          const sec = SECTIONS.find(x => x.id === s);\n757\t          return sec ? `<a href=\"${sec.file}\">§${s} ${sec.name}</a>` : '';\n758\t        }).join('')}</div>\n759\t      `;\n760\t    }\n761\t\n762\t    function showFlowDetail(flowKey) {\n763\t      const flow = FLOWS[flowKey];\n764\t      document.getElementById('detailEmpty').hidden = true;\n765\t      const content = document.getElementById('detailContent');\n766\t      content.hidden = false;\n767\t      content.innerHTML = `\n768\t        <h2>${flow.title}</h2>\n769\t        <p>Click steps to highlight nodes on the diagram.</p>\n770\t        <h3>Steps</h3>\n771\t        ${flow.steps.map((step, i) => `\n772\t          <div class=\"flow-step${i === flowStepIndex ? ' active' : ''}\" data-step=\"${i}\">\n773\t            <strong>${i + 1}.</strong> ${step.text}\n774\t          </div>\n775\t        `).join('')}\n776\t        <h3>Related sections</h3>\n777\t        <div class=\"section-links\">${flow.sections.map(s => {\n778\t          const sec = SECTIONS.find(x => x.id === s);\n779\t          return sec ? `<a href=\"${sec.file}\">§${s} ${sec.name}</a>` : '';\n780\t        }).join('')}</div>\n781\t      `;\n782\t      content.querySelectorAll('.flow-step').forEach(el => {\n783\t        el.addEventListener('click', () => {\n784\t          const idx = Number(el.dataset.step);\n785\t          highlightFlowStep(flowKey, idx);\n786\t          showFlowDetail(flowKey);\n787\t        });\n788\t      });\n789\t    }\n790\t\n791\t    function highlightFlowStep(flowKey, stepIndex) {\n792\t      const flow = FLOWS[flowKey];\n793\t      const step = flow?.steps[stepIndex];\n794\t      if (!step) return;\n795\t      activeFlow = flowKey;\n796\t      flowStepIndex = stepIndex;\n797\t      renderNodes();\n798\t      renderEdges(getFlowHighlightEdges(step.nodes));\n799\t    }\n800\t\n801\t    function startFlow(flowKey) {\n802\t      activeFlow = flowKey;\n803\t      flowStepIndex = 0;\n804\t      selectedNode = null;\n805\t      document.querySelectorAll('.flow-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.toggle('active', b.dataset.flow === flowKey));\n806\t      renderNodes();\n807\t      highlightFlowStep(flowKey, 0);\n808\t      showFlowDetail(flowKey);\n809\t    }\n810\t\n811\t    function buildFilters() {\n812\t      const lf = document.getElementById('layerFilters');\n813\t      Object.entries(LAYERS).forEach(([key, val]) => {\n814\t        const chip = document.createElement('button');\n815\t        chip.type = 'button';\n816\t        chip.className = `chip layer-${key} active`;\n817\t        chip.textContent = val.label;\n818\t        chip.addEventListener('click', () => {\n819\t          if (activeLayers.has(key)) { activeLayers.delete(key); chip.classList.remove('active'); }\n820\t          else { activeLayers.add(key); chip.classList.add('active'); }\n821\t          refresh();\n822\t        });\n823\t        lf.appendChild(chip);\n824\t      });\n825\t\n826\t      const sf = document.getElementById('sectionFilters');\n827\t      SECTIONS.forEach(sec => {\n828\t        const chip = document.createElement('button');\n829\t        chip.type = 'button';\n830\t        chip.className = 'chip active';\n831\t        chip.textContent = sec.id + ' ' + sec.name;\n832\t        chip.addEventListener('click', () => {\n833\t          if (activeSections.has(sec.id)) { activeSections.delete(sec.id); chip.classList.remove('active'); }\n834\t          else { activeSections.add(sec.id); chip.classList.add('active'); }\n835\t          refresh();\n836\t        });\n837\t        sf.appendChild(chip);\n838\t      });\n839\t\n840\t      const fb = document.getElementById('flowButtons');\n841\t      Object.entries(FLOWS).forEach(([key, flow]) => {\n842\t        const btn = document.createElement('button');\n843\t        btn.type = 'button';\n844\t        btn.className = 'flow-btn';\n845\t        btn.dataset.flow = key;\n846\t        btn.textContent = flow.title;\n847\t        btn.addEventListener('click', () => startFlow(key));\n848\t        fb.appendChild(btn);\n849\t      });\n850\t\n851\t      const legend = document.getElementById('legend');\n852\t      Object.entries(LAYERS).forEach(([key, val]) => {\n853\t        legend.innerHTML += `<div><span style=\"background:${val.color}\"></span>${val.label}</div>`;\n854\t      });\n855\t    }\n856\t\n857\t    function refresh() {\n858\t      renderLanes();\n859\t      renderNodes();\n860\t      if (activeFlow && flowStepIndex >= 0) {\n861\t        const step = FLOWS[activeFlow]?.steps[flowStepIndex];\n862\t        renderEdges(step ? getFlowHighlightEdges(step.nodes) : []);\n863\t      } else {\n864\t        renderEdges();\n865\t      }\n866\t    }\n867\t\n868\t    document.getElementById('search').addEventListener('input', e => {\n869\t      searchQuery = e.target.value;\n870\t      refresh();\n871\t    });\n872\t\n873\t    document.getElementById('zoomIn').addEventListener('click', () => { scale = Math.min(1.4, scale + 0.1); applyTransform(); });\n874\t    document.getElementById('zoomOut').addEventListener('click', () => { scale = Math.max(0.45, scale - 0.1); applyTransform(); });\n875\t    document.getElementById('resetView').addEventListener('click', () => { scale = 0.82; panX = 20; panY = 10; applyTransform(); });\n876\t\n877\t    let dragging = false;\n878\t    let lastX = 0, lastY = 0;\n879\t    canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {\n880\t      if (e.target.closest('.node')) return;\n881\t      dragging = true;\n882\t      lastX = e.clientX;\n883\t      lastY = e.clientY;\n884\t      canvas.classList.add('dragging');\n885\t      canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n886\t    });\n887\t    canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', e => {\n888\t      if (!dragging) return;\n889\t      panX += e.clientX - lastX;\n890\t      panY += e.clientY - lastY;\n891\t      lastX = e.clientX;\n892\t      lastY = e.clientY;\n893\t      applyTransform();\n894\t    });\n895\t    canvas.addEventListener('pointerup', () => { dragging = false; canvas.classList.remove('dragging'); });\n896\t\n897\t    buildFilters();\n898\t    renderLanes();\n899\t    renderNodes();\n900\t    renderEdges();\n901\t    applyTransform();\n902\t  </script>\n903\t</body>\n904\t</html>\n905\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ab96e0e-8f96-4d88-841c-51b1b26eaeef","uuid":"525ae85c-6b24-4fa9-8c06-6fec709e013d","timestamp":"2026-06-20T19:44:03.831Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/claude/claude-frontend-architecture.html","content":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Claude Frontend System — Interactive Architecture</title>\n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Interactive architecture map covering all 10 Claude-style AI chat frontend system design prep sections.\">\n  <style>\n    :root {\n      --bg: #0f1219;\n      --surface: #171c28;\n      --surface2: #1e2536;\n      --text: #e8ecf4;\n      --muted: #8b95a8;\n      --border: #2d3548;\n      --accent: #c97840;\n      --accent-soft: rgba(201, 120, 64, 0.15);\n      --ui: #5b9bd5;\n      --client: #70ad47;\n      --transport: #ffc000;\n      --api: #9966cc;\n      --provider: #ed7d31;\n      --data: #4472c4;\n      --security: #e74c3c;\n      --shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,.35);\n    }\n    @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {\n      :root {\n        --bg: #f4f2ef;\n        --surface: #fff;\n        --surface2: #faf8f5;\n        --text: #1a1d26;\n        --muted: #5c6370;\n        --border: #e2e6ed;\n        --accent: #b85c28;\n        --accent-soft: rgba(184, 92, 40, 0.1);\n        --shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.08);\n      }\n    }\n    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    html, body { height: 100%; margin: 0; }\n    body {\n      font-family: \"Segoe UI\", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\n      background: var(--bg);\n      color: var(--text);\n      overflow: hidden;\n    }\n    .app {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 280px 1fr 340px;\n      grid-template-rows: auto 1fr;\n      height: 100vh;\n    }\n    header {\n      grid-column: 1 / -1;\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      gap: 1rem;\n      padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;\n      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n      background: var(--surface);\n    }\n    header h1 {\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      margin: 0;\n      letter-spacing: -0.02em;\n    }\n    header p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--muted); }\n    .header-links { margin-left: auto; display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; }\n    .header-links a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }\n    .header-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }\n\n    .sidebar {\n      border-right: 1px solid var(--border);\n      background: var(--surface);\n      overflow-y: auto;\n      padding: 1rem;\n    }\n    .sidebar h2 {\n      font-size: 0.6875rem;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.06em;\n      color: var(--muted);\n      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;\n    }\n    .sidebar section { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }\n    .filter-group { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.35rem; }\n    .chip {\n      font-size: 0.75rem;\n      padding: 0.25rem 0.55rem;\n      border-radius: 999px;\n      border: 1px solid var(--border);\n      background: var(--surface2);\n      color: var(--muted);\n      cursor: pointer;\n      user-select: none;\n      transition: all 0.15s;\n    }\n    .chip:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--text); }\n    .chip.active { background: var(--accent-soft); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }\n    .chip.layer-ui.active { border-color: var(--ui); color: var(--ui); background: rgba(91,155,213,.12); }\n    .chip.layer-client.active { border-color: var(--client); color: var(--client); background: rgba(112,173,71,.12); }\n    .chip.layer-transport.active { border-color: var(--transport); color: #b8860b; background: rgba(255,192,0,.12); }\n    .chip.layer-api.active { border-color: var(--api); color: var(--api); background: rgba(153,102,204,.12); }\n    .chip.layer-provider.active { border-color: var(--provider); color: var(--provider); background: rgba(237,125,49,.12); }\n    .chip.layer-data.active { border-color: var(--data); color: var(--data); background: rgba(68,114,196,.12); }\n    .chip.layer-security.active { border-color: var(--security); color: var(--security); background: rgba(231,76,60,.12); }\n\n    select, input[type=\"search\"] {\n      width: 100%;\n      font: inherit;\n      font-size: 0.8125rem;\n      padding: 0.45rem 0.65rem;\n      border: 1px solid var(--border);\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      background: var(--surface2);\n      color: var(--text);\n    }\n    .flow-btn {\n      display: block;\n      width: 100%;\n      text-align: left;\n      font: inherit;\n      font-size: 0.8125rem;\n      padding: 0.5rem 0.65rem;\n      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;\n      border: 1px solid var(--border);\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      background: var(--surface2);\n      color: var(--text);\n      cursor: pointer;\n    }\n    .flow-btn:hover, .flow-btn.active { border-color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft); }\n    .legend { font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }\n    .legend span { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 4px; vertical-align: middle; }\n\n    .canvas-wrap {\n      position: relative;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      background:\n        radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgba(201,120,64,.06), transparent 50%),\n        var(--bg);\n    }\n    .canvas-toolbar {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: 0.75rem;\n      left: 0.75rem;\n      z-index: 5;\n      display: flex;\n      gap: 0.35rem;\n    }\n    .canvas-toolbar button {\n      font: inherit;\n      font-size: 0.75rem;\n      padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem;\n      border: 1px solid var(--border);\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      background: var(--surface);\n      color: var(--text);\n      cursor: pointer;\n    }\n    .canvas {\n      width: 100%;\n      height: 100%;\n      cursor: grab;\n      touch-action: none;\n    }\n    .canvas.dragging { cursor: grabbing; }\n    .diagram-inner {\n      position: absolute;\n      width: 1200px;\n      height: 920px;\n      transform-origin: 0 0;\n    }\n    svg.connections {\n      position: absolute;\n      inset: 0;\n      width: 100%;\n      height: 100%;\n      pointer-events: none;\n    }\n    svg.connections line, svg.connections path {\n      stroke: var(--border);\n      stroke-width: 1.5;\n      fill: none;\n      transition: stroke 0.2s, stroke-width 0.2s;\n    }\n    svg.connections .flow-active {\n      stroke: var(--accent);\n      stroke-width: 2.5;\n      stroke-dasharray: 8 4;\n      animation: flowDash 0.6s linear infinite;\n    }\n    @keyframes flowDash { to { stroke-dashoffset: -12; } }\n\n    .lane {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 12px;\n      right: 12px;\n      border: 1px dashed var(--border);\n      border-radius: 10px;\n      background: rgba(255,255,255,.02);\n    }\n    .lane-label {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 12px;\n      top: 6px;\n      font-size: 0.6875rem;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      color: var(--muted);\n    }\n    .node {\n      position: absolute;\n      width: 148px;\n      padding: 0.55rem 0.65rem;\n      border-radius: 8px;\n      border: 2px solid var(--border);\n      background: var(--surface);\n      font-size: 0.75rem;\n      line-height: 1.35;\n      cursor: pointer;\n      transition: transform 0.15s, box-shadow 0.15s, opacity 0.2s, border-color 0.15s;\n      box-shadow: var(--shadow);\n    }\n    .node:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); z-index: 10; }\n    .node.selected { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--accent-soft); z-index: 11; }\n    .node.dimmed { opacity: 0.2; pointer-events: none; }\n    .node.highlight { border-color: var(--accent); animation: pulse 1s ease infinite; }\n    @keyframes pulse { 50% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--accent-soft); } }\n    .node-title { font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.15rem; }\n    .node-sub { font-size: 0.6875rem; color: var(--muted); }\n    .node-tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px; margin-top: 0.35rem; }\n    .node-tag {\n      font-size: 0.5625rem;\n      padding: 1px 4px;\n      border-radius: 3px;\n      background: var(--surface2);\n      color: var(--muted);\n    }\n    .node[data-layer=\"ui\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--ui); }\n    .node[data-layer=\"client\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--client); }\n    .node[data-layer=\"transport\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--transport); }\n    .node[data-layer=\"api\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--api); }\n    .node[data-layer=\"provider\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--provider); }\n    .node[data-layer=\"data\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--data); }\n    .node[data-layer=\"security\"] { border-left: 4px solid var(--security); }\n\n    .detail {\n      border-left: 1px solid var(--border);\n      background: var(--surface);\n      overflow-y: auto;\n      padding: 1.25rem;\n    }\n    .detail-empty { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center; }\n    .detail h2 { font-size: 1.125rem; margin: 0 0 0.35rem; }\n    .detail .layer-badge {\n      display: inline-block;\n      font-size: 0.6875rem;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;\n      border-radius: 4px;\n      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n    }\n    .detail p { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }\n    .detail h3 { font-size: 0.8125rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--accent); margin: 1rem 0 0.4rem; }\n    .detail ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.55; }\n    .detail li { margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }\n    .section-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; }\n    .section-links a {\n      font-size: 0.75rem;\n      padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;\n      border-radius: 4px;\n      background: var(--accent-soft);\n      color: var(--accent);\n      text-decoration: none;\n    }\n    .section-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }\n    .flow-step {\n      font-size: 0.8125rem;\n      padding: 0.5rem 0.65rem;\n      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;\n      border-left: 3px solid var(--border);\n      background: var(--surface2);\n      border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;\n    }\n    .flow-step.active { border-left-color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft); }\n\n    @media (max-width: 1100px) {\n      .app { grid-template-columns: 1fr; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr auto; overflow-y: auto; height: auto; min-height: 100vh; }\n      body { overflow: auto; }\n      .sidebar { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); max-height: none; }\n      .canvas-wrap { min-height: 520px; }\n      .detail { border-left: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); max-height: none; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class=\"app\">\n    <header>\n      <div>\n        <h1>Claude Frontend System Architecture</h1>\n        <p>Interactive map · all 10 prep sections</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"header-links\">\n        <a href=\"answers-html/index.html\">Answer pages</a>\n        <a href=\"Claude-design-doc.md\">Question bank</a>\n      </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <aside class=\"sidebar\">\n      <section>\n        <h2>Search</h2>\n        <input type=\"search\" id=\"search\" placeholder=\"Filter nodes…\" autocomplete=\"off\">\n      </section>\n      <section>\n        <h2>Layer filter</h2>\n        <div class=\"filter-group\" id=\"layerFilters\"></div>\n      </section>\n      <section>\n        <h2>Section filter</h2>\n        <div class=\"filter-group\" id=\"sectionFilters\"></div>\n      </section>\n      <section>\n        <h2>Walk a flow</h2>\n        <div id=\"flowButtons\"></div>\n      </section>\n      <section>\n        <h2>Legend</h2>\n        <div class=\"legend\" id=\"legend\"></div>\n      </section>\n    </aside>\n\n    <main class=\"canvas-wrap\">\n      <div class=\"canvas-toolbar\">\n        <button type=\"button\" id=\"zoomIn\">+</button>\n        <button type=\"button\" id=\"zoomOut\">−</button>\n        <button type=\"button\" id=\"resetView\">Reset view</button>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"canvas\" id=\"canvas\">\n        <div class=\"diagram-inner\" id=\"diagram\">\n          <svg class=\"connections\" id=\"connections\"></svg>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <aside class=\"detail\" id=\"detailPanel\">\n      <div class=\"detail-empty\" id=\"detailEmpty\">\n        Click a node or run a flow walkthrough to see details, interview angles, and links to answer sections.\n      </div>\n      <div id=\"detailContent\" hidden></div>\n    </aside>\n  </div>\n\n  <script>\n    const LAYERS = {\n      ui: { label: 'UI Surfaces', color: 'var(--ui)' },\n      client: { label: 'Client State', color: 'var(--client)' },\n      transport: { label: 'Transport', color: 'var(--transport)' },\n      api: { label: 'API / BFF', color: 'var(--api)' },\n      provider: { label: 'Providers', color: 'var(--provider)' },\n      data: { label: 'Data', color: 'var(--data)' },\n      security: { label: 'Security', color: 'var(--security)' }\n    };\n\n    const SECTIONS = [\n      { id: '01', name: 'Streaming', file: 'answers-html/01-streaming-real-time-rendering.html' },\n      { id: '02', name: 'State', file: 'answers-html/02-conversation-state-management.html' },\n      { id: '03', name: 'MCP Tools', file: 'answers-html/03-mcp-tool-use-ui.html' },\n      { id: '04', name: 'Artifacts', file: 'answers-html/04-artifacts-sandboxed-rendering.html' },\n      { id: '05', name: 'Performance', file: 'answers-html/05-performance-scalability.html' },\n      { id: '06', name: 'Auth', file: 'answers-html/06-auth-security-multitenancy.html' },\n      { id: '07', name: 'Resilience', file: 'answers-html/07-offline-resilience-error-handling.html' },\n      { id: '08', name: 'Input', file: 'answers-html/08-input-multimodal-ux.html' },\n      { id: '09', name: 'Providers', file: 'answers-html/09-api-design-provider-abstraction.html' },\n      { id: '10', name: 'Killer Qs', file: 'answers-html/10-killer-questions.html' }\n    ];\n\n    const NODES = [\n      { id: 'composer', layer: 'ui', x: 40, y: 48, title: 'Composer', sub: 'Input · attach · send/stop', sections: ['02','08','01'],\n        desc: 'Captures drafts, multimodal attachments, slash commands, token estimate, and stop-generation. Never part of the committed message graph until send.',\n        bullets: ['Auto-grow textarea with max height cap', 'AttachmentController: drag/drop/paste', 'AbortController wired to active SSE stream', 'Draft in localStorage/IDB, separate from graph'],\n        questions: ['Draft persistence', 'Mixed multimodal send', 'Stop generation chain'] },\n      { id: 'sidebar', layer: 'ui', x: 220, y: 48, title: 'Sidebar', sub: '10k convos · search', sections: ['05','10','02'],\n        desc: 'Virtualized conversation list with metadata-only rows, cursor pagination, FTS search, optimistic rename/delete.',\n        bullets: ['Prefetch on hover/focus', 'IndexedDB cache ~1000 rows', 'No message bodies in list rows'],\n        questions: ['Sidebar at 10k scale', 'Preload next conversation'] },\n      { id: 'msgList', layer: 'ui', x: 400, y: 48, title: 'Message List', sub: 'Virtualized thread', sections: ['01','05','02'],\n        desc: 'Windowed view of active branch path. Pinned streaming row, scroll anchoring, dynamic height cache.',\n        bullets: ['Only visible rows in DOM', 'isPinnedToBottom + \"New messages ↓\"', 'Stable keys per markdown block'],\n        questions: ['Virtualize 500 messages', 'Scroll anchoring', 'Avoid full-list re-render'] },\n      { id: 'streamBubble', layer: 'ui', x: 580, y: 48, title: 'Streaming Bubble', sub: 'Typing → tokens → done', sections: ['01'],\n        desc: 'Single assistant slot: pending indicator crossfades into incremental markdown render.',\n        bullets: ['rAF batching decouples network from paint', 'Incomplete fence/table state machines', 'Backpressure: pause read(), shed highlight'],\n        questions: ['Layout thrash', 'Token throttle', 'Open code fence', 'Backpressure'] },\n      { id: 'toolPills', layer: 'ui', x: 760, y: 48, title: 'Tool Pills', sub: 'HITL · chains · audit', sections: ['03','06','10'],\n        desc: 'Per tool_use_id UI: loading → success/error, confirm card for destructive actions, trust/egress disclosure.',\n        bullets: ['UI lock + idempotency key on confirm', 'Multi-step stepper in one turn', 'Activity drawer for audit trail'],\n        questions: ['Double confirm in 200ms', 'tool_result as user role', 'MCP OAuth expiry'] },\n      { id: 'artifactPanel', layer: 'ui', x: 940, y: 48, title: 'Artifact Panel', sub: 'Editor + preview', sections: ['04','10'],\n        desc: 'Code editor + sandboxed live preview with version timeline, diff, revert.',\n        bullets: ['Heartbeat detects infinite render loops', 'postMessage bridge host ↔ iframe', 'Debounced compile in worker'],\n        questions: ['iframe sandbox + CSP', 'Infinite loop detection', 'Version/revert'] },\n\n      { id: 'convStore', layer: 'client', x: 120, y: 200, title: 'Conversation Store', sub: 'Graph view + active leaf', sections: ['02','10'],\n        desc: 'Client mirror of server message tree. Derives linear visible path via active_leaf_id. Optimistic nodes with clientRequestId.',\n        bullets: ['Edit = sibling fork, not overwrite', 'Branch switcher swaps active leaf', 'BroadcastChannel for multi-tab'],\n        questions: ['Edit message N', 'Branching model', 'Multi-tab sync'] },\n      { id: 'streamPipeline', layer: 'client', x: 320, y: 200, title: 'Streaming Pipeline', sub: 'Buffer · parse · patch', sections: ['01','05'],\n        desc: 'Token ring buffer → rAF flush → incremental markdown blocks → stable DOM patch.',\n        bullets: ['Refs hold hot string; state commits per frame', 'startTransition for responsiveness', 'Canonical string never dropped on shed work'],\n        questions: ['Buffer interval', 'Debounced markdown parse', 'Render lag metrics'] },\n      { id: 'branchAsm', layer: 'client', x: 520, y: 200, title: 'Branch Assembler', sub: 'pathToLeaf · token budget', sections: ['02','09','10'],\n        desc: 'Walk active leaf to root, reverse to chronological order, apply context window truncate/summarize policy.',\n        bullets: ['Preview on client; server authoritative', 'IR blocks compiled at adapter boundary', 'Summary nodes on long threads'],\n        questions: ['Context window strategy', 'Reassemble after edit', 'Provider normalization'] },\n      { id: 'outbox', layer: 'client', x: 720, y: 200, title: 'Outbox Queue', sub: 'Offline · IDB', sections: ['07','02'],\n        desc: 'IndexedDB queue for offline sends and upload resume. FIFO drain on reconnect with Idempotency-Key.',\n        bullets: ['Optimistic user bubble while queued', 'Leader election across tabs', 'Conflict on conversation_revision mismatch'],\n        questions: ['Offline message queue', 'Stream drop recovery'] },\n      { id: 'clientCache', layer: 'client', x: 920, y: 200, title: 'Client Cache', sub: 'Memory · IDB · RQ', sections: ['05','02'],\n        desc: 'Three-tier: in-memory hot set, IndexedDB pages, React Query server sync. Org-scoped namespaces.',\n        bullets: ['LRU ~20 threads in memory', 'Paginated history prepend on scroll-up', 'Height cache for virtualizer'],\n        questions: ['Caching strategy', 'Lazy-load history'] },\n\n      { id: 'rest', layer: 'transport', x: 200, y: 352, title: 'REST', sub: 'CRUD · control · upload', sections: ['01','07','08','03'],\n        desc: 'Send message, cancel, tool execute, paginated history, presigned uploads, search, share links.',\n        bullets: ['Idempotency-Key on destructive ops', 'PATCH events + revision vector', 'parseApiError taxonomy'],\n        questions: ['Cancel/retry control plane', 'Error taxonomy', 'Chunked uploads'] },\n      { id: 'sse', layer: 'transport', x: 480, y: 352, title: 'SSE Stream', sub: 'Token · tool · status', sections: ['01','07','09'],\n        desc: 'Default LLM output transport. fetch + ReadableStream or EventSource with Last-Event-ID reconnect.',\n        bullets: ['AbortController closes HTTP → stops billing', 'Resume via generation_id + cursor', 'Exponential backoff on drop'],\n        questions: ['SSE vs WebSocket', 'Stream drop at token 400', 'Resume stream'] },\n      { id: 'ws', layer: 'transport', x: 760, y: 352, title: 'WebSocket', sub: 'Optional sync', sections: ['01','02'],\n        desc: 'Bidirectional session sync, presence, async job updates. Hybrid: SSE tokens + WS patches.',\n        bullets: ['Manual heartbeat + resume protocol', 'Use when client→server churn is high', 'Not default for pure completion streams'],\n        questions: ['When to pick WS', 'Multi-tab fan-out'] },\n\n      { id: 'gateway', layer: 'api', x: 80, y: 504, title: 'API Gateway', sub: 'Auth · rate limit', sections: ['06','07'],\n        desc: 'JWT validation, org context, rate limiting, request shedding, stream lease issuance.',\n        bullets: ['ctx from claims never body user_id', 'session_version invalidates access tokens', 'Stream lease for in-flight generation'],\n        questions: ['JWT + RLS scoping', 'Session invalidate mid-stream', 'Rate limit UX'] },\n      { id: 'convSvc', layer: 'api', x: 280, y: 504, title: 'Conversation Svc', sub: 'Graph CRUD · share', sections: ['02','06','10'],\n        desc: 'Message nodes tree, branching edits, public share tokens, conversation search metadata.',\n        bullets: ['message_nodes: parent_id, status, branch_label', 'active_leaf_id on conversation row', '409 on concurrent generation'],\n        questions: ['Edit creates sibling node', 'Public share permissions', 'Org isolation'] },\n      { id: 'streamGw', layer: 'api', x: 480, y: 504, title: 'Stream Gateway', sub: 'Checkpoints · replay', sections: ['01','07','10'],\n        desc: 'Inference proxy: streams normalized events, writes partial checkpoints, supports resume cursor.',\n        bullets: ['Debounced DB checkpoint every N tokens', 'Redis event buffer for Last-Event-ID', 'generation_id correlates client/server'],\n        questions: ['Partial persist mid-stream', 'Continue from prefix fallback'] },\n      { id: 'orchestrator', layer: 'api', x: 680, y: 504, title: 'Agent Orchestrator', sub: 'Tool loop · tasks', sections: ['03','09','10'],\n        desc: 'Runs LLM ↔ tool cycles, agent task state machine, pause/resume on auth_required.',\n        bullets: ['pending_tool_executions table', 'paused_auth + SSE auth_required event', 'Resume with same idempotency key'],\n        questions: ['Multi-step tool chains', 'MCP OAuth mid-task', '529 fallback routing'] },\n      { id: 'mcpClient', layer: 'api', x: 880, y: 504, title: 'MCP Client', sub: 'Policy · egress · audit', sections: ['03','06'],\n        desc: 'Sandboxed tool execution with allowlisted egress, data minimization, immutable audit log.',\n        bullets: ['Never pass full history to hostile MCP', 'Policy engine before network', 'Hashes in compliance log'],\n        questions: ['Trust boundary UI', 'Malicious MCP exfiltration', 'Audit logging'] },\n\n      { id: 'irAdapter', layer: 'provider', x: 320, y: 656, title: 'IR + Adapters', sub: 'Anthropic · OpenAI · Gemini', sections: ['09','03'],\n        desc: 'Internal representation compiled at boundary: system field vs message, tool_use vs tool role, thinking blocks.',\n        bullets: ['CapabilityResolver not if(provider) in UI', 'NormalizedStreamEvent reducer', 'Model alias → pinned model_id per message'],\n        questions: ['Normalize history', 'Streaming adapter', 'Extended thinking flag'] },\n      { id: 'llm', layer: 'provider', x: 560, y: 656, title: 'LLM APIs', sub: 'Primary + fallback', sections: ['09','01','07'],\n        desc: 'Provider SDK streams with 529 backoff, capability-matched fallback, cost estimation pre-send.',\n        bullets: ['No silent stitch of two models in one bubble', 'Mid-stream: surface interrupted', 'Token counter per provider shape'],\n        questions: ['Model fallback', 'Cost estimate', 'Model deprecation'] },\n      { id: 'mcpServers', layer: 'provider', x: 800, y: 656, title: 'MCP Servers', sub: 'Slack · Calendar · …', sections: ['03','06'],\n        desc: 'Third-party integrations via OAuth token vault (server-only refresh with serialized lock).',\n        bullets: ['OAuth refresh mid-conversation', 'Scoped args only', 'Timeout → pill failed + user retry/skip'],\n        questions: ['OAuth token refresh', 'Tool timeout 30s'] },\n\n      { id: 'pgGraph', layer: 'data', x: 160, y: 808, title: 'Postgres Graph', sub: 'Nodes · branches · ACL', sections: ['02','06','10'],\n        desc: 'Source of truth: message tree, memberships, shares, agent_tasks, artifact version chain.',\n        bullets: ['RLS: org_id + owner_user_id', 'status: streaming → interrupted → final', 'Unique generation_id constraint'],\n        questions: ['Tree vs linear array', 'Partial message in DB'] },\n      { id: 'redis', layer: 'data', x: 400, y: 808, title: 'Redis', sub: 'Locks · replay · dedup', sections: ['07','03','02'],\n        desc: 'Active branch pointer, SSE replay buffer, idempotency TTL, session denylist, stream checkpoints.',\n        bullets: ['(user_id, idempotency_key) dedup', 'Short TTL event buffer', 'Refresh lock for OAuth'],\n        questions: ['Double booking dedup', 'SSE reconnect replay'] },\n      { id: 'objectStore', layer: 'data', x: 640, y: 808, title: 'Object Storage', sub: 'Uploads · artifacts', sections: ['08','04','06'],\n        desc: 'Quarantine bucket, presigned multipart uploads, attachment CDN URLs, WORM audit exports.',\n        bullets: ['Magic-byte sniff at ingest', 'Stable fileId refs not base64 in state', 'Per-org S3 prefix'],\n        questions: ['Large file uploads', 'PDF extract pipeline', 'Upload quarantine'] },\n      { id: 'indexedDb', layer: 'data', x: 880, y: 808, title: 'IndexedDB', sub: 'Client pages · outbox', sections: ['05','07','02'],\n        desc: 'Browser persistence: message pages, sidebar cache, offline outbox, upload session resume.',\n        bullets: ['Key: userId:orgId:conversationId', 'BroadcastChannel invalidation', 'Partial stream on disconnect'],\n        questions: ['Client cache tiers', 'Offline replay'] },\n\n      { id: 'authBoundary', layer: 'security', x: 40, y: 656, title: 'Auth Boundary', sub: 'JWT · org · RLS', sections: ['06'],\n        desc: 'Every request derives tenant from token/key record. Defense in depth: API filter + Postgres RLS.',\n        bullets: ['Multi-org context switch aborts streams', 'API key org bound, scopes enforced', 'Share token capability URL'],\n        questions: ['Org switching', 'API key scope', 'Public link permissions'] },\n      { id: 'sandbox', layer: 'security', x: 1040, y: 200, title: 'Sandbox iframe', sub: 'CSP · postMessage', sections: ['04','10'],\n        desc: 'Origin-isolated artifact preview. allow-scripts only, no allow-same-origin. Heartbeat + render budget.',\n        bullets: ['CDN imports via vendor proxy or block', 'Kill iframe on RENDER_LOOP', 'Replace iframe as recovery unit'],\n        questions: ['Sandbox attacks prevented', 'Infinite loop in React artifact'] },\n      { id: 'contentFw', layer: 'security', x: 1040, y: 504, title: 'Content Firewall', sub: 'Upload · inject', sections: ['06','08'],\n        desc: 'Extracted upload text wrapped as untrusted document; never in system role. Instruction pattern stripping.',\n        bullets: ['Client extract vs server OCR for PDF', 'Prompt injection via hidden PDF text', 'Page/token caps'],\n        questions: ['Prompt injection uploads', 'PDF handling'] }\n    ];\n\n    const EDGES = [\n      ['composer', 'rest', 'POST send'],\n      ['composer', 'sse', 'Abort stop'],\n      ['composer', 'convStore', 'optimistic user node'],\n      ['sidebar', 'clientCache', 'prefetch metadata'],\n      ['msgList', 'streamPipeline', 'render commits'],\n      ['streamBubble', 'streamPipeline', 'token buffer'],\n      ['toolPills', 'rest', 'confirm execute'],\n      ['artifactPanel', 'sandbox', 'postMessage'],\n      ['convStore', 'branchAsm', 'active leaf path'],\n      ['convStore', 'outbox', 'offline queue'],\n      ['streamPipeline', 'convStore', 'finalize assistant'],\n      ['streamPipeline', 'artifactPanel', 'code fence deltas'],\n      ['branchAsm', 'rest', 'compiled context preview'],\n      ['clientCache', 'msgList', 'history pages'],\n      ['rest', 'gateway', 'HTTP'],\n      ['sse', 'streamGw', 'token stream'],\n      ['ws', 'convSvc', 'patch events'],\n      ['gateway', 'convSvc', 'authorized'],\n      ['convSvc', 'pgGraph', 'persist graph'],\n      ['streamGw', 'orchestrator', 'generation job'],\n      ['streamGw', 'sse', 'normalized events'],\n      ['orchestrator', 'irAdapter', 'IR compile'],\n      ['orchestrator', 'mcpClient', 'tool_use'],\n      ['mcpClient', 'mcpServers', 'scoped call'],\n      ['mcpClient', 'convStore', 'tool_result blocks'],\n      ['irAdapter', 'llm', 'provider SDK'],\n      ['streamGw', 'redis', 'checkpoints'],\n      ['mcpClient', 'redis', 'idempotency'],\n      ['rest', 'objectStore', 'presign upload'],\n      ['clientCache', 'indexedDb', 'hydrate'],\n      ['authBoundary', 'gateway', 'ctx claims'],\n      ['contentFw', 'orchestrator', 'sanitized blocks'],\n      ['objectStore', 'contentFw', 'extract pipeline']\n    ];\n\n    const FLOWS = {\n      send: {\n        title: 'Send message → stream response',\n        steps: [\n          { nodes: ['composer'], text: 'User sends; optimistic user node appended to store' },\n          { nodes: ['rest', 'gateway', 'convSvc'], text: 'POST validated; graph node persisted; generation leased' },\n          { nodes: ['streamGw', 'orchestrator', 'irAdapter', 'llm'], text: 'IR compiled; provider streams tokens' },\n          { nodes: ['sse', 'streamPipeline', 'streamBubble'], text: 'SSE chunks batched via rAF into markdown blocks' },\n          { nodes: ['convStore', 'pgGraph'], text: 'Stream end finalizes assistant node in graph + DB' }\n        ],\n        sections: ['01','02','09']\n      },\n      tool: {\n        title: 'Tool call → HITL confirm → resume',\n        steps: [\n          { nodes: ['llm', 'orchestrator'], text: 'Model emits tool_use block in stream' },\n          { nodes: ['toolPills', 'streamBubble'], text: 'Pill shows loading; sensitive tools show confirm + egress disclosure' },\n          { nodes: ['rest', 'mcpClient', 'redis'], text: 'Confirm POST with idempotency key; dedup if double-clicked' },\n          { nodes: ['mcpServers'], text: 'MCP executes with minimized args; audit log written' },\n          { nodes: ['convStore', 'orchestrator', 'llm'], text: 'tool_result as user blocks; model turn resumes' }\n        ],\n        sections: ['03','10']\n      },\n      drop: {\n        title: 'Stream drops at token 400/1000',\n        steps: [\n          { nodes: ['sse', 'streamPipeline'], text: 'TCP close; partial text retained in bubble (never blank)' },\n          { nodes: ['streamGw', 'redis', 'pgGraph'], text: 'Checkpoint row status=interrupted; cursor persisted' },\n          { nodes: ['streamBubble', 'rest'], text: 'UI: Continue (resume cursor) | Retry (idempotent regen)' },\n          { nodes: ['outbox', 'indexedDb'], text: 'Client mirrors partial in IDB for refresh survival' }\n        ],\n        sections: ['07','10','01']\n      },\n      edit: {\n        title: 'Edit message N → branch regen',\n        steps: [\n          { nodes: ['composer', 'convStore'], text: 'Edit creates sibling node under same parent (fork, not overwrite)' },\n          { nodes: ['branchAsm'], text: 'New active_leaf; path reassembled with token budget' },\n          { nodes: ['convSvc', 'pgGraph'], text: 'Server persists branch; returns branch_generation/version' },\n          { nodes: ['msgList'], text: 'UI swaps visible path; optional branch switcher keeps both subtrees' }\n        ],\n        sections: ['02','10']\n      },\n      artifact: {\n        title: 'Artifact stream → sandbox preview',\n        steps: [\n          { nodes: ['streamPipeline', 'artifactPanel'], text: 'Code fence deltas debounced in worker' },\n          { nodes: ['sandbox'], text: 'postMessage ARTIFACT_UPDATE; CSP-isolated render' },\n          { nodes: ['sandbox'], text: 'Heartbeat detects infinite loop → kill iframe → error UI' },\n          { nodes: ['pgGraph', 'objectStore'], text: 'Version chain persisted; revert-to-N available' }\n        ],\n        sections: ['04','10']\n      },\n      auth: {\n        title: 'MCP OAuth expires mid-agent-task',\n        steps: [\n          { nodes: ['mcpClient', 'mcpServers'], text: '401 on tool call; orchestrator → paused_auth' },\n          { nodes: ['sse', 'toolPills'], text: 'SSE auth_required event; UI modal Reconnect Slack' },\n          { nodes: ['orchestrator', 'redis'], text: 'Task checkpoint: completed_steps[], pending_tool_call' },\n          { nodes: ['rest', 'mcpClient'], text: 'After OAuth: POST /tasks/:id/resume same idempotency key' }\n        ],\n        sections: ['03','06','10']\n      }\n    };\n\n    const LANES = [\n      { y: 28, h: 130, label: 'UI Surfaces', layer: 'ui' },\n      { y: 178, h: 130, label: 'Client State & Pipelines', layer: 'client' },\n      { y: 330, h: 110, label: 'Transport', layer: 'transport' },\n      { y: 482, h: 130, label: 'API / BFF', layer: 'api' },\n      { y: 634, h: 110, label: 'Providers', layer: 'provider' },\n      { y: 786, h: 110, label: 'Data', layer: 'data' }\n    ];\n\n    let scale = 0.82;\n    let panX = 20;\n    let panY = 10;\n    let activeLayers = new Set(Object.keys(LAYERS));\n    let activeSections = new Set(SECTIONS.map(s => s.id));\n    let selectedNode = null;\n    let activeFlow = null;\n    let flowStepIndex = -1;\n    let searchQuery = '';\n\n    const diagram = document.getElementById('diagram');\n    const connections = document.getElementById('connections');\n    const canvas = document.getElementById('canvas');\n\n    function nodeCenter(id) {\n      const n = NODES.find(x => x.id === id);\n      return { x: n.x + 74, y: n.y + 28 };\n    }\n\n    function renderLanes() {\n      diagram.querySelectorAll('.lane').forEach(el => el.remove());\n      LANES.forEach(lane => {\n        if (!activeLayers.has(lane.layer) && lane.layer !== 'security') return;\n        const el = document.createElement('div');\n        el.className = 'lane';\n        el.style.top = lane.y + 'px';\n        el.style.height = lane.h + 'px';\n        el.innerHTML = `<span class=\"lane-label\">${lane.label}</span>`;\n        diagram.insertBefore(el, connections);\n      });\n    }\n\n    function nodeMatchesFilters(n) {\n      const q = searchQuery.toLowerCase();\n      const matchSearch = !q || n.title.toLowerCase().includes(q) || n.sub.toLowerCase().includes(q) || n.desc.toLowerCase().includes(q);\n      const matchLayer = activeLayers.has(n.layer);\n      const matchSection = n.sections.some(s => activeSections.has(s));\n      return matchSearch && matchLayer && matchSection;\n    }\n\n    function getActiveFlowStep() {\n      if (!activeFlow || flowStepIndex < 0) return null;\n      return FLOWS[activeFlow]?.steps[flowStepIndex] || null;\n    }\n\n    function getFlowHighlightEdges(stepNodes) {\n      const inStep = new Set(stepNodes);\n      return EDGES.filter(([from, to]) => inStep.has(from) && inStep.has(to));\n    }\n\n    function renderNodes() {\n      diagram.querySelectorAll('.node').forEach(el => el.remove());\n      const flowStep = getActiveFlowStep();\n      const flowNodeIds = flowStep ? new Set(flowStep.nodes) : null;\n\n      NODES.forEach(n => {\n        const el = document.createElement('div');\n        el.className = 'node';\n        el.dataset.id = n.id;\n        el.dataset.layer = n.layer;\n        el.style.left = n.x + 'px';\n        el.style.top = n.y + 'px';\n\n        const visible = nodeMatchesFilters(n);\n        if (!visible) {\n          el.classList.add('dimmed');\n        } else if (flowNodeIds && !flowNodeIds.has(n.id)) {\n          el.classList.add('dimmed');\n        }\n\n        if (flowNodeIds && flowNodeIds.has(n.id) && visible) {\n          el.classList.add('highlight');\n        }\n        if (selectedNode === n.id) el.classList.add('selected');\n\n        el.innerHTML = `\n          <div class=\"node-title\">${n.title}</div>\n          <div class=\"node-sub\">${n.sub}</div>\n          <div class=\"node-tags\">${n.sections.map(s => `<span class=\"node-tag\">${s}</span>`).join('')}</div>\n        `;\n        el.addEventListener('click', () => selectNode(n.id));\n        diagram.appendChild(el);\n      });\n    }\n\n    function renderEdges(highlightPairs) {\n      const hl = new Set((highlightPairs || []).map(p => p.join('|')));\n      connections.innerHTML = '';\n      EDGES.forEach(([from, to, label]) => {\n        const a = nodeCenter(from);\n        const b = nodeCenter(to);\n        const line = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'line');\n        line.setAttribute('x1', a.x);\n        line.setAttribute('y1', a.y);\n        line.setAttribute('x2', b.x);\n        line.setAttribute('y2', b.y);\n        if (hl.has(from + '|' + to) || hl.has(to + '|' + from)) line.classList.add('flow-active');\n        const nf = NODES.find(n => n.id === from);\n        const nt = NODES.find(n => n.id === to);\n        const visible = nf && nt &&\n          activeLayers.has(nf.layer) && activeLayers.has(nt.layer) &&\n          nf.sections.some(s => activeSections.has(s)) &&\n          nt.sections.some(s => activeSections.has(s));\n        if (!visible) line.style.opacity = '0.15';\n        connections.appendChild(line);\n      });\n    }\n\n    function applyTransform() {\n      diagram.style.transform = `translate(${panX}px, ${panY}px) scale(${scale})`;\n    }\n\n    function selectNode(id) {\n      selectedNode = id;\n      activeFlow = null;\n      flowStepIndex = -1;\n      document.querySelectorAll('.flow-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));\n      renderNodes();\n      renderEdges();\n      showNodeDetail(id);\n    }\n\n    function showNodeDetail(id) {\n      const n = NODES.find(x => x.id === id);\n      if (!n) return;\n      document.getElementById('detailEmpty').hidden = true;\n      const content = document.getElementById('detailContent');\n      content.hidden = false;\n      const layer = LAYERS[n.layer];\n      content.innerHTML = `\n        <span class=\"layer-badge\" style=\"background:${layer.color}22;color:${layer.color}\">${layer.label}</span>\n        <h2>${n.title}</h2>\n        <p>${n.desc}</p>\n        <h3>Key mechanisms</h3>\n        <ul>${n.bullets.map(b => `<li>${b}</li>`).join('')}</ul>\n        <h3>Interview questions</h3>\n        <ul>${n.questions.map(q => `<li>${q}</li>`).join('')}</ul>\n        <h3>Prep sections</h3>\n        <div class=\"section-links\">${n.sections.map(s => {\n          const sec = SECTIONS.find(x => x.id === s);\n          return sec ? `<a href=\"${sec.file}\">§${s} ${sec.name}</a>` : '';\n        }).join('')}</div>\n      `;\n    }\n\n    function showFlowDetail(flowKey) {\n      const flow = FLOWS[flowKey];\n      document.getElementById('detailEmpty').hidden = true;\n      const content = document.getElementById('detailContent');\n      content.hidden = false;\n      content.innerHTML = `\n        <h2>${flow.title}</h2>\n        <p>Click steps to highlight nodes on the diagram.</p>\n        <h3>Steps</h3>\n        ${flow.steps.map((step, i) => `\n          <div class=\"flow-step${i === flowStepIndex ? ' active' : ''}\" data-step=\"${i}\">\n            <strong>${i + 1}.</strong> ${step.text}\n          </div>\n        `).join('')}\n        <h3>Related sections</h3>\n        <div class=\"section-links\">${flow.sections.map(s => {\n          const sec = SECTIONS.find(x => x.id === s);\n          return sec ? `<a href=\"${sec.file}\">§${s} ${sec.name}</a>` : '';\n        }).join('')}</div>\n      `;\n      content.querySelectorAll('.flow-step').forEach(el => {\n        el.addEventListener('click', () => {\n          const idx = Number(el.dataset.step);\n          highlightFlowStep(flowKey, idx);\n          showFlowDetail(flowKey);\n        });\n      });\n    }\n\n    function highlightFlowStep(flowKey, stepIndex) {\n      const flow = FLOWS[flowKey];\n      const step = flow?.steps[stepIndex];\n      if (!step) return;\n      activeFlow = flowKey;\n      flowStepIndex = stepIndex;\n      renderNodes();\n      renderEdges(getFlowHighlightEdges(step.nodes));\n    }\n\n    function startFlow(flowKey) {\n      activeFlow = flowKey;\n      flowStepIndex = 0;\n      selectedNode = null;\n      document.querySelectorAll('.flow-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.toggle('active', b.dataset.flow === flowKey));\n      renderNodes();\n      highlightFlowStep(flowKey, 0);\n      showFlowDetail(flowKey);\n    }\n\n    function buildFilters() {\n      const lf = document.getElementById('layerFilters');\n      Object.entries(LAYERS).forEach(([key, val]) => {\n        const chip = document.createElement('button');\n        chip.type = 'button';\n        chip.className = `chip layer-${key} active`;\n        chip.textContent = val.label;\n        chip.addEventListener('click', () => {\n          if (activeLayers.has(key)) { activeLayers.delete(key); chip.classList.remove('active'); }\n          else { activeLayers.add(key); chip.classList.add('active'); }\n          refresh();\n        });\n        lf.appendChild(chip);\n      });\n\n      const sf = document.getElementById('sectionFilters');\n      SECTIONS.forEach(sec => {\n        const chip = document.createElement('button');\n        chip.type = 'button';\n        chip.className = 'chip active';\n        chip.textContent = sec.id + ' ' + sec.name;\n        chip.addEventListener('click', () => {\n          if (activeSections.has(sec.id)) { activeSections.delete(sec.id); chip.classList.remove('active'); }\n          else { activeSections.add(sec.id); chip.classList.add('active'); }\n          refresh();\n        });\n        sf.appendChild(chip);\n      });\n\n      const fb = document.getElementById('flowButtons');\n      Object.entries(FLOWS).forEach(([key, flow]) => {\n        const btn = document.createElement('button');\n        btn.type = 'button';\n        btn.className = 'flow-btn';\n        btn.dataset.flow = key;\n        btn.textContent = flow.title;\n        btn.addEventListener('click', () => startFlow(key));\n        fb.appendChild(btn);\n      });\n\n      const legend = document.getElementById('legend');\n      Object.entries(LAYERS).forEach(([key, val]) => {\n        legend.innerHTML += `<div><span style=\"background:${val.color}\"></span>${val.label}</div>`;\n      });\n    }\n\n    function refresh() {\n      renderLanes();\n      renderNodes();\n      if (activeFlow && flowStepIndex >= 0) {\n        const step = FLOWS[activeFlow]?.steps[flowStepIndex];\n        renderEdges(step ? getFlowHighlightEdges(step.nodes) : []);\n      } else {\n        renderEdges();\n      }\n    }\n\n    document.getElementById('search').addEventListener('input', e => {\n      searchQuery = e.target.value;\n      refresh();\n    });\n\n    document.getElementById('zoomIn').addEventListener('click', () => { scale = Math.min(1.4, scale + 0.1); applyTransform(); });\n    document.getElementById('zoomOut').addEventListener('click', () => { scale = Math.max(0.45, scale - 0.1); applyTransform(); });\n    document.getElementById('resetView').addEventListener('click', () => { scale = 0.82; panX = 20; panY = 10; applyTransform(); });\n\n    let dragging = false;\n    let lastX = 0, lastY = 0;\n    canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {\n      if (e.target.closest('.node')) return;\n      dragging = true;\n      lastX = e.clientX;\n      lastY = e.clientY;\n      canvas.classList.add('dragging');\n      canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n    });\n    canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', e => {\n      if (!dragging) return;\n      panX += e.clientX - lastX;\n      panY += e.clientY - lastY;\n      lastX = e.clientX;\n      lastY = e.clientY;\n      applyTransform();\n    });\n    canvas.addEventListener('pointerup', () => { dragging = false; canvas.classList.remove('dragging'); });\n\n    buildFilters();\n    renderLanes();\n    renderNodes();\n    renderEdges();\n    applyTransform();\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n","numLines":905,"startLine":1,"totalLines":905}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01CjeUeLDNTQBNij3ozFwtgp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the context I need. Let me build the payments-system architecture map using the Claude reference as a structural template, adapted for payments."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7153,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16168,"cache_read_input_tokens":36480,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16168,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ab96e0e-8f96-4d88-841c-51b1b26eaeef","uuid":"088b5b0f-48f1-44a5-843f-de09bb18dc36"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01CjeUeLDNTQBNij3ozFwtgp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01QWuQsjTa7gpjn1M7GDVLBQ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Build payments-system frontend architecture HTML","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Write a file at `/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/payments-system-frontend-architecture.html`.\n\nThis is an interactive architecture map for a payments system frontend (think Stripe checkout, Adyen, Braintree). It should follow the exact same structure and JavaScript patterns as the Claude reference file below, but with payments-specific nodes, edges, flows, lanes, and sections.\n\n## Reference structure (from claude-frontend-architecture.html)\nThe file uses:\n- A fixed 3-column app layout: sidebar (280px) | canvas (flex) | detail panel (340px)\n- LAYERS object (ui, client, transport, api, provider, data, security)\n- SECTIONS array mapped to the 9 answer files\n- NODES array — each node has: id, layer, x, y, title, sub, sections[], desc, bullets[], questions[]\n- EDGES array — [fromId, toId, label]\n- FLOWS object — named flow walkthroughs with steps (each step has nodes[] and text)\n- LANES array — visual horizontal bands for each layer\n- All rendering is pure JS DOM manipulation (no external libraries)\n- Mermaid: NOT used in this file\n- No interactive demo widgets (data-demo)\n\n## Payments-specific content\n\n### SECTIONS (map to the 9 answer files)\n```js\nconst SECTIONS = [\n  { id: '01', name: 'Checkout UX', file: 'answers-html/01-checkout-flow-form-ux.html' },\n  { id: '02', name: 'PCI/Security', file: 'answers-html/02-payment-security-pci-compliance.html' },\n  { id: '03', name: 'State/Lifecycle', file: 'answers-html/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.html' },\n  { id: '04', name: 'Real-Time', file: 'answers-html/04-real-time-updates-webhooks.html' },\n  { id: '05', name: 'Performance', file: 'answers-html/05-performance-core-web-vitals.html' },\n  { id: '06', name: 'Error Handling', file: 'answers-html/06-error-handling-resilience.html' },\n  { id: '07', name: 'i18n/l10n', file: 'answers-html/07-internationalization-localization.html' },\n  { id: '08', name: 'Observability', file: 'answers-html/08-observability-analytics.html' },\n  { id: '09', name: 'PSP Abstraction', file: 'answers-html/09-architecture-provider-abstraction.html' },\n];\n```\n\n### NODES — use these (with their x/y positions adapted to a 1200×920 canvas)\n\n**UI Layer (y≈48, h=130)**\n- id: `checkoutForm`, layer: ui, x:40, y:48, title: \"Checkout Form\", sub: \"Multi-step · card input · CTA\", sections: ['01','03','06']\n  desc: \"Multi-step shell: cart → shipping → payment → confirmation. State machine drives step visibility and back-nav guards. Never allows step-skipping.\"\n  bullets: [\"Step machine: pending|shipping|payment|processing|done\", \"Hosted Fields or Elements injected in payment step\", \"Back nav flushes sensitive field refs, not values\", \"Disabled CTA + spinner on submission to prevent double-submit\"]\n  questions: [\"Multi-step state machine\", \"Prevent step skipping\", \"Back navigation + data preservation\"]\n\n- id: `cardFields`, layer: ui, x:220, y:48, title: \"Card Input Fields\", sub: \"Stripe Elements · iframe\", sections: ['01','02','05']\n  desc: \"Cross-origin iframe from PSP. Parent page never touches raw PAN/CVV. BIN detection for card type icon. Appearance API for styling. CLS prevention via fixed-height placeholder.\"\n  bullets: [\"postMessage bridge: parent ↔ iframe\", \"CardNumberElement + ExpiryElement + CVCElement\", \"Stripe appearance API — no direct CSS cross-origin\", \"Fixed 48px container prevents layout shift (CLS)\"]\n  questions: [\"Cross-origin card field isolation\", \"CLS prevention on iframe mount\", \"BIN detection for card type\"]\n\n- id: `orderSummary`, layer: ui, x:400, y:48, title: \"Order Summary\", sub: \"Cart · tax · coupon sync\", sections: ['01','07']\n  desc: \"Live-synced panel showing item totals, tax (inclusive/exclusive by locale), coupon discounts, and final charge amount. Never shows stale data during cart mutations.\"\n  bullets: [\"Derived from server cart state — no client-side tax calculation\", \"Tax-inclusive display for EU/AU locales\", \"Coupon applied → revalidates server-side → re-renders\", \"Currency formatted via Intl.NumberFormat with minor-unit conversion\"]\n  questions: [\"Tax-inclusive vs exclusive display\", \"Cart sync without full-page reload\", \"Currency formatting minor units\"]\n\n- id: `paymentMethodSelector`, layer: ui, x:580, y:48, title: \"Payment Method Selector\", sub: \"Card · wallet · BNPL · local\", sections: ['01','07','09']\n  desc: \"Data-driven list of available payment methods filtered by country, currency, and cart value. Ranked by local preference (iDEAL first in NL). Each method mounts its own SDK component.\"\n  bullets: [\"Config from server: [{type, psp, rank, logoUrl}]\", \"Lazy-loads PSP SDK only when method selected\", \"Hides methods incompatible with cart currency\", \"Fallback to card-only if config unavailable\"]\n  questions: [\"Data-driven payment method ranking\", \"Lazy PSP SDK loading\", \"Hide incompatible methods\"]\n\n- id: `confirmationScreen`, layer: ui, x:760, y:48, title: \"Confirmation Screen\", sub: \"Success · pending · failed\", sections: ['03','04','06']\n  desc: \"Terminal checkout UI. Three states: succeeded (immediate), processing (async — bank transfer/konbini), failed (retry or abandon). Must handle re-entry after navigation.\"\n  bullets: [\"Reads payment_intent status on mount — not only redirect param\", \"Processing state: polling or SSE until terminal\", \"Re-entry: server re-fetches PaymentIntent and re-derives UI state\", \"Beacon API logs abandonment if tab closes in processing\"]\n  questions: [\"Processing vs succeeded vs failed UI\", \"Re-entry after browser close\", \"Async payment method pending screen\"]\n\n- id: `errorDisplay`, layer: ui, x:940, y:48, title: \"Error Display\", sub: \"Decline · 3DS · network\", sections: ['06','03']\n  desc: \"Hierarchical error surface: field-level inline errors, form-level decline banners, global network error toasts. Decline code allowlist maps to specific messaging; remainder → generic.\"\n  bullets: [\"insufficient_funds → 'Check available balance'\", \"stolen_card → generic (anti-enumeration)\", \"3DS cancel → retry prompt, same PaymentIntent\", \"Network timeout → ambiguous state banner\"]\n  questions: [\"Decline code allowlist vs generic messages\", \"Anti-enumeration for fraud codes\", \"Ambiguous timeout UX\"]\n\n**Client Layer (y≈200, h=130)**\n- id: `paymentIntentFSM`, layer: client, x:80, y:200, title: \"PaymentIntent FSM\", sub: \"State machine · transitions\", sections: ['03','06']\n  desc: \"Client-side mirror of PaymentIntent status. XState or equivalent drives UI rendering at each state. Guards prevent illegal transitions. Side effects trigger API calls or UI changes.\"\n  bullets: [\"States: idle|submitting|requires_action|processing|succeeded|failed\", \"Guards: no re-submit if processing\", \"Entry actions: disable form, show spinner\", \"Final states trigger analytics + redirect\"]\n  questions: [\"XState payment machine definition\", \"Guard illegal transitions\", \"Optimistic UI limits for payments\"]\n\n- id: `idempotencyLayer`, layer: client, x:280, y:200, title: \"Idempotency Layer\", sub: \"Keys · retry-safe\", sections: ['03','06']\n  desc: \"Per-submission UUID keyed to (sessionId, cartId). Stored in sessionStorage. Passed as header on every payment confirm request. Server deduplicates on this key — safe to retry on timeout.\"\n  bullets: [\"Key generated once per checkout session\", \"Rotated only on explicit user retry action\", \"sessionStorage prevents cross-tab key collision\", \"Server: 409 if same key + different amount\"]\n  questions: [\"Idempotency key lifecycle\", \"Safe retry on network timeout\", \"Double-click prevention\"]\n\n- id: `formStateCache`, layer: client, x:480, y:200, title: \"Form State Cache\", sub: \"sessionStorage · no card data\", sections: ['01','03','07']\n  desc: \"Non-sensitive form fields persisted to sessionStorage for refresh recovery: email, shipping address, selected payment method type. Raw card numbers NEVER persisted.\"\n  bullets: [\"Stores: email, address, method type, step index\", \"Never stores: PAN, expiry, CVV, client_secret\", \"Restored on mount if cart session still valid\", \"Cleared on successful payment or explicit abandon\"]\n  questions: [\"What to persist across refresh\", \"Security boundary for sessionStorage\", \"Multi-step re-entry recovery\"]\n\n- id: `pspAdapterClient`, layer: client, x:680, y:200, title: \"PSP Adapter (Client)\", sub: \"IPaymentProvider interface\", sections: ['09','02']\n  desc: \"Client-side adapter pattern normalizing Stripe.js, Adyen Web Components, and Braintree Drop-in into a single IPaymentProvider interface. Checkout component never calls Stripe APIs directly.\"\n  bullets: [\"mount(container) → returns cleanup fn\", \"confirm(params) → Promise<{status, error}>\", \"on(event, handler) → normalized events\", \"CapabilityResolver: does provider support BNPL?\"]\n  questions: [\"IPaymentProvider adapter pattern\", \"Normalize cross-PSP APIs\", \"Capability resolution without UI conditionals\"]\n\n- id: `analyticsLayer`, layer: client, x:880, y:200, title: \"Analytics Layer\", sub: \"Funnel events · RUM\", sections: ['08','05']\n  desc: \"Typed event bus for funnel instrumentation. PII/PAN sanitizer runs before every dispatch. Custom performance.mark for Stripe.js init and Elements mount. Beacon API for abandonment events.\"\n  bullets: [\"checkout_step_viewed, payment_submitted, payment_succeeded\", \"beforeSend hook strips card-shaped strings\", \"performance.mark('stripe-elements-mounted')\", \"Beacon API: checkout_abandoned on beforeunload\"]\n  questions: [\"Funnel event taxonomy\", \"PAN sanitization before Sentry/GA\", \"RUM marks for Elements load\"]\n\n**Transport Layer (y≈352, h=110)**\n- id: `httpClient`, layer: transport, x:200, y:352, title: \"HTTP / REST\", sub: \"PaymentIntent · cart · session\", sections: ['03','05','09']\n  desc: \"Core API transport: create/confirm PaymentIntent, cart mutations, session management. Idempotency-Key header on all payment mutations. AbortController for in-flight request cancellation.\"\n  bullets: [\"POST /payment-intents with idempotency key\", \"Idempotency-Key: <uuid> on confirm requests\", \"AbortController on tab close / step back\", \"parseApiError → typed FrontendPaymentError\"]\n  questions: [\"AbortController for payment cancellation\", \"Error taxonomy from API responses\", \"Retry-safe HTTP methods\"]\n\n- id: `sseTransport`, layer: transport, x:450, y:352, title: \"SSE / Polling\", sub: \"Payment status push\", sections: ['04','06']\n  desc: \"Server-Sent Events for real-time payment status delivery. Fallback to exponential-backoff polling when SSE is blocked (corporate proxies). Last-Event-ID for reconnection without missed events.\"\n  bullets: [\"EventSource with Last-Event-ID on reconnect\", \"Fallback: poll /payment-intents/:id every 2→4→8→16s\", \"Max 90s polling window then show 'check email' UI\", \"Dedup events by payment_intent_id + status\"]\n  questions: [\"SSE vs polling vs WebSocket for payment status\", \"Reconnection with Last-Event-ID\", \"Fallback polling backoff\"]\n\n- id: `webhookBridge`, layer: transport, x:720, y:352, title: \"Webhook→Push Bridge\", sub: \"Stripe → server → client\", sections: ['04','08']\n  desc: \"Server-side bridge: Stripe webhook → verified → stored → pushed to frontend via SSE/WS. Ensures frontend update is consistent with DB state. Deduplicates on Stripe event ID.\"\n  bullets: [\"Stripe-Signature verification before processing\", \"payment_intent.succeeded → DB update → SSE push\", \"Dedup on stripe_event_id (idempotent handler)\", \"Stale UI correction: server always wins on conflict\"]\n  questions: [\"Webhook-to-frontend push architecture\", \"Stripe-Signature verification\", \"Frontend-server status conflict resolution\"]\n\n**API / BFF Layer (y≈504, h=130)**\n- id: `checkoutBFF`, layer: api, x:80, y:504, title: \"Checkout BFF\", sub: \"Cart · session · intent\", sections: ['03','05','09']\n  desc: \"Backend-for-frontend: creates PaymentIntents, validates cart totals server-side, issues client_secret, and manages checkout sessions. Never exposed to raw card data.\"\n  bullets: [\"POST /checkout/session → {clientSecret, cartSnapshot}\", \"Cart total re-validated server-side before intent creation\", \"client_secret scoped to session — never in DB unencrypted\", \"Session cookie stores cart_id + user_id, not card data\"]\n  questions: [\"Client secret lifecycle and scoping\", \"Server-side cart total validation\", \"BFF vs direct Stripe API from frontend\"]\n\n- id: `paymentIntentAPI`, layer: api, x:280, y:504, title: \"PaymentIntent API\", sub: \"Create · confirm · capture\", sections: ['03','04','06']\n  desc: \"Stripe PaymentIntent lifecycle management. Server creates with idempotency_key. Frontend confirms via Stripe.js (never sends raw card to your server). Webhook updates DB state on async events.\"\n  bullets: [\"Idempotency key = (user_id, cart_id, attempt_number)\", \"capture_method: manual for auth-only flows\", \"status transitions: requires_payment_method → succeeded\", \"Webhook handler: payment_intent.succeeded, .payment_failed\"]\n  questions: [\"PaymentIntent vs Charge API\", \"Manual capture flow\", \"Idempotency on server-side intent creation\"]\n\n- id: `webhookReceiver`, layer: api, x:480, y:504, title: \"Webhook Receiver\", sub: \"Stripe events · verify · dispatch\", sections: ['04','08']\n  desc: \"Receives Stripe webhook events. Verifies Stripe-Signature with webhook signing secret. Idempotent handler keyed on event ID. Dispatches to domain handlers and triggers SSE push.\"\n  bullets: [\"stripe.webhooks.constructEvent() verification\", \"Idempotent: processed_events table with stripe_event_id\", \"Dispatches: payment_intent.succeeded → order fulfillment\", \"SSE push to connected frontend sessions after DB commit\"]\n  questions: [\"Stripe-Signature verification\", \"Idempotent webhook processing\", \"Order of operations: DB commit before SSE push\"]\n\n- id: `pspRouter`, layer: api, x:680, y:504, title: \"PSP Router\", sub: \"Stripe · Adyen · Braintree\", sections: ['09','06']\n  desc: \"Server-side routing logic: selects PSP based on user country, payment method, cart value, and provider health. Returns provider-specific client token to frontend adapter. Handles provider failover.\"\n  bullets: [\"Rules: EU cards → Adyen, US cards → Stripe, BNPL → Klarna\", \"Health check: 5xx rate circuit breaker per provider\", \"Failover: server creates new token on backup provider\", \"Frontend never knows which PSP was switched to\"]\n  questions: [\"PSP routing rules\", \"Provider failover architecture\", \"Client token abstraction per PSP\"]\n\n- id: `fraudRiskAPI`, layer: api, x:880, y:504, title: \"Fraud / Risk API\", sub: \"Device signals · velocity\", sections: ['02','08']\n  desc: \"Collects device fingerprint signals from frontend (Stripe Radar, own signals). Server-side velocity checks. Risk score influences 3DS trigger threshold and decline handling.\"\n  bullets: [\"Stripe Radar rules: block if risk_score > threshold\", \"Device signals: IP, user-agent, interaction timing\", \"Velocity: 3+ failed attempts → require 3DS\", \"Never expose raw risk score to frontend\"]\n  questions: [\"Device fingerprinting for fraud\", \"3DS trigger threshold\", \"Risk signal collection without PCI scope expansion\"]\n\n**Provider Layer (y≈656, h=110)**\n- id: `stripeSDK`, layer: provider, x:160, y:656, title: \"Stripe.js / Elements\", sub: \"Card fields · confirmPayment\", sections: ['02','05','09']\n  desc: \"Primary PSP SDK. Loads from js.stripe.com on every page (Stripe recommends this for fraud signals). Mounts card fields in cross-origin iframes. confirmCardPayment handles 3DS automatically.\"\n  bullets: [\"Load on every page for Radar fraud signals\", \"stripe.confirmCardPayment() → handles 3DS inline\", \"Appearance API for cross-origin field styling\", \"PaymentElement: unified UI for all Stripe methods\"]\n  questions: [\"Why load Stripe.js on every page\", \"confirmCardPayment 3DS handling\", \"Stripe vs manual card collection PCI scope\"]\n\n- id: `adyenSDK`, layer: provider, x:380, y:656, title: \"Adyen Web Components\", sub: \"Drop-in · redirect flows\", sections: ['09','06']\n  desc: \"Alternative PSP SDK. Drop-in component or individual components. Some payment methods (SOFORT, some bank redirects) require full-page redirect rather than iframe. Requires server-side session token.\"\n  bullets: [\"AdyenCheckout({session: serverToken})\", \"Drop-in vs individual components\", \"3DS handled via redirect or iframe per card issuer\", \"resultCode normalization: Authorised/Refused/Error\"]\n  questions: [\"Adyen resultCode normalization\", \"Full-page redirect vs iframe 3DS\", \"Session token vs client key\"]\n\n- id: `localPSPs`, layer: provider, x:600, y:656, title: \"Local Payment Methods\", sub: \"iDEAL · Pix · BNPL · konbini\", sections: ['07','09','04']\n  desc: \"Async local payment methods. iDEAL: bank redirect returns to success URL. Pix: QR code display with polling. Konbini: voucher code + async confirmation. BNPL: separate SDK flow.\"\n  bullets: [\"iDEAL: redirect → webhook → SSE → confirmation\", \"Pix: QR code + 30-min TTL polling\", \"Konbini: voucher issued → async bank confirmation\", \"Klarna/Afterpay: hosted page redirect\"]\n  questions: [\"Async payment method UX (processing state)\", \"QR code polling lifecycle\", \"Konbini voucher flow architecture\"]\n\n- id: `walletAPIs`, layer: provider, x:820, y:656, title: \"Wallet APIs\", sub: \"Apple Pay · Google Pay · Link\", sections: ['01','05','09']\n  desc: \"Browser-native wallet APIs. PaymentRequest API unifies Apple Pay and Google Pay. Stripe Link for saved cross-merchant credentials. One-click checkout optimization.\"\n  bullets: [\"canMakePayment() capability check before showing button\", \"PaymentRequestButton mounts Stripe-hosted button\", \"Apple Pay: merchant validation via server endpoint\", \"Link: auto-fill returning users, expired method handling\"]\n  questions: [\"PaymentRequest API capability detection\", \"Apple Pay merchant validation\", \"Saved payment method UX handoff\"]\n\n**Data Layer (y≈808, h=110)**\n- id: `cartSessionDB`, layer: data, x:100, y:808, title: \"Cart / Session DB\", sub: \"PostgreSQL · server-side cart\", sections: ['03','01']\n  desc: \"Authoritative cart and checkout session state. Cart totals always re-validated here before PaymentIntent creation. Session stores non-sensitive checkout progress. RLS enforces user isolation.\"\n  bullets: [\"cart_items: {product_id, quantity, price_snapshot}\", \"checkout_sessions: {cart_id, user_id, step, expires_at}\", \"Price snapshot at session creation — immutable\", \"RLS: user can only read own cart and session\"]\n  questions: [\"Server-side cart total validation\", \"Session expiry handling\", \"Price snapshot immutability\"]\n\n- id: `paymentRecordsDB`, layer: data, x:320, y:808, title: \"Payment Records DB\", sub: \"PaymentIntents · orders · audit\", sections: ['03','04','08']\n  desc: \"Stores PaymentIntent IDs, statuses, idempotency keys, and fulfilled orders. Source of truth for payment status. Processed_events table for webhook idempotency.\"\n  bullets: [\"payment_intents: {id, stripe_pi_id, status, idempotency_key}\", \"processed_events: {stripe_event_id} for dedup\", \"orders: created only after succeeded status\", \"Audit log: all status transitions timestamped\"]\n  questions: [\"Payment status source of truth\", \"Idempotent webhook storage\", \"Order creation timing (webhook vs confirmPayment return)\"]\n\n- id: `sseEventBus`, layer: data, x:540, y:808, title: \"SSE Event Bus\", sub: \"Redis pub/sub · replay\", sections: ['04','06']\n  desc: \"Redis pub/sub for broadcasting payment events to connected SSE clients. Short-TTL event buffer for Last-Event-ID replay on reconnect. Keyed by user_id + payment_intent_id.\"\n  bullets: [\"Publish after DB commit — not before\", \"event_id: stripe_event_id for client dedup\", \"Replay buffer: last 20 events per user, 5min TTL\", \"SSE connections subscribe to user-scoped channel\"]\n  questions: [\"SSE event replay on reconnect\", \"Ordering: DB commit before SSE push\", \"Multi-tab SSE fan-out\"]\n\n- id: `clientStorage`, layer: data, x:760, y:808, title: \"Client Storage\", sub: \"sessionStorage · no card data\", sections: ['03','05']\n  desc: \"Browser-side: sessionStorage for non-sensitive form state (step, email, address type). No localStorage for payment data (tab-persistent is risky). client_secret in memory variable only.\"\n  bullets: [\"sessionStorage: step_index, email, shipping_address\", \"In-memory only: client_secret, card element refs\", \"Never persist: PAN, CVV, expiry in any browser storage\", \"Clear all on payment success or session expiry\"]\n  questions: [\"client_secret storage security\", \"sessionStorage vs localStorage for checkout\", \"Clearing sensitive state after payment\"]\n\n**Security nodes (scattered)**\n- id: `pciScope`, layer: security, x:40, y:656, title: \"PCI Scope Boundary\", sub: \"SAQ A · hosted fields\", sections: ['02']\n  desc: \"Hosted field iframe isolates raw card data in PSP's origin. Your page never handles PAN/CVV. Reduces compliance to PCI SAQ A (self-assessment). Any direct card handling = SAQ D.\"\n  bullets: [\"SAQ A: only if PSP hosts all card input fields\", \"SAQ D: if any card data transits your server\", \"CSP: script-src must allow js.stripe.com\", \"No card data in network requests to your server\"]\n  questions: [\"PCI DSS scope reduction via hosted fields\", \"SAQ A vs SAQ D\", \"What CSP directives Stripe requires\"]\n\n- id: `cspLayer`, layer: security, x:1040, y:504, title: \"CSP / Clickjacking\", sub: \"Content-Security-Policy\", sections: ['02','08']\n  desc: \"CSP configured to allow Stripe domains. X-Frame-Options + frame-ancestors CSP prevents clickjacking of checkout page while allowing legitimate Stripe iframes to function.\"\n  bullets: [\"script-src: 'self' https://js.stripe.com\", \"frame-src: https://js.stripe.com (for Elements iframes)\", \"frame-ancestors 'none': prevents your page being framed\", \"report-uri for CSP violation monitoring\"]\n  questions: [\"CSP for Stripe.js checkout page\", \"X-Frame-Options vs frame-ancestors\", \"CSP violation reporting\"]\n\n### EDGES (connections between nodes)\n```\n['checkoutForm', 'cardFields', 'mounts iframe'],\n['checkoutForm', 'orderSummary', 'cart sync'],\n['checkoutForm', 'paymentMethodSelector', 'method selection'],\n['checkoutForm', 'confirmationScreen', 'on success'],\n['checkoutForm', 'errorDisplay', 'decline/error'],\n['cardFields', 'stripeSDK', 'Stripe Elements'],\n['paymentMethodSelector', 'pspAdapterClient', 'selected provider'],\n['paymentMethodSelector', 'localPSPs', 'iDEAL/Pix/konbini'],\n['paymentMethodSelector', 'walletAPIs', 'Apple/Google Pay'],\n['paymentIntentFSM', 'checkoutForm', 'drive UI state'],\n['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer', 'key on submit'],\n['formStateCache', 'checkoutForm', 'restore on mount'],\n['pspAdapterClient', 'stripeSDK', 'Stripe adapter'],\n['pspAdapterClient', 'adyenSDK', 'Adyen adapter'],\n['analyticsLayer', 'checkoutForm', 'funnel events'],\n['analyticsLayer', 'paymentIntentFSM', 'state transitions'],\n['httpClient', 'checkoutBFF', 'REST'],\n['httpClient', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'confirm intent'],\n['sseTransport', 'webhookBridge', 'status push'],\n['sseTransport', 'confirmationScreen', 'status update'],\n['webhookBridge', 'webhookReceiver', 'verified event'],\n['checkoutBFF', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'create intent'],\n['checkoutBFF', 'cartSessionDB', 'validate totals'],\n['paymentIntentAPI', 'pspRouter', 'route to PSP'],\n['pspRouter', 'stripeSDK', 'Stripe token'],\n['pspRouter', 'adyenSDK', 'Adyen session'],\n['webhookReceiver', 'paymentRecordsDB', 'update status'],\n['webhookReceiver', 'sseEventBus', 'publish event'],\n['fraudRiskAPI', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'risk score'],\n['stripeSDK', 'cardFields', 'iframe mount'],\n['sseEventBus', 'sseTransport', 'SSE push'],\n['paymentRecordsDB', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'status read'],\n['cartSessionDB', 'clientStorage', 'session ref'],\n['pciScope', 'cardFields', 'PCI boundary'],\n['cspLayer', 'checkoutBFF', 'header policy'],\n['idempotencyLayer', 'httpClient', 'header'],\n['formStateCache', 'clientStorage', 'sessionStorage'],\n['analyticsLayer', 'cspLayer', 'CSP report-uri'],\n```\n\n### FLOWS (key payment walkthroughs)\n```js\nconst FLOWS = {\n  checkout: {\n    title: 'User submits payment → success',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['checkoutForm', 'cardFields', 'paymentMethodSelector'], text: 'User fills card fields in Stripe iframe, selects method' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer', 'httpClient'], text: 'FSM transitions to submitting; idempotency key set; POST to BFF' },\n      { nodes: ['checkoutBFF', 'cartSessionDB', 'paymentIntentAPI'], text: 'BFF re-validates cart; creates/retrieves PaymentIntent; returns client_secret' },\n      { nodes: ['pspAdapterClient', 'stripeSDK'], text: 'Adapter calls stripe.confirmCardPayment(clientSecret); Stripe handles 3DS if needed' },\n      { nodes: ['webhookReceiver', 'paymentRecordsDB', 'sseEventBus'], text: 'Stripe webhook arrives; verified; DB updated; SSE event published' },\n      { nodes: ['sseTransport', 'confirmationScreen'], text: 'SSE push received; PaymentIntent FSM → succeeded; confirmation rendered' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['01','03','04']\n  },\n  decline: {\n    title: 'Card decline → smart retry UX',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['stripeSDK', 'pspAdapterClient'], text: 'confirmCardPayment returns error: card_declined, insufficient_funds' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer'], text: 'FSM transitions to failed; idempotency key rotated for retry' },\n      { nodes: ['errorDisplay', 'checkoutForm'], text: 'Specific decline message shown; card fields cleared (not raw data — just focus reset)' },\n      { nodes: ['httpClient', 'paymentIntentAPI'], text: 'Same PaymentIntent reused (not new one); PATCH to update payment method' },\n      { nodes: ['analyticsLayer'], text: 'payment_failed event with decline_code and attempt_number tracked' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['06','03','08']\n  },\n  threeds: {\n    title: '3DS authentication challenge',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['stripeSDK', 'checkoutBFF'], text: 'Card requires 3DS; confirmCardPayment detects requires_action status' },\n      { nodes: ['cardFields', 'checkoutForm'], text: '3DS modal or redirect opens automatically via Stripe.js' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM'], text: 'FSM in requires_action state; submit button remains disabled' },\n      { nodes: ['webhookReceiver', 'sseEventBus', 'sseTransport'], text: 'Bank authenticates; Stripe fires webhook; SSE push to frontend' },\n      { nodes: ['confirmationScreen', 'paymentRecordsDB'], text: 'FSM → succeeded; server DB source of truth; confirmation rendered' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['06','03','04']\n  },\n  asyncPayment: {\n    title: 'Async payment (iDEAL / Pix / konbini)',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['paymentMethodSelector', 'localPSPs'], text: 'User selects local payment method; SDK loads for that method' },\n      { nodes: ['checkoutBFF', 'paymentIntentAPI'], text: 'PaymentIntent created with payment_method_types including local method' },\n      { nodes: ['localPSPs', 'checkoutForm'], text: 'Redirect to bank (iDEAL) or QR code displayed (Pix) or voucher issued (konbini)' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'confirmationScreen'], text: 'Frontend shows \"processing\" screen; polling or SSE waits for webhook' },\n      { nodes: ['webhookReceiver', 'sseTransport', 'confirmationScreen'], text: 'Webhook fires on bank confirmation (minutes to days); SSE updates UI' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['07','04','03']\n  },\n  pspFailover: {\n    title: 'PSP failover (Stripe 5xx → Adyen)',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['stripeSDK', 'pspAdapterClient'], text: 'stripe.confirmCardPayment() returns 5xx; adapter detects provider error' },\n      { nodes: ['pspRouter', 'checkoutBFF'], text: 'Server-side: create new Adyen session token for same cart' },\n      { nodes: ['adyenSDK', 'pspAdapterClient'], text: 'Adapter switches to Adyen provider; loads Adyen SDK; re-mounts card fields' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer'], text: 'New idempotency key issued; FSM resets to submitting' },\n      { nodes: ['analyticsLayer'], text: 'psp_failover event tracked; user sees no provider change' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['09','06']\n  }\n};\n```\n\n### LANES\n```js\nconst LANES = [\n  { y: 28, h: 130, label: 'UI Surfaces', layer: 'ui' },\n  { y: 178, h: 130, label: 'Client State & Adapters', layer: 'client' },\n  { y: 330, h: 110, label: 'Transport', layer: 'transport' },\n  { y: 482, h: 130, label: 'API / BFF', layer: 'api' },\n  { y: 634, h: 110, label: 'PSP Providers', layer: 'provider' },\n  { y: 786, h: 110, label: 'Data', layer: 'data' },\n];\n```\n\n## Requirements\n- Copy the CSS and JS structure exactly from the Claude reference — same variables, same layout, same rendering functions\n- Change the title to \"Payments System Frontend Architecture\"\n- Change subtitle to \"Interactive map · all 9 prep sections\"\n- Header links: link to `answers-html/index.html` and `payments-system-design-doc.md`\n- Use diagram-inner size: 1200px × 920px (same as Claude)\n- Initial scale: 0.82, panX: 20, panY: 10\n- Do NOT add any interactive demo widgets\n- Do NOT use Mermaid\n- The security nodes (pciScope, cspLayer) should appear layered between other lanes — pciScope at y:656 on the left (x:40) within the provider lane area, cspLayer at x:1040 y:504 within the api lane area\n- The canvas colors/variables remain the same (dark/light mode support)\n- No external dependencies — pure inline HTML/CSS/JS\n\nWrite the complete file. It should be self-contained and match the structural quality of the Claude reference file.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7153,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16168,"cache_read_input_tokens":36480,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16168,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ab96e0e-8f96-4d88-841c-51b1b26eaeef","uuid":"70bd89f1-9837-4615-b2e3-1c602e49f9a3"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a277c11aa399dd126","tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01QWuQsjTa7gpjn1M7GDVLBQ","description":"Build payments-system frontend architecture HTML","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Write a file at `/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/payments-system-frontend-architecture.html`.\n\nThis is an interactive architecture map for a payments system frontend (think Stripe checkout, Adyen, Braintree). It should follow the exact same structure and JavaScript patterns as the Claude reference file below, but with payments-specific nodes, edges, flows, lanes, and sections.\n\n## Reference structure (from claude-frontend-architecture.html)\nThe file uses:\n- A fixed 3-column app layout: sidebar (280px) | canvas (flex) | detail panel (340px)\n- LAYERS object (ui, client, transport, api, provider, data, security)\n- SECTIONS array mapped to the 9 answer files\n- NODES array — each node has: id, layer, x, y, title, sub, sections[], desc, bullets[], questions[]\n- EDGES array — [fromId, toId, label]\n- FLOWS object — named flow walkthroughs with steps (each step has nodes[] and text)\n- LANES array — visual horizontal bands for each layer\n- All rendering is pure JS DOM manipulation (no external libraries)\n- Mermaid: NOT used in this file\n- No interactive demo widgets (data-demo)\n\n## Payments-specific content\n\n### SECTIONS (map to the 9 answer files)\n```js\nconst SECTIONS = [\n  { id: '01', name: 'Checkout UX', file: 'answers-html/01-checkout-flow-form-ux.html' },\n  { id: '02', name: 'PCI/Security', file: 'answers-html/02-payment-security-pci-compliance.html' },\n  { id: '03', name: 'State/Lifecycle', file: 'answers-html/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.html' },\n  { id: '04', name: 'Real-Time', file: 'answers-html/04-real-time-updates-webhooks.html' },\n  { id: '05', name: 'Performance', file: 'answers-html/05-performance-core-web-vitals.html' },\n  { id: '06', name: 'Error Handling', file: 'answers-html/06-error-handling-resilience.html' },\n  { id: '07', name: 'i18n/l10n', file: 'answers-html/07-internationalization-localization.html' },\n  { id: '08', name: 'Observability', file: 'answers-html/08-observability-analytics.html' },\n  { id: '09', name: 'PSP Abstraction', file: 'answers-html/09-architecture-provider-abstraction.html' },\n];\n```\n\n### NODES — use these (with their x/y positions adapted to a 1200×920 canvas)\n\n**UI Layer (y≈48, h=130)**\n- id: `checkoutForm`, layer: ui, x:40, y:48, title: \"Checkout Form\", sub: \"Multi-step · card input · CTA\", sections: ['01','03','06']\n  desc: \"Multi-step shell: cart → shipping → payment → confirmation. State machine drives step visibility and back-nav guards. Never allows step-skipping.\"\n  bullets: [\"Step machine: pending|shipping|payment|processing|done\", \"Hosted Fields or Elements injected in payment step\", \"Back nav flushes sensitive field refs, not values\", \"Disabled CTA + spinner on submission to prevent double-submit\"]\n  questions: [\"Multi-step state machine\", \"Prevent step skipping\", \"Back navigation + data preservation\"]\n\n- id: `cardFields`, layer: ui, x:220, y:48, title: \"Card Input Fields\", sub: \"Stripe Elements · iframe\", sections: ['01','02','05']\n  desc: \"Cross-origin iframe from PSP. Parent page never touches raw PAN/CVV. BIN detection for card type icon. Appearance API for styling. CLS prevention via fixed-height placeholder.\"\n  bullets: [\"postMessage bridge: parent ↔ iframe\", \"CardNumberElement + ExpiryElement + CVCElement\", \"Stripe appearance API — no direct CSS cross-origin\", \"Fixed 48px container prevents layout shift (CLS)\"]\n  questions: [\"Cross-origin card field isolation\", \"CLS prevention on iframe mount\", \"BIN detection for card type\"]\n\n- id: `orderSummary`, layer: ui, x:400, y:48, title: \"Order Summary\", sub: \"Cart · tax · coupon sync\", sections: ['01','07']\n  desc: \"Live-synced panel showing item totals, tax (inclusive/exclusive by locale), coupon discounts, and final charge amount. Never shows stale data during cart mutations.\"\n  bullets: [\"Derived from server cart state — no client-side tax calculation\", \"Tax-inclusive display for EU/AU locales\", \"Coupon applied → revalidates server-side → re-renders\", \"Currency formatted via Intl.NumberFormat with minor-unit conversion\"]\n  questions: [\"Tax-inclusive vs exclusive display\", \"Cart sync without full-page reload\", \"Currency formatting minor units\"]\n\n- id: `paymentMethodSelector`, layer: ui, x:580, y:48, title: \"Payment Method Selector\", sub: \"Card · wallet · BNPL · local\", sections: ['01','07','09']\n  desc: \"Data-driven list of available payment methods filtered by country, currency, and cart value. Ranked by local preference (iDEAL first in NL). Each method mounts its own SDK component.\"\n  bullets: [\"Config from server: [{type, psp, rank, logoUrl}]\", \"Lazy-loads PSP SDK only when method selected\", \"Hides methods incompatible with cart currency\", \"Fallback to card-only if config unavailable\"]\n  questions: [\"Data-driven payment method ranking\", \"Lazy PSP SDK loading\", \"Hide incompatible methods\"]\n\n- id: `confirmationScreen`, layer: ui, x:760, y:48, title: \"Confirmation Screen\", sub: \"Success · pending · failed\", sections: ['03','04','06']\n  desc: \"Terminal checkout UI. Three states: succeeded (immediate), processing (async — bank transfer/konbini), failed (retry or abandon). Must handle re-entry after navigation.\"\n  bullets: [\"Reads payment_intent status on mount — not only redirect param\", \"Processing state: polling or SSE until terminal\", \"Re-entry: server re-fetches PaymentIntent and re-derives UI state\", \"Beacon API logs abandonment if tab closes in processing\"]\n  questions: [\"Processing vs succeeded vs failed UI\", \"Re-entry after browser close\", \"Async payment method pending screen\"]\n\n- id: `errorDisplay`, layer: ui, x:940, y:48, title: \"Error Display\", sub: \"Decline · 3DS · network\", sections: ['06','03']\n  desc: \"Hierarchical error surface: field-level inline errors, form-level decline banners, global network error toasts. Decline code allowlist maps to specific messaging; remainder → generic.\"\n  bullets: [\"insufficient_funds → 'Check available balance'\", \"stolen_card → generic (anti-enumeration)\", \"3DS cancel → retry prompt, same PaymentIntent\", \"Network timeout → ambiguous state banner\"]\n  questions: [\"Decline code allowlist vs generic messages\", \"Anti-enumeration for fraud codes\", \"Ambiguous timeout UX\"]\n\n**Client Layer (y≈200, h=130)**\n- id: `paymentIntentFSM`, layer: client, x:80, y:200, title: \"PaymentIntent FSM\", sub: \"State machine · transitions\", sections: ['03','06']\n  desc: \"Client-side mirror of PaymentIntent status. XState or equivalent drives UI rendering at each state. Guards prevent illegal transitions. Side effects trigger API calls or UI changes.\"\n  bullets: [\"States: idle|submitting|requires_action|processing|succeeded|failed\", \"Guards: no re-submit if processing\", \"Entry actions: disable form, show spinner\", \"Final states trigger analytics + redirect\"]\n  questions: [\"XState payment machine definition\", \"Guard illegal transitions\", \"Optimistic UI limits for payments\"]\n\n- id: `idempotencyLayer`, layer: client, x:280, y:200, title: \"Idempotency Layer\", sub: \"Keys · retry-safe\", sections: ['03','06']\n  desc: \"Per-submission UUID keyed to (sessionId, cartId). Stored in sessionStorage. Passed as header on every payment confirm request. Server deduplicates on this key — safe to retry on timeout.\"\n  bullets: [\"Key generated once per checkout session\", \"Rotated only on explicit user retry action\", \"sessionStorage prevents cross-tab key collision\", \"Server: 409 if same key + different amount\"]\n  questions: [\"Idempotency key lifecycle\", \"Safe retry on network timeout\", \"Double-click prevention\"]\n\n- id: `formStateCache`, layer: client, x:480, y:200, title: \"Form State Cache\", sub: \"sessionStorage · no card data\", sections: ['01','03','07']\n  desc: \"Non-sensitive form fields persisted to sessionStorage for refresh recovery: email, shipping address, selected payment method type. Raw card numbers NEVER persisted.\"\n  bullets: [\"Stores: email, address, method type, step index\", \"Never stores: PAN, expiry, CVV, client_secret\", \"Restored on mount if cart session still valid\", \"Cleared on successful payment or explicit abandon\"]\n  questions: [\"What to persist across refresh\", \"Security boundary for sessionStorage\", \"Multi-step re-entry recovery\"]\n\n- id: `pspAdapterClient`, layer: client, x:680, y:200, title: \"PSP Adapter (Client)\", sub: \"IPaymentProvider interface\", sections: ['09','02']\n  desc: \"Client-side adapter pattern normalizing Stripe.js, Adyen Web Components, and Braintree Drop-in into a single IPaymentProvider interface. Checkout component never calls Stripe APIs directly.\"\n  bullets: [\"mount(container) → returns cleanup fn\", \"confirm(params) → Promise<{status, error}>\", \"on(event, handler) → normalized events\", \"CapabilityResolver: does provider support BNPL?\"]\n  questions: [\"IPaymentProvider adapter pattern\", \"Normalize cross-PSP APIs\", \"Capability resolution without UI conditionals\"]\n\n- id: `analyticsLayer`, layer: client, x:880, y:200, title: \"Analytics Layer\", sub: \"Funnel events · RUM\", sections: ['08','05']\n  desc: \"Typed event bus for funnel instrumentation. PII/PAN sanitizer runs before every dispatch. Custom performance.mark for Stripe.js init and Elements mount. Beacon API for abandonment events.\"\n  bullets: [\"checkout_step_viewed, payment_submitted, payment_succeeded\", \"beforeSend hook strips card-shaped strings\", \"performance.mark('stripe-elements-mounted')\", \"Beacon API: checkout_abandoned on beforeunload\"]\n  questions: [\"Funnel event taxonomy\", \"PAN sanitization before Sentry/GA\", \"RUM marks for Elements load\"]\n\n**Transport Layer (y≈352, h=110)**\n- id: `httpClient`, layer: transport, x:200, y:352, title: \"HTTP / REST\", sub: \"PaymentIntent · cart · session\", sections: ['03','05','09']\n  desc: \"Core API transport: create/confirm PaymentIntent, cart mutations, session management. Idempotency-Key header on all payment mutations. AbortController for in-flight request cancellation.\"\n  bullets: [\"POST /payment-intents with idempotency key\", \"Idempotency-Key: <uuid> on confirm requests\", \"AbortController on tab close / step back\", \"parseApiError → typed FrontendPaymentError\"]\n  questions: [\"AbortController for payment cancellation\", \"Error taxonomy from API responses\", \"Retry-safe HTTP methods\"]\n\n- id: `sseTransport`, layer: transport, x:450, y:352, title: \"SSE / Polling\", sub: \"Payment status push\", sections: ['04','06']\n  desc: \"Server-Sent Events for real-time payment status delivery. Fallback to exponential-backoff polling when SSE is blocked (corporate proxies). Last-Event-ID for reconnection without missed events.\"\n  bullets: [\"EventSource with Last-Event-ID on reconnect\", \"Fallback: poll /payment-intents/:id every 2→4→8→16s\", \"Max 90s polling window then show 'check email' UI\", \"Dedup events by payment_intent_id + status\"]\n  questions: [\"SSE vs polling vs WebSocket for payment status\", \"Reconnection with Last-Event-ID\", \"Fallback polling backoff\"]\n\n- id: `webhookBridge`, layer: transport, x:720, y:352, title: \"Webhook→Push Bridge\", sub: \"Stripe → server → client\", sections: ['04','08']\n  desc: \"Server-side bridge: Stripe webhook → verified → stored → pushed to frontend via SSE/WS. Ensures frontend update is consistent with DB state. Deduplicates on Stripe event ID.\"\n  bullets: [\"Stripe-Signature verification before processing\", \"payment_intent.succeeded → DB update → SSE push\", \"Dedup on stripe_event_id (idempotent handler)\", \"Stale UI correction: server always wins on conflict\"]\n  questions: [\"Webhook-to-frontend push architecture\", \"Stripe-Signature verification\", \"Frontend-server status conflict resolution\"]\n\n**API / BFF Layer (y≈504, h=130)**\n- id: `checkoutBFF`, layer: api, x:80, y:504, title: \"Checkout BFF\", sub: \"Cart · session · intent\", sections: ['03','05','09']\n  desc: \"Backend-for-frontend: creates PaymentIntents, validates cart totals server-side, issues client_secret, and manages checkout sessions. Never exposed to raw card data.\"\n  bullets: [\"POST /checkout/session → {clientSecret, cartSnapshot}\", \"Cart total re-validated server-side before intent creation\", \"client_secret scoped to session — never in DB unencrypted\", \"Session cookie stores cart_id + user_id, not card data\"]\n  questions: [\"Client secret lifecycle and scoping\", \"Server-side cart total validation\", \"BFF vs direct Stripe API from frontend\"]\n\n- id: `paymentIntentAPI`, layer: api, x:280, y:504, title: \"PaymentIntent API\", sub: \"Create · confirm · capture\", sections: ['03','04','06']\n  desc: \"Stripe PaymentIntent lifecycle management. Server creates with idempotency_key. Frontend confirms via Stripe.js (never sends raw card to your server). Webhook updates DB state on async events.\"\n  bullets: [\"Idempotency key = (user_id, cart_id, attempt_number)\", \"capture_method: manual for auth-only flows\", \"status transitions: requires_payment_method → succeeded\", \"Webhook handler: payment_intent.succeeded, .payment_failed\"]\n  questions: [\"PaymentIntent vs Charge API\", \"Manual capture flow\", \"Idempotency on server-side intent creation\"]\n\n- id: `webhookReceiver`, layer: api, x:480, y:504, title: \"Webhook Receiver\", sub: \"Stripe events · verify · dispatch\", sections: ['04','08']\n  desc: \"Receives Stripe webhook events. Verifies Stripe-Signature with webhook signing secret. Idempotent handler keyed on event ID. Dispatches to domain handlers and triggers SSE push.\"\n  bullets: [\"stripe.webhooks.constructEvent() verification\", \"Idempotent: processed_events table with stripe_event_id\", \"Dispatches: payment_intent.succeeded → order fulfillment\", \"SSE push to connected frontend sessions after DB commit\"]\n  questions: [\"Stripe-Signature verification\", \"Idempotent webhook processing\", \"Order of operations: DB commit before SSE push\"]\n\n- id: `pspRouter`, layer: api, x:680, y:504, title: \"PSP Router\", sub: \"Stripe · Adyen · Braintree\", sections: ['09','06']\n  desc: \"Server-side routing logic: selects PSP based on user country, payment method, cart value, and provider health. Returns provider-specific client token to frontend adapter. Handles provider failover.\"\n  bullets: [\"Rules: EU cards → Adyen, US cards → Stripe, BNPL → Klarna\", \"Health check: 5xx rate circuit breaker per provider\", \"Failover: server creates new token on backup provider\", \"Frontend never knows which PSP was switched to\"]\n  questions: [\"PSP routing rules\", \"Provider failover architecture\", \"Client token abstraction per PSP\"]\n\n- id: `fraudRiskAPI`, layer: api, x:880, y:504, title: \"Fraud / Risk API\", sub: \"Device signals · velocity\", sections: ['02','08']\n  desc: \"Collects device fingerprint signals from frontend (Stripe Radar, own signals). Server-side velocity checks. Risk score influences 3DS trigger threshold and decline handling.\"\n  bullets: [\"Stripe Radar rules: block if risk_score > threshold\", \"Device signals: IP, user-agent, interaction timing\", \"Velocity: 3+ failed attempts → require 3DS\", \"Never expose raw risk score to frontend\"]\n  questions: [\"Device fingerprinting for fraud\", \"3DS trigger threshold\", \"Risk signal collection without PCI scope expansion\"]\n\n**Provider Layer (y≈656, h=110)**\n- id: `stripeSDK`, layer: provider, x:160, y:656, title: \"Stripe.js / Elements\", sub: \"Card fields · confirmPayment\", sections: ['02','05','09']\n  desc: \"Primary PSP SDK. Loads from js.stripe.com on every page (Stripe recommends this for fraud signals). Mounts card fields in cross-origin iframes. confirmCardPayment handles 3DS automatically.\"\n  bullets: [\"Load on every page for Radar fraud signals\", \"stripe.confirmCardPayment() → handles 3DS inline\", \"Appearance API for cross-origin field styling\", \"PaymentElement: unified UI for all Stripe methods\"]\n  questions: [\"Why load Stripe.js on every page\", \"confirmCardPayment 3DS handling\", \"Stripe vs manual card collection PCI scope\"]\n\n- id: `adyenSDK`, layer: provider, x:380, y:656, title: \"Adyen Web Components\", sub: \"Drop-in · redirect flows\", sections: ['09','06']\n  desc: \"Alternative PSP SDK. Drop-in component or individual components. Some payment methods (SOFORT, some bank redirects) require full-page redirect rather than iframe. Requires server-side session token.\"\n  bullets: [\"AdyenCheckout({session: serverToken})\", \"Drop-in vs individual components\", \"3DS handled via redirect or iframe per card issuer\", \"resultCode normalization: Authorised/Refused/Error\"]\n  questions: [\"Adyen resultCode normalization\", \"Full-page redirect vs iframe 3DS\", \"Session token vs client key\"]\n\n- id: `localPSPs`, layer: provider, x:600, y:656, title: \"Local Payment Methods\", sub: \"iDEAL · Pix · BNPL · konbini\", sections: ['07','09','04']\n  desc: \"Async local payment methods. iDEAL: bank redirect returns to success URL. Pix: QR code display with polling. Konbini: voucher code + async confirmation. BNPL: separate SDK flow.\"\n  bullets: [\"iDEAL: redirect → webhook → SSE → confirmation\", \"Pix: QR code + 30-min TTL polling\", \"Konbini: voucher issued → async bank confirmation\", \"Klarna/Afterpay: hosted page redirect\"]\n  questions: [\"Async payment method UX (processing state)\", \"QR code polling lifecycle\", \"Konbini voucher flow architecture\"]\n\n- id: `walletAPIs`, layer: provider, x:820, y:656, title: \"Wallet APIs\", sub: \"Apple Pay · Google Pay · Link\", sections: ['01','05','09']\n  desc: \"Browser-native wallet APIs. PaymentRequest API unifies Apple Pay and Google Pay. Stripe Link for saved cross-merchant credentials. One-click checkout optimization.\"\n  bullets: [\"canMakePayment() capability check before showing button\", \"PaymentRequestButton mounts Stripe-hosted button\", \"Apple Pay: merchant validation via server endpoint\", \"Link: auto-fill returning users, expired method handling\"]\n  questions: [\"PaymentRequest API capability detection\", \"Apple Pay merchant validation\", \"Saved payment method UX handoff\"]\n\n**Data Layer (y≈808, h=110)**\n- id: `cartSessionDB`, layer: data, x:100, y:808, title: \"Cart / Session DB\", sub: \"PostgreSQL · server-side cart\", sections: ['03','01']\n  desc: \"Authoritative cart and checkout session state. Cart totals always re-validated here before PaymentIntent creation. Session stores non-sensitive checkout progress. RLS enforces user isolation.\"\n  bullets: [\"cart_items: {product_id, quantity, price_snapshot}\", \"checkout_sessions: {cart_id, user_id, step, expires_at}\", \"Price snapshot at session creation — immutable\", \"RLS: user can only read own cart and session\"]\n  questions: [\"Server-side cart total validation\", \"Session expiry handling\", \"Price snapshot immutability\"]\n\n- id: `paymentRecordsDB`, layer: data, x:320, y:808, title: \"Payment Records DB\", sub: \"PaymentIntents · orders · audit\", sections: ['03','04','08']\n  desc: \"Stores PaymentIntent IDs, statuses, idempotency keys, and fulfilled orders. Source of truth for payment status. Processed_events table for webhook idempotency.\"\n  bullets: [\"payment_intents: {id, stripe_pi_id, status, idempotency_key}\", \"processed_events: {stripe_event_id} for dedup\", \"orders: created only after succeeded status\", \"Audit log: all status transitions timestamped\"]\n  questions: [\"Payment status source of truth\", \"Idempotent webhook storage\", \"Order creation timing (webhook vs confirmPayment return)\"]\n\n- id: `sseEventBus`, layer: data, x:540, y:808, title: \"SSE Event Bus\", sub: \"Redis pub/sub · replay\", sections: ['04','06']\n  desc: \"Redis pub/sub for broadcasting payment events to connected SSE clients. Short-TTL event buffer for Last-Event-ID replay on reconnect. Keyed by user_id + payment_intent_id.\"\n  bullets: [\"Publish after DB commit — not before\", \"event_id: stripe_event_id for client dedup\", \"Replay buffer: last 20 events per user, 5min TTL\", \"SSE connections subscribe to user-scoped channel\"]\n  questions: [\"SSE event replay on reconnect\", \"Ordering: DB commit before SSE push\", \"Multi-tab SSE fan-out\"]\n\n- id: `clientStorage`, layer: data, x:760, y:808, title: \"Client Storage\", sub: \"sessionStorage · no card data\", sections: ['03','05']\n  desc: \"Browser-side: sessionStorage for non-sensitive form state (step, email, address type). No localStorage for payment data (tab-persistent is risky). client_secret in memory variable only.\"\n  bullets: [\"sessionStorage: step_index, email, shipping_address\", \"In-memory only: client_secret, card element refs\", \"Never persist: PAN, CVV, expiry in any browser storage\", \"Clear all on payment success or session expiry\"]\n  questions: [\"client_secret storage security\", \"sessionStorage vs localStorage for checkout\", \"Clearing sensitive state after payment\"]\n\n**Security nodes (scattered)**\n- id: `pciScope`, layer: security, x:40, y:656, title: \"PCI Scope Boundary\", sub: \"SAQ A · hosted fields\", sections: ['02']\n  desc: \"Hosted field iframe isolates raw card data in PSP's origin. Your page never handles PAN/CVV. Reduces compliance to PCI SAQ A (self-assessment). Any direct card handling = SAQ D.\"\n  bullets: [\"SAQ A: only if PSP hosts all card input fields\", \"SAQ D: if any card data transits your server\", \"CSP: script-src must allow js.stripe.com\", \"No card data in network requests to your server\"]\n  questions: [\"PCI DSS scope reduction via hosted fields\", \"SAQ A vs SAQ D\", \"What CSP directives Stripe requires\"]\n\n- id: `cspLayer`, layer: security, x:1040, y:504, title: \"CSP / Clickjacking\", sub: \"Content-Security-Policy\", sections: ['02','08']\n  desc: \"CSP configured to allow Stripe domains. X-Frame-Options + frame-ancestors CSP prevents clickjacking of checkout page while allowing legitimate Stripe iframes to function.\"\n  bullets: [\"script-src: 'self' https://js.stripe.com\", \"frame-src: https://js.stripe.com (for Elements iframes)\", \"frame-ancestors 'none': prevents your page being framed\", \"report-uri for CSP violation monitoring\"]\n  questions: [\"CSP for Stripe.js checkout page\", \"X-Frame-Options vs frame-ancestors\", \"CSP violation reporting\"]\n\n### EDGES (connections between nodes)\n```\n['checkoutForm', 'cardFields', 'mounts iframe'],\n['checkoutForm', 'orderSummary', 'cart sync'],\n['checkoutForm', 'paymentMethodSelector', 'method selection'],\n['checkoutForm', 'confirmationScreen', 'on success'],\n['checkoutForm', 'errorDisplay', 'decline/error'],\n['cardFields', 'stripeSDK', 'Stripe Elements'],\n['paymentMethodSelector', 'pspAdapterClient', 'selected provider'],\n['paymentMethodSelector', 'localPSPs', 'iDEAL/Pix/konbini'],\n['paymentMethodSelector', 'walletAPIs', 'Apple/Google Pay'],\n['paymentIntentFSM', 'checkoutForm', 'drive UI state'],\n['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer', 'key on submit'],\n['formStateCache', 'checkoutForm', 'restore on mount'],\n['pspAdapterClient', 'stripeSDK', 'Stripe adapter'],\n['pspAdapterClient', 'adyenSDK', 'Adyen adapter'],\n['analyticsLayer', 'checkoutForm', 'funnel events'],\n['analyticsLayer', 'paymentIntentFSM', 'state transitions'],\n['httpClient', 'checkoutBFF', 'REST'],\n['httpClient', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'confirm intent'],\n['sseTransport', 'webhookBridge', 'status push'],\n['sseTransport', 'confirmationScreen', 'status update'],\n['webhookBridge', 'webhookReceiver', 'verified event'],\n['checkoutBFF', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'create intent'],\n['checkoutBFF', 'cartSessionDB', 'validate totals'],\n['paymentIntentAPI', 'pspRouter', 'route to PSP'],\n['pspRouter', 'stripeSDK', 'Stripe token'],\n['pspRouter', 'adyenSDK', 'Adyen session'],\n['webhookReceiver', 'paymentRecordsDB', 'update status'],\n['webhookReceiver', 'sseEventBus', 'publish event'],\n['fraudRiskAPI', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'risk score'],\n['stripeSDK', 'cardFields', 'iframe mount'],\n['sseEventBus', 'sseTransport', 'SSE push'],\n['paymentRecordsDB', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'status read'],\n['cartSessionDB', 'clientStorage', 'session ref'],\n['pciScope', 'cardFields', 'PCI boundary'],\n['cspLayer', 'checkoutBFF', 'header policy'],\n['idempotencyLayer', 'httpClient', 'header'],\n['formStateCache', 'clientStorage', 'sessionStorage'],\n['analyticsLayer', 'cspLayer', 'CSP report-uri'],\n```\n\n### FLOWS (key payment walkthroughs)\n```js\nconst FLOWS = {\n  checkout: {\n    title: 'User submits payment → success',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['checkoutForm', 'cardFields', 'paymentMethodSelector'], text: 'User fills card fields in Stripe iframe, selects method' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer', 'httpClient'], text: 'FSM transitions to submitting; idempotency key set; POST to BFF' },\n      { nodes: ['checkoutBFF', 'cartSessionDB', 'paymentIntentAPI'], text: 'BFF re-validates cart; creates/retrieves PaymentIntent; returns client_secret' },\n      { nodes: ['pspAdapterClient', 'stripeSDK'], text: 'Adapter calls stripe.confirmCardPayment(clientSecret); Stripe handles 3DS if needed' },\n      { nodes: ['webhookReceiver', 'paymentRecordsDB', 'sseEventBus'], text: 'Stripe webhook arrives; verified; DB updated; SSE event published' },\n      { nodes: ['sseTransport', 'confirmationScreen'], text: 'SSE push received; PaymentIntent FSM → succeeded; confirmation rendered' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['01','03','04']\n  },\n  decline: {\n    title: 'Card decline → smart retry UX',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['stripeSDK', 'pspAdapterClient'], text: 'confirmCardPayment returns error: card_declined, insufficient_funds' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer'], text: 'FSM transitions to failed; idempotency key rotated for retry' },\n      { nodes: ['errorDisplay', 'checkoutForm'], text: 'Specific decline message shown; card fields cleared (not raw data — just focus reset)' },\n      { nodes: ['httpClient', 'paymentIntentAPI'], text: 'Same PaymentIntent reused (not new one); PATCH to update payment method' },\n      { nodes: ['analyticsLayer'], text: 'payment_failed event with decline_code and attempt_number tracked' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['06','03','08']\n  },\n  threeds: {\n    title: '3DS authentication challenge',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['stripeSDK', 'checkoutBFF'], text: 'Card requires 3DS; confirmCardPayment detects requires_action status' },\n      { nodes: ['cardFields', 'checkoutForm'], text: '3DS modal or redirect opens automatically via Stripe.js' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM'], text: 'FSM in requires_action state; submit button remains disabled' },\n      { nodes: ['webhookReceiver', 'sseEventBus', 'sseTransport'], text: 'Bank authenticates; Stripe fires webhook; SSE push to frontend' },\n      { nodes: ['confirmationScreen', 'paymentRecordsDB'], text: 'FSM → succeeded; server DB source of truth; confirmation rendered' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['06','03','04']\n  },\n  asyncPayment: {\n    title: 'Async payment (iDEAL / Pix / konbini)',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['paymentMethodSelector', 'localPSPs'], text: 'User selects local payment method; SDK loads for that method' },\n      { nodes: ['checkoutBFF', 'paymentIntentAPI'], text: 'PaymentIntent created with payment_method_types including local method' },\n      { nodes: ['localPSPs', 'checkoutForm'], text: 'Redirect to bank (iDEAL) or QR code displayed (Pix) or voucher issued (konbini)' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'confirmationScreen'], text: 'Frontend shows \"processing\" screen; polling or SSE waits for webhook' },\n      { nodes: ['webhookReceiver', 'sseTransport', 'confirmationScreen'], text: 'Webhook fires on bank confirmation (minutes to days); SSE updates UI' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['07','04','03']\n  },\n  pspFailover: {\n    title: 'PSP failover (Stripe 5xx → Adyen)',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['stripeSDK', 'pspAdapterClient'], text: 'stripe.confirmCardPayment() returns 5xx; adapter detects provider error' },\n      { nodes: ['pspRouter', 'checkoutBFF'], text: 'Server-side: create new Adyen session token for same cart' },\n      { nodes: ['adyenSDK', 'pspAdapterClient'], text: 'Adapter switches to Adyen provider; loads Adyen SDK; re-mounts card fields' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer'], text: 'New idempotency key issued; FSM resets to submitting' },\n      { nodes: ['analyticsLayer'], text: 'psp_failover event tracked; user sees no provider change' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['09','06']\n  }\n};\n```\n\n### LANES\n```js\nconst LANES = [\n  { y: 28, h: 130, label: 'UI Surfaces', layer: 'ui' },\n  { y: 178, h: 130, label: 'Client State & Adapters', layer: 'client' },\n  { y: 330, h: 110, label: 'Transport', layer: 'transport' },\n  { y: 482, h: 130, label: 'API / BFF', layer: 'api' },\n  { y: 634, h: 110, label: 'PSP Providers', layer: 'provider' },\n  { y: 786, h: 110, label: 'Data', layer: 'data' },\n];\n```\n\n## Requirements\n- Copy the CSS and JS structure exactly from the Claude reference — same variables, same layout, same rendering functions\n- Change the title to \"Payments System Frontend Architecture\"\n- Change subtitle to \"Interactive map · all 9 prep sections\"\n- Header links: link to `answers-html/index.html` and `payments-system-design-doc.md`\n- Use diagram-inner size: 1200px × 920px (same as Claude)\n- Initial scale: 0.82, panX: 20, panY: 10\n- Do NOT add any interactive demo widgets\n- Do NOT use Mermaid\n- The security nodes (pciScope, cspLayer) should appear layered between other lanes — pciScope at y:656 on the left (x:40) within the provider lane area, cspLayer at x:1040 y:504 within the api lane area\n- The canvas colors/variables remain the same (dark/light mode support)\n- No external dependencies — pure inline HTML/CSS/JS\n\nWrite the complete file. It should be self-contained and match the structural quality of the Claude reference file.\n","uuid":"f99f830c-17a9-4a87-8ce2-8b064875d98a","session_id":"7ab96e0e-8f96-4d88-841c-51b1b26eaeef"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Write a file at `/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/payments-system-frontend-architecture.html`.\n\nThis is an interactive architecture map for a payments system frontend (think Stripe checkout, Adyen, Braintree). It should follow the exact same structure and JavaScript patterns as the Claude reference file below, but with payments-specific nodes, edges, flows, lanes, and sections.\n\n## Reference structure (from claude-frontend-architecture.html)\nThe file uses:\n- A fixed 3-column app layout: sidebar (280px) | canvas (flex) | detail panel (340px)\n- LAYERS object (ui, client, transport, api, provider, data, security)\n- SECTIONS array mapped to the 9 answer files\n- NODES array — each node has: id, layer, x, y, title, sub, sections[], desc, bullets[], questions[]\n- EDGES array — [fromId, toId, label]\n- FLOWS object — named flow walkthroughs with steps (each step has nodes[] and text)\n- LANES array — visual horizontal bands for each layer\n- All rendering is pure JS DOM manipulation (no external libraries)\n- Mermaid: NOT used in this file\n- No interactive demo widgets (data-demo)\n\n## Payments-specific content\n\n### SECTIONS (map to the 9 answer files)\n```js\nconst SECTIONS = [\n  { id: '01', name: 'Checkout UX', file: 'answers-html/01-checkout-flow-form-ux.html' },\n  { id: '02', name: 'PCI/Security', file: 'answers-html/02-payment-security-pci-compliance.html' },\n  { id: '03', name: 'State/Lifecycle', file: 'answers-html/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.html' },\n  { id: '04', name: 'Real-Time', file: 'answers-html/04-real-time-updates-webhooks.html' },\n  { id: '05', name: 'Performance', file: 'answers-html/05-performance-core-web-vitals.html' },\n  { id: '06', name: 'Error Handling', file: 'answers-html/06-error-handling-resilience.html' },\n  { id: '07', name: 'i18n/l10n', file: 'answers-html/07-internationalization-localization.html' },\n  { id: '08', name: 'Observability', file: 'answers-html/08-observability-analytics.html' },\n  { id: '09', name: 'PSP Abstraction', file: 'answers-html/09-architecture-provider-abstraction.html' },\n];\n```\n\n### NODES — use these (with their x/y positions adapted to a 1200×920 canvas)\n\n**UI Layer (y≈48, h=130)**\n- id: `checkoutForm`, layer: ui, x:40, y:48, title: \"Checkout Form\", sub: \"Multi-step · card input · CTA\", sections: ['01','03','06']\n  desc: \"Multi-step shell: cart → shipping → payment → confirmation. State machine drives step visibility and back-nav guards. Never allows step-skipping.\"\n  bullets: [\"Step machine: pending|shipping|payment|processing|done\", \"Hosted Fields or Elements injected in payment step\", \"Back nav flushes sensitive field refs, not values\", \"Disabled CTA + spinner on submission to prevent double-submit\"]\n  questions: [\"Multi-step state machine\", \"Prevent step skipping\", \"Back navigation + data preservation\"]\n\n- id: `cardFields`, layer: ui, x:220, y:48, title: \"Card Input Fields\", sub: \"Stripe Elements · iframe\", sections: ['01','02','05']\n  desc: \"Cross-origin iframe from PSP. Parent page never touches raw PAN/CVV. BIN detection for card type icon. Appearance API for styling. CLS prevention via fixed-height placeholder.\"\n  bullets: [\"postMessage bridge: parent ↔ iframe\", \"CardNumberElement + ExpiryElement + CVCElement\", \"Stripe appearance API — no direct CSS cross-origin\", \"Fixed 48px container prevents layout shift (CLS)\"]\n  questions: [\"Cross-origin card field isolation\", \"CLS prevention on iframe mount\", \"BIN detection for card type\"]\n\n- id: `orderSummary`, layer: ui, x:400, y:48, title: \"Order Summary\", sub: \"Cart · tax · coupon sync\", sections: ['01','07']\n  desc: \"Live-synced panel showing item totals, tax (inclusive/exclusive by locale), coupon discounts, and final charge amount. Never shows stale data during cart mutations.\"\n  bullets: [\"Derived from server cart state — no client-side tax calculation\", \"Tax-inclusive display for EU/AU locales\", \"Coupon applied → revalidates server-side → re-renders\", \"Currency formatted via Intl.NumberFormat with minor-unit conversion\"]\n  questions: [\"Tax-inclusive vs exclusive display\", \"Cart sync without full-page reload\", \"Currency formatting minor units\"]\n\n- id: `paymentMethodSelector`, layer: ui, x:580, y:48, title: \"Payment Method Selector\", sub: \"Card · wallet · BNPL · local\", sections: ['01','07','09']\n  desc: \"Data-driven list of available payment methods filtered by country, currency, and cart value. Ranked by local preference (iDEAL first in NL). Each method mounts its own SDK component.\"\n  bullets: [\"Config from server: [{type, psp, rank, logoUrl}]\", \"Lazy-loads PSP SDK only when method selected\", \"Hides methods incompatible with cart currency\", \"Fallback to card-only if config unavailable\"]\n  questions: [\"Data-driven payment method ranking\", \"Lazy PSP SDK loading\", \"Hide incompatible methods\"]\n\n- id: `confirmationScreen`, layer: ui, x:760, y:48, title: \"Confirmation Screen\", sub: \"Success · pending · failed\", sections: ['03','04','06']\n  desc: \"Terminal checkout UI. Three states: succeeded (immediate), processing (async — bank transfer/konbini), failed (retry or abandon). Must handle re-entry after navigation.\"\n  bullets: [\"Reads payment_intent status on mount — not only redirect param\", \"Processing state: polling or SSE until terminal\", \"Re-entry: server re-fetches PaymentIntent and re-derives UI state\", \"Beacon API logs abandonment if tab closes in processing\"]\n  questions: [\"Processing vs succeeded vs failed UI\", \"Re-entry after browser close\", \"Async payment method pending screen\"]\n\n- id: `errorDisplay`, layer: ui, x:940, y:48, title: \"Error Display\", sub: \"Decline · 3DS · network\", sections: ['06','03']\n  desc: \"Hierarchical error surface: field-level inline errors, form-level decline banners, global network error toasts. Decline code allowlist maps to specific messaging; remainder → generic.\"\n  bullets: [\"insufficient_funds → 'Check available balance'\", \"stolen_card → generic (anti-enumeration)\", \"3DS cancel → retry prompt, same PaymentIntent\", \"Network timeout → ambiguous state banner\"]\n  questions: [\"Decline code allowlist vs generic messages\", \"Anti-enumeration for fraud codes\", \"Ambiguous timeout UX\"]\n\n**Client Layer (y≈200, h=130)**\n- id: `paymentIntentFSM`, layer: client, x:80, y:200, title: \"PaymentIntent FSM\", sub: \"State machine · transitions\", sections: ['03','06']\n  desc: \"Client-side mirror of PaymentIntent status. XState or equivalent drives UI rendering at each state. Guards prevent illegal transitions. Side effects trigger API calls or UI changes.\"\n  bullets: [\"States: idle|submitting|requires_action|processing|succeeded|failed\", \"Guards: no re-submit if processing\", \"Entry actions: disable form, show spinner\", \"Final states trigger analytics + redirect\"]\n  questions: [\"XState payment machine definition\", \"Guard illegal transitions\", \"Optimistic UI limits for payments\"]\n\n- id: `idempotencyLayer`, layer: client, x:280, y:200, title: \"Idempotency Layer\", sub: \"Keys · retry-safe\", sections: ['03','06']\n  desc: \"Per-submission UUID keyed to (sessionId, cartId). Stored in sessionStorage. Passed as header on every payment confirm request. Server deduplicates on this key — safe to retry on timeout.\"\n  bullets: [\"Key generated once per checkout session\", \"Rotated only on explicit user retry action\", \"sessionStorage prevents cross-tab key collision\", \"Server: 409 if same key + different amount\"]\n  questions: [\"Idempotency key lifecycle\", \"Safe retry on network timeout\", \"Double-click prevention\"]\n\n- id: `formStateCache`, layer: client, x:480, y:200, title: \"Form State Cache\", sub: \"sessionStorage · no card data\", sections: ['01','03','07']\n  desc: \"Non-sensitive form fields persisted to sessionStorage for refresh recovery: email, shipping address, selected payment method type. Raw card numbers NEVER persisted.\"\n  bullets: [\"Stores: email, address, method type, step index\", \"Never stores: PAN, expiry, CVV, client_secret\", \"Restored on mount if cart session still valid\", \"Cleared on successful payment or explicit abandon\"]\n  questions: [\"What to persist across refresh\", \"Security boundary for sessionStorage\", \"Multi-step re-entry recovery\"]\n\n- id: `pspAdapterClient`, layer: client, x:680, y:200, title: \"PSP Adapter (Client)\", sub: \"IPaymentProvider interface\", sections: ['09','02']\n  desc: \"Client-side adapter pattern normalizing Stripe.js, Adyen Web Components, and Braintree Drop-in into a single IPaymentProvider interface. Checkout component never calls Stripe APIs directly.\"\n  bullets: [\"mount(container) → returns cleanup fn\", \"confirm(params) → Promise<{status, error}>\", \"on(event, handler) → normalized events\", \"CapabilityResolver: does provider support BNPL?\"]\n  questions: [\"IPaymentProvider adapter pattern\", \"Normalize cross-PSP APIs\", \"Capability resolution without UI conditionals\"]\n\n- id: `analyticsLayer`, layer: client, x:880, y:200, title: \"Analytics Layer\", sub: \"Funnel events · RUM\", sections: ['08','05']\n  desc: \"Typed event bus for funnel instrumentation. PII/PAN sanitizer runs before every dispatch. Custom performance.mark for Stripe.js init and Elements mount. Beacon API for abandonment events.\"\n  bullets: [\"checkout_step_viewed, payment_submitted, payment_succeeded\", \"beforeSend hook strips card-shaped strings\", \"performance.mark('stripe-elements-mounted')\", \"Beacon API: checkout_abandoned on beforeunload\"]\n  questions: [\"Funnel event taxonomy\", \"PAN sanitization before Sentry/GA\", \"RUM marks for Elements load\"]\n\n**Transport Layer (y≈352, h=110)**\n- id: `httpClient`, layer: transport, x:200, y:352, title: \"HTTP / REST\", sub: \"PaymentIntent · cart · session\", sections: ['03','05','09']\n  desc: \"Core API transport: create/confirm PaymentIntent, cart mutations, session management. Idempotency-Key header on all payment mutations. AbortController for in-flight request cancellation.\"\n  bullets: [\"POST /payment-intents with idempotency key\", \"Idempotency-Key: <uuid> on confirm requests\", \"AbortController on tab close / step back\", \"parseApiError → typed FrontendPaymentError\"]\n  questions: [\"AbortController for payment cancellation\", \"Error taxonomy from API responses\", \"Retry-safe HTTP methods\"]\n\n- id: `sseTransport`, layer: transport, x:450, y:352, title: \"SSE / Polling\", sub: \"Payment status push\", sections: ['04','06']\n  desc: \"Server-Sent Events for real-time payment status delivery. Fallback to exponential-backoff polling when SSE is blocked (corporate proxies). Last-Event-ID for reconnection without missed events.\"\n  bullets: [\"EventSource with Last-Event-ID on reconnect\", \"Fallback: poll /payment-intents/:id every 2→4→8→16s\", \"Max 90s polling window then show 'check email' UI\", \"Dedup events by payment_intent_id + status\"]\n  questions: [\"SSE vs polling vs WebSocket for payment status\", \"Reconnection with Last-Event-ID\", \"Fallback polling backoff\"]\n\n- id: `webhookBridge`, layer: transport, x:720, y:352, title: \"Webhook→Push Bridge\", sub: \"Stripe → server → client\", sections: ['04','08']\n  desc: \"Server-side bridge: Stripe webhook → verified → stored → pushed to frontend via SSE/WS. Ensures frontend update is consistent with DB state. Deduplicates on Stripe event ID.\"\n  bullets: [\"Stripe-Signature verification before processing\", \"payment_intent.succeeded → DB update → SSE push\", \"Dedup on stripe_event_id (idempotent handler)\", \"Stale UI correction: server always wins on conflict\"]\n  questions: [\"Webhook-to-frontend push architecture\", \"Stripe-Signature verification\", \"Frontend-server status conflict resolution\"]\n\n**API / BFF Layer (y≈504, h=130)**\n- id: `checkoutBFF`, layer: api, x:80, y:504, title: \"Checkout BFF\", sub: \"Cart · session · intent\", sections: ['03','05','09']\n  desc: \"Backend-for-frontend: creates PaymentIntents, validates cart totals server-side, issues client_secret, and manages checkout sessions. Never exposed to raw card data.\"\n  bullets: [\"POST /checkout/session → {clientSecret, cartSnapshot}\", \"Cart total re-validated server-side before intent creation\", \"client_secret scoped to session — never in DB unencrypted\", \"Session cookie stores cart_id + user_id, not card data\"]\n  questions: [\"Client secret lifecycle and scoping\", \"Server-side cart total validation\", \"BFF vs direct Stripe API from frontend\"]\n\n- id: `paymentIntentAPI`, layer: api, x:280, y:504, title: \"PaymentIntent API\", sub: \"Create · confirm · capture\", sections: ['03','04','06']\n  desc: \"Stripe PaymentIntent lifecycle management. Server creates with idempotency_key. Frontend confirms via Stripe.js (never sends raw card to your server). Webhook updates DB state on async events.\"\n  bullets: [\"Idempotency key = (user_id, cart_id, attempt_number)\", \"capture_method: manual for auth-only flows\", \"status transitions: requires_payment_method → succeeded\", \"Webhook handler: payment_intent.succeeded, .payment_failed\"]\n  questions: [\"PaymentIntent vs Charge API\", \"Manual capture flow\", \"Idempotency on server-side intent creation\"]\n\n- id: `webhookReceiver`, layer: api, x:480, y:504, title: \"Webhook Receiver\", sub: \"Stripe events · verify · dispatch\", sections: ['04','08']\n  desc: \"Receives Stripe webhook events. Verifies Stripe-Signature with webhook signing secret. Idempotent handler keyed on event ID. Dispatches to domain handlers and triggers SSE push.\"\n  bullets: [\"stripe.webhooks.constructEvent() verification\", \"Idempotent: processed_events table with stripe_event_id\", \"Dispatches: payment_intent.succeeded → order fulfillment\", \"SSE push to connected frontend sessions after DB commit\"]\n  questions: [\"Stripe-Signature verification\", \"Idempotent webhook processing\", \"Order of operations: DB commit before SSE push\"]\n\n- id: `pspRouter`, layer: api, x:680, y:504, title: \"PSP Router\", sub: \"Stripe · Adyen · Braintree\", sections: ['09','06']\n  desc: \"Server-side routing logic: selects PSP based on user country, payment method, cart value, and provider health. Returns provider-specific client token to frontend adapter. Handles provider failover.\"\n  bullets: [\"Rules: EU cards → Adyen, US cards → Stripe, BNPL → Klarna\", \"Health check: 5xx rate circuit breaker per provider\", \"Failover: server creates new token on backup provider\", \"Frontend never knows which PSP was switched to\"]\n  questions: [\"PSP routing rules\", \"Provider failover architecture\", \"Client token abstraction per PSP\"]\n\n- id: `fraudRiskAPI`, layer: api, x:880, y:504, title: \"Fraud / Risk API\", sub: \"Device signals · velocity\", sections: ['02','08']\n  desc: \"Collects device fingerprint signals from frontend (Stripe Radar, own signals). Server-side velocity checks. Risk score influences 3DS trigger threshold and decline handling.\"\n  bullets: [\"Stripe Radar rules: block if risk_score > threshold\", \"Device signals: IP, user-agent, interaction timing\", \"Velocity: 3+ failed attempts → require 3DS\", \"Never expose raw risk score to frontend\"]\n  questions: [\"Device fingerprinting for fraud\", \"3DS trigger threshold\", \"Risk signal collection without PCI scope expansion\"]\n\n**Provider Layer (y≈656, h=110)**\n- id: `stripeSDK`, layer: provider, x:160, y:656, title: \"Stripe.js / Elements\", sub: \"Card fields · confirmPayment\", sections: ['02','05','09']\n  desc: \"Primary PSP SDK. Loads from js.stripe.com on every page (Stripe recommends this for fraud signals). Mounts card fields in cross-origin iframes. confirmCardPayment handles 3DS automatically.\"\n  bullets: [\"Load on every page for Radar fraud signals\", \"stripe.confirmCardPayment() → handles 3DS inline\", \"Appearance API for cross-origin field styling\", \"PaymentElement: unified UI for all Stripe methods\"]\n  questions: [\"Why load Stripe.js on every page\", \"confirmCardPayment 3DS handling\", \"Stripe vs manual card collection PCI scope\"]\n\n- id: `adyenSDK`, layer: provider, x:380, y:656, title: \"Adyen Web Components\", sub: \"Drop-in · redirect flows\", sections: ['09','06']\n  desc: \"Alternative PSP SDK. Drop-in component or individual components. Some payment methods (SOFORT, some bank redirects) require full-page redirect rather than iframe. Requires server-side session token.\"\n  bullets: [\"AdyenCheckout({session: serverToken})\", \"Drop-in vs individual components\", \"3DS handled via redirect or iframe per card issuer\", \"resultCode normalization: Authorised/Refused/Error\"]\n  questions: [\"Adyen resultCode normalization\", \"Full-page redirect vs iframe 3DS\", \"Session token vs client key\"]\n\n- id: `localPSPs`, layer: provider, x:600, y:656, title: \"Local Payment Methods\", sub: \"iDEAL · Pix · BNPL · konbini\", sections: ['07','09','04']\n  desc: \"Async local payment methods. iDEAL: bank redirect returns to success URL. Pix: QR code display with polling. Konbini: voucher code + async confirmation. BNPL: separate SDK flow.\"\n  bullets: [\"iDEAL: redirect → webhook → SSE → confirmation\", \"Pix: QR code + 30-min TTL polling\", \"Konbini: voucher issued → async bank confirmation\", \"Klarna/Afterpay: hosted page redirect\"]\n  questions: [\"Async payment method UX (processing state)\", \"QR code polling lifecycle\", \"Konbini voucher flow architecture\"]\n\n- id: `walletAPIs`, layer: provider, x:820, y:656, title: \"Wallet APIs\", sub: \"Apple Pay · Google Pay · Link\", sections: ['01','05','09']\n  desc: \"Browser-native wallet APIs. PaymentRequest API unifies Apple Pay and Google Pay. Stripe Link for saved cross-merchant credentials. One-click checkout optimization.\"\n  bullets: [\"canMakePayment() capability check before showing button\", \"PaymentRequestButton mounts Stripe-hosted button\", \"Apple Pay: merchant validation via server endpoint\", \"Link: auto-fill returning users, expired method handling\"]\n  questions: [\"PaymentRequest API capability detection\", \"Apple Pay merchant validation\", \"Saved payment method UX handoff\"]\n\n**Data Layer (y≈808, h=110)**\n- id: `cartSessionDB`, layer: data, x:100, y:808, title: \"Cart / Session DB\", sub: \"PostgreSQL · server-side cart\", sections: ['03','01']\n  desc: \"Authoritative cart and checkout session state. Cart totals always re-validated here before PaymentIntent creation. Session stores non-sensitive checkout progress. RLS enforces user isolation.\"\n  bullets: [\"cart_items: {product_id, quantity, price_snapshot}\", \"checkout_sessions: {cart_id, user_id, step, expires_at}\", \"Price snapshot at session creation — immutable\", \"RLS: user can only read own cart and session\"]\n  questions: [\"Server-side cart total validation\", \"Session expiry handling\", \"Price snapshot immutability\"]\n\n- id: `paymentRecordsDB`, layer: data, x:320, y:808, title: \"Payment Records DB\", sub: \"PaymentIntents · orders · audit\", sections: ['03','04','08']\n  desc: \"Stores PaymentIntent IDs, statuses, idempotency keys, and fulfilled orders. Source of truth for payment status. Processed_events table for webhook idempotency.\"\n  bullets: [\"payment_intents: {id, stripe_pi_id, status, idempotency_key}\", \"processed_events: {stripe_event_id} for dedup\", \"orders: created only after succeeded status\", \"Audit log: all status transitions timestamped\"]\n  questions: [\"Payment status source of truth\", \"Idempotent webhook storage\", \"Order creation timing (webhook vs confirmPayment return)\"]\n\n- id: `sseEventBus`, layer: data, x:540, y:808, title: \"SSE Event Bus\", sub: \"Redis pub/sub · replay\", sections: ['04','06']\n  desc: \"Redis pub/sub for broadcasting payment events to connected SSE clients. Short-TTL event buffer for Last-Event-ID replay on reconnect. Keyed by user_id + payment_intent_id.\"\n  bullets: [\"Publish after DB commit — not before\", \"event_id: stripe_event_id for client dedup\", \"Replay buffer: last 20 events per user, 5min TTL\", \"SSE connections subscribe to user-scoped channel\"]\n  questions: [\"SSE event replay on reconnect\", \"Ordering: DB commit before SSE push\", \"Multi-tab SSE fan-out\"]\n\n- id: `clientStorage`, layer: data, x:760, y:808, title: \"Client Storage\", sub: \"sessionStorage · no card data\", sections: ['03','05']\n  desc: \"Browser-side: sessionStorage for non-sensitive form state (step, email, address type). No localStorage for payment data (tab-persistent is risky). client_secret in memory variable only.\"\n  bullets: [\"sessionStorage: step_index, email, shipping_address\", \"In-memory only: client_secret, card element refs\", \"Never persist: PAN, CVV, expiry in any browser storage\", \"Clear all on payment success or session expiry\"]\n  questions: [\"client_secret storage security\", \"sessionStorage vs localStorage for checkout\", \"Clearing sensitive state after payment\"]\n\n**Security nodes (scattered)**\n- id: `pciScope`, layer: security, x:40, y:656, title: \"PCI Scope Boundary\", sub: \"SAQ A · hosted fields\", sections: ['02']\n  desc: \"Hosted field iframe isolates raw card data in PSP's origin. Your page never handles PAN/CVV. Reduces compliance to PCI SAQ A (self-assessment). Any direct card handling = SAQ D.\"\n  bullets: [\"SAQ A: only if PSP hosts all card input fields\", \"SAQ D: if any card data transits your server\", \"CSP: script-src must allow js.stripe.com\", \"No card data in network requests to your server\"]\n  questions: [\"PCI DSS scope reduction via hosted fields\", \"SAQ A vs SAQ D\", \"What CSP directives Stripe requires\"]\n\n- id: `cspLayer`, layer: security, x:1040, y:504, title: \"CSP / Clickjacking\", sub: \"Content-Security-Policy\", sections: ['02','08']\n  desc: \"CSP configured to allow Stripe domains. X-Frame-Options + frame-ancestors CSP prevents clickjacking of checkout page while allowing legitimate Stripe iframes to function.\"\n  bullets: [\"script-src: 'self' https://js.stripe.com\", \"frame-src: https://js.stripe.com (for Elements iframes)\", \"frame-ancestors 'none': prevents your page being framed\", \"report-uri for CSP violation monitoring\"]\n  questions: [\"CSP for Stripe.js checkout page\", \"X-Frame-Options vs frame-ancestors\", \"CSP violation reporting\"]\n\n### EDGES (connections between nodes)\n```\n['checkoutForm', 'cardFields', 'mounts iframe'],\n['checkoutForm', 'orderSummary', 'cart sync'],\n['checkoutForm', 'paymentMethodSelector', 'method selection'],\n['checkoutForm', 'confirmationScreen', 'on success'],\n['checkoutForm', 'errorDisplay', 'decline/error'],\n['cardFields', 'stripeSDK', 'Stripe Elements'],\n['paymentMethodSelector', 'pspAdapterClient', 'selected provider'],\n['paymentMethodSelector', 'localPSPs', 'iDEAL/Pix/konbini'],\n['paymentMethodSelector', 'walletAPIs', 'Apple/Google Pay'],\n['paymentIntentFSM', 'checkoutForm', 'drive UI state'],\n['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer', 'key on submit'],\n['formStateCache', 'checkoutForm', 'restore on mount'],\n['pspAdapterClient', 'stripeSDK', 'Stripe adapter'],\n['pspAdapterClient', 'adyenSDK', 'Adyen adapter'],\n['analyticsLayer', 'checkoutForm', 'funnel events'],\n['analyticsLayer', 'paymentIntentFSM', 'state transitions'],\n['httpClient', 'checkoutBFF', 'REST'],\n['httpClient', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'confirm intent'],\n['sseTransport', 'webhookBridge', 'status push'],\n['sseTransport', 'confirmationScreen', 'status update'],\n['webhookBridge', 'webhookReceiver', 'verified event'],\n['checkoutBFF', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'create intent'],\n['checkoutBFF', 'cartSessionDB', 'validate totals'],\n['paymentIntentAPI', 'pspRouter', 'route to PSP'],\n['pspRouter', 'stripeSDK', 'Stripe token'],\n['pspRouter', 'adyenSDK', 'Adyen session'],\n['webhookReceiver', 'paymentRecordsDB', 'update status'],\n['webhookReceiver', 'sseEventBus', 'publish event'],\n['fraudRiskAPI', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'risk score'],\n['stripeSDK', 'cardFields', 'iframe mount'],\n['sseEventBus', 'sseTransport', 'SSE push'],\n['paymentRecordsDB', 'paymentIntentAPI', 'status read'],\n['cartSessionDB', 'clientStorage', 'session ref'],\n['pciScope', 'cardFields', 'PCI boundary'],\n['cspLayer', 'checkoutBFF', 'header policy'],\n['idempotencyLayer', 'httpClient', 'header'],\n['formStateCache', 'clientStorage', 'sessionStorage'],\n['analyticsLayer', 'cspLayer', 'CSP report-uri'],\n```\n\n### FLOWS (key payment walkthroughs)\n```js\nconst FLOWS = {\n  checkout: {\n    title: 'User submits payment → success',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['checkoutForm', 'cardFields', 'paymentMethodSelector'], text: 'User fills card fields in Stripe iframe, selects method' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer', 'httpClient'], text: 'FSM transitions to submitting; idempotency key set; POST to BFF' },\n      { nodes: ['checkoutBFF', 'cartSessionDB', 'paymentIntentAPI'], text: 'BFF re-validates cart; creates/retrieves PaymentIntent; returns client_secret' },\n      { nodes: ['pspAdapterClient', 'stripeSDK'], text: 'Adapter calls stripe.confirmCardPayment(clientSecret); Stripe handles 3DS if needed' },\n      { nodes: ['webhookReceiver', 'paymentRecordsDB', 'sseEventBus'], text: 'Stripe webhook arrives; verified; DB updated; SSE event published' },\n      { nodes: ['sseTransport', 'confirmationScreen'], text: 'SSE push received; PaymentIntent FSM → succeeded; confirmation rendered' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['01','03','04']\n  },\n  decline: {\n    title: 'Card decline → smart retry UX',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['stripeSDK', 'pspAdapterClient'], text: 'confirmCardPayment returns error: card_declined, insufficient_funds' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer'], text: 'FSM transitions to failed; idempotency key rotated for retry' },\n      { nodes: ['errorDisplay', 'checkoutForm'], text: 'Specific decline message shown; card fields cleared (not raw data — just focus reset)' },\n      { nodes: ['httpClient', 'paymentIntentAPI'], text: 'Same PaymentIntent reused (not new one); PATCH to update payment method' },\n      { nodes: ['analyticsLayer'], text: 'payment_failed event with decline_code and attempt_number tracked' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['06','03','08']\n  },\n  threeds: {\n    title: '3DS authentication challenge',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['stripeSDK', 'checkoutBFF'], text: 'Card requires 3DS; confirmCardPayment detects requires_action status' },\n      { nodes: ['cardFields', 'checkoutForm'], text: '3DS modal or redirect opens automatically via Stripe.js' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM'], text: 'FSM in requires_action state; submit button remains disabled' },\n      { nodes: ['webhookReceiver', 'sseEventBus', 'sseTransport'], text: 'Bank authenticates; Stripe fires webhook; SSE push to frontend' },\n      { nodes: ['confirmationScreen', 'paymentRecordsDB'], text: 'FSM → succeeded; server DB source of truth; confirmation rendered' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['06','03','04']\n  },\n  asyncPayment: {\n    title: 'Async payment (iDEAL / Pix / konbini)',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['paymentMethodSelector', 'localPSPs'], text: 'User selects local payment method; SDK loads for that method' },\n      { nodes: ['checkoutBFF', 'paymentIntentAPI'], text: 'PaymentIntent created with payment_method_types including local method' },\n      { nodes: ['localPSPs', 'checkoutForm'], text: 'Redirect to bank (iDEAL) or QR code displayed (Pix) or voucher issued (konbini)' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'confirmationScreen'], text: 'Frontend shows \"processing\" screen; polling or SSE waits for webhook' },\n      { nodes: ['webhookReceiver', 'sseTransport', 'confirmationScreen'], text: 'Webhook fires on bank confirmation (minutes to days); SSE updates UI' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['07','04','03']\n  },\n  pspFailover: {\n    title: 'PSP failover (Stripe 5xx → Adyen)',\n    steps: [\n      { nodes: ['stripeSDK', 'pspAdapterClient'], text: 'stripe.confirmCardPayment() returns 5xx; adapter detects provider error' },\n      { nodes: ['pspRouter', 'checkoutBFF'], text: 'Server-side: create new Adyen session token for same cart' },\n      { nodes: ['adyenSDK', 'pspAdapterClient'], text: 'Adapter switches to Adyen provider; loads Adyen SDK; re-mounts card fields' },\n      { nodes: ['paymentIntentFSM', 'idempotencyLayer'], text: 'New idempotency key issued; FSM resets to submitting' },\n      { nodes: ['analyticsLayer'], text: 'psp_failover event tracked; user sees no provider change' }\n    ],\n    sections: ['09','06']\n  }\n};\n```\n\n### LANES\n```js\nconst LANES = [\n  { y: 28, h: 130, label: 'UI Surfaces', layer: 'ui' },\n  { y: 178, h: 130, label: 'Client State & Adapters', layer: 'client' },\n  { y: 330, h: 110, label: 'Transport', layer: 'transport' },\n  { y: 482, h: 130, label: 'API / BFF', layer: 'api' },\n  { y: 634, h: 110, label: 'PSP Providers', layer: 'provider' },\n  { y: 786, h: 110, label: 'Data', layer: 'data' },\n];\n```\n\n## Requirements\n- Copy the CSS and JS structure exactly from the Claude reference — same variables, same layout, same rendering functions\n- Change the title to \"Payments System Frontend Architecture\"\n- Change subtitle to \"Interactive map · all 9 prep sections\"\n- Header links: link to `answers-html/index.html` and `payments-system-design-doc.md`\n- Use diagram-inner size: 1200px × 920px (same as Claude)\n- Initial scale: 0.82, panX: 20, panY: 10\n- Do NOT add any interactive demo widgets\n- Do NOT use Mermaid\n- The security nodes (pciScope, cspLayer) should appear layered between other lanes — pciScope at y:656 on the left (x:40) within the provider lane area, cspLayer at x:1040 y:504 within the api lane area\n- The canvas colors/variables remain the same (dark/light mode support)\n- No external dependencies — pure inline HTML/CSS/JS\n\nWrite the complete file. It should be self-contained and match the structural quality of the Claude reference file.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01QWuQsjTa7gpjn1M7GDVLBQ","session_id":"7ab96e0e-8f96-4d88-841c-51b1b26eaeef","uuid":"c4306932-a7a5-4c04-b60f-81f91e23c421","timestamp":"2026-06-20T19:46:43.199Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Build payments-system frontend architecture HTML"}
