{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01SuBdp1aKGhJ6tF1VaNL9fz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was built:\n\n## `architecture-map` ✅ — `payments-system-frontend-architecture.html`\n\n**1,186-line interactive diagram** with the same engine as the Claude reference:\n\n| Layer | Nodes |\n|-------|-------|\n| UI Surfaces | Checkout Form, Card Input Fields, Order Summary, Payment Method Selector, Confirmation Screen, Error Display |\n| Client State | PaymentIntent FSM, Idempotency Layer, Form State Cache, PSP Adapter (Client), Analytics Layer |\n| Transport | HTTP/REST, SSE/Polling, Webhook→Push Bridge |\n| API/BFF | Checkout BFF, PaymentIntent API, Webhook Receiver, PSP Router, Fraud/Risk API |\n| PSP Providers | Stripe.js/Elements, Adyen Web Components, Local Payment Methods, Wallet APIs |\n| Data | Cart/Session DB, Payment Records DB, SSE Event Bus, Client Storage |\n| Security | PCI Scope Boundary, CSP/Clickjacking |\n\n**5 flow walkthroughs** to walk step-by-step:\n1. User submits payment → success (SSE confirmation)\n2. Card decline → smart retry UX\n3. 3DS authentication challenge\n4. Async payment (iDEAL / Pix / konbini)\n5. PSP failover (Stripe 5xx → Adyen)\n\nSidebar has layer/section chips for filtering, flow buttons, and a search bar. Each node click opens the detail panel with description, key mechanisms, interview questions, and links to the relevant answer sections.\n\n**Next up:** `interview-template` — `payments-system-system-design-interview.html`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":354,"cache_read_input_tokens":71540,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":354,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ab96e0e-8f96-4d88-841c-51b1b26eaeef","uuid":"eb1cc4f7-e39f-4f2f-a3db-680893f928dc"}
